[Term]
id: CL:4306226
name: MV-SPIV Slc6a2 Glut_1 Scn7a glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Mecom (Mmus), Lhx9 (Mmus), Chat (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MV-SPIV Slc6a2 Glut cells by expression of Scn7a. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Chat). These cells are located in the Medulla , in or close to the regions: Medial vestibular nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4406 MV-SPIV Slc6a2 Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, MV-SPIV Slc6a2 Glut_1 Scn7a does not have cells in spinal vestibular nucleus (SPIV). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "4406 MV-SPIV Slc6a2 Glut_1" EXACT []
