[Term]
id: PCL:0110154
name: SCH Six6 Cdc14a Gaba SCN pacemaker neuron (Mmus)
def: "A SCN pacemaker neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Six6 (Mmus), Cdc14a (Mmus). Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Subclass:094 SCH Six6 Cdc14a Gaba." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z, https://doi.org/10.1146/annurev-physiol-021909-135919;https\://doi.org/10.1038/s41593-020-0586-x]
comment: Rationale for assigning this type to reference data: Mapping of this cell set to a SCN pacemaker neuron is supported by spatial transcriptomic evidence and specific expression of Avp, Nms, Vip and Cck. Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. {xref="https://doi.org/10.1146/annurev-physiol-021909-135919;https://doi.org/10.1038/s41593-020-0586-x"}
