[Term]
id: PCL:0110786
name: Sst Gaba_3 Oriens-Lacunosum Moleculare neuron (Mmus)
def: "A Oriens-Lacunosum Moleculare neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Npffr1 (Mmus), Gm31218 (Mmus), Rbp4 (Mmus), Sp9 (Mmus), Reln (Mmus). Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Supertype:0216 Sst Gaba_3." [10.1073/pnas.2306382121, 10.1111/ejn.14549, https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Rationale for assigning this type to reference data: Morphology-anchored patch-seq annotation transfer: Winterer et al. 2019 triple-validated OLM cells (patch-clamp + electrophysiology + post-hoc morphology, n=46) and pooled Chrna2-/Htr3a-Cre OLM cohorts map to this Sst Gaba_3 supertype at F1=0.97; Sst/Chrna2/Reln/Grm1 concordant, CA1 stratum oriens soma. Mapped at supertype rather than cluster because OLM cells scatter across Sst Gaba_3 children (best child CLUS_0768 F1=0.65). skos:broadMatch. Tier: location + markers + patch-seq annotation transfer (strongest). Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. {xref="10.1073/pnas.2306382121", xref="10.1111/ejn.14549"}
synonym: "0216 Sst Gaba_3" EXACT []
