[Term]
id: PCL:0110994
name: BST-MPN Six3 Nrgn Gaba_5 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Isl1 (Mmus), Scn5a (Mmus), Adarb2 (Mmus), Pgpep1l (Mmus), Meis2 (Mmus), Ntn1 (Mmus). Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Supertype:0424 BST-MPN Six3 Nrgn Gaba_5." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, BST-MPN Six3 Nrgn Gaba_5 does not have cells in medial preoptic nucleus (MPN). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
