[Term]
id: PCL:0111073
name: TRS-BAC Sln Glut_2 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Sln (Mmus), Ebf2 (Mmus), Fam129a (Mmus). Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Supertype:0503 TRS-BAC Sln Glut_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type TRS-BAC Sln Glut_2 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for triangular nucleus of septum (TRS), bed nucleus of the anterior commissure (BAC). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
