[Term]
id: PCL:0111074
name: GPi shell neuron (Mmus)
def: "A internal globus pallidus shell projection neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Cngb3 (Mmus), Tbr1 (Mmus). Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Supertype:0504 GPi Tbr1 Cngb3 Gaba-Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1016/j.neuron.2017.03.017, https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Rationale for assigning this type to reference data: Mapped to the general type GPi shell neuron (internal globus pallidus shell projection neuron) based on soma location (to GPi & surrounding GPi core neurons), neurotransmitter (dual GABA-Glut), somastatin expression and MapMyCells heirarchical annotation transfer mapping to Primate GPi core (CS20250428_GROUP_0016) in the Basal Ganglion taxonomy. Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. {xref="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.neuron.2017.03.017"}
synonym: "0504 GPi Tbr1 Cngb3 Gaba-Glut_1" EXACT []
