[Term]
id: PCL:0111175
name: PMv-TMv Pitx2 Glut_1 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Lmx1a (Mmus), Aldh3b2 (Mmus), Nxph1 (Mmus), Ttc6 (Mmus). Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Supertype:0605 PMv-TMv Pitx2 Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type PMv-TMv Pitx2 Glut_1 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for ventral premammillary nucleus (PMv), tuberomammillary nucleus, ventral part (TMv). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "0605 PMv-TMv Pitx2 Glut_1" EXACT []
