[Term]
id: PCL:0111202
name: MH Tac2 Glut_1 cholinergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A cholinergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Chrnb4 (Mmus), Chrnb3 (Mmus), Epha3 (Mmus). Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Supertype:0632 MH Tac2 Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06808-9, https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Rationale for assigning this type to reference data: Assigned by automated classification (ELK) of a definition built from soma location Medial habenula (MH; ≥80% of grey-matter cells in both the Yao 2023 and Zhuang 2023 MERFISH atlases) and neurotransmitter acetylcholine (all clusters) against CL 2026-06-08. Basis: NT. Other inferred CL parents: neuron of the forebrain. [WMBO CL promotion round 1, 2026-10-13] Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. {xref="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z", xref="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06808-9"}
