[Term]
id: PCL:0111499
name: PCG-PRNr Vsx2 Nkx6-1 Glut_5 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Vsx2 (Mmus), Hoxb3 (Mmus), B130024G19Rik (Mmus), Kazald1 (Mmus). Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Supertype:0929 PCG-PRNr Vsx2 Nkx6-1 Glut_5." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type PCG-PRNr Vsx2 Nkx6-1 Glut_5 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for pontine central gray (PCG), pontine reticular nucleus (PRNr). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "0929 PCG-PRNr Vsx2 Nkx6-1 Glut_5" EXACT []
