[Term]
id: PCL:0111549
name: PGRN-PARN-MDRN Hoxb5 Glut_7 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Gng2 (Mmus), Cabp7 (Mmus), Hoxb3 (Mmus), Sncg (Mmus), Slc17a6 (Mmus), Onecut2 (Mmus), Scn4b (Mmus), Pou3f3 (Mmus). Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Supertype:0979 PGRN-PARN-MDRN Hoxb5 Glut_7." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06808-9, https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Rationale for assigning this type to reference data: Assigned by automated classification (ELK) of a definition built from soma location Brain stem (BS; ≥80% of grey-matter cells in both the Yao 2023 and Zhuang 2023 MERFISH atlases) and neurotransmitter glutamate (all clusters) against CL 2026-06-08. Basis: NT. Other inferred CL parents: central nervous system neuron. [WMBO CL promotion round 1, 2026-10-13] Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, PGRN-PARN-MDRN Hoxb5 Glut_7 does not have cells in paragigantocellular reticular nucleus (PGRN), medullary reticular nucleus (MDRN), paragigantocellular reticular nucleus (PGRN), parvicellular reticular nucleus (PARN), medullary reticular nucleus (MDRN). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme. {xref="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z", xref="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06808-9"}
synonym: "0979 PGRN-PARN-MDRN Hoxb5 Glut_7" EXACT []
