[Term]
id: PCL:0112383
name: CLA-EPd-CTX Car3 Glut_1 Ccbe1 cerebral cortex neuron (Mmus)
def: "A cerebral cortex neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Car3 (Mmus), Satb2 (Mmus), Ccbe1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other CLA-EPd-CTX Car3 Glut_1 cells by expression of Ccbe1. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a7, Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Isocortex , in or close to the regions: Temporal association areas, layer 6a, Agranular insular area, dorsal part, layer 6a, Supplemental somatosensory area, layer 6a . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0003 CLA-EPd-CTX Car3 Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, CLA-EPd-CTX Car3 Glut_1 Ccbe1 does not have cells in endopiriform nucleus, dorsal part (EPd). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "0003 CLA-EPd-CTX Car3 Glut_1" EXACT []
