[Term]
id: PCL:0112583
name: MEA Slc17a7 Glut_2 Pax6 cerebral cortex neuron (Mmus)
def: "A cerebral cortex neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Them7 (Mmus), Prox1 (Mmus), Angpt1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MEA Slc17a7 Glut_2 cells by expression of Pax6. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Slc17a6, Slc17a7). These cells are located in the Striatum-like amygdalar nuclei, Pallidum , in or close to the regions: Bed nuclei of the stria terminalis, Medial amygdalar nucleus, Central amygdalar nucleus, medial part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0203 MEA Slc17a7 Glut_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions.
synonym: "0203 MEA Slc17a7 Glut_2" EXACT []
