[Term]
id: PCL:0112598
name: COAp Grxcr2 Glut_2 Dusp5 cerebral cortex neuron (Mmus)
def: "A cerebral cortex neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Slc23a3 (Mmus), Zic2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other COAp Grxcr2 Glut_2 cells by expression of Dusp5. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a7). These cells are located in the Striatum-like amygdalar nuclei, Olfactory areas , in or close to the regions: Medial amygdalar nucleus, Cortical amygdalar area, posterior part, lateral zone, Cortical amygdalar area, posterior part, medial zone . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0218 COAp Grxcr2 Glut_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
