[Term]
id: PCL:0112610
name: LA-BLA-BMA-PA Glut_2 Tac1 cerebral cortex neuron (Mmus)
def: "A cerebral cortex neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Mgp (Mmus), Bmpr1b (Mmus), Calb2 (Mmus), Met (Mmus). It is distinguished from other LA-BLA-BMA-PA Glut_2 cells by expression of Tac1. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a7). These cells are located in the Olfactory areas, Cortical subplate , in or close to the regions: Basolateral amygdalar nucleus, ventral part, Piriform area, Endopiriform nucleus, ventral part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0230 LA-BLA-BMA-PA Glut_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, LA-BLA-BMA-PA Glut_2 Tac1 does not have cells in lateral amygdalar nucleus (LA), basomedial amygdalar nucleus (BMA), posterior amygdalar nucleus (PA). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "0230 LA-BLA-BMA-PA Glut_2" EXACT []
