[Term]
id: PCL:0112625
name: LA-BLA-BMA-PA Glut_5 Gm5535 cerebral cortex neuron (Mmus)
def: "A cerebral cortex neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Ptprc (Mmus), Il1rapl2 (Mmus), Npsr1 (Mmus), Cbln4 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other LA-BLA-BMA-PA Glut_5 cells by expression of Gm5535, Cbln4, Rspo2. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a7, Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Cortical subplate , in or close to the regions: Basolateral amygdalar nucleus, anterior part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0245 LA-BLA-BMA-PA Glut_5." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, LA-BLA-BMA-PA Glut_5 Gm5535 does not have cells in lateral amygdalar nucleus (LA), basomedial amygdalar nucleus (BMA), posterior amygdalar nucleus (PA). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "0245 LA-BLA-BMA-PA Glut_5" EXACT []
