id: PCL:0112636
name: ENTmv-PA-COAp Glut_2 Osr1 hippocampal neuron (Mmus)
def: "A hippocampal neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Osr1 (Mmus), Dio3 (Mmus), Met (Mmus). It is distinguished from other ENTmv-PA-COAp Glut_2 cells by expression of Osr1. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a7). These cells are located in the Retrohippocampal region , in or close to the regions: Subiculum, Entorhinal area, medial part, dorsal zone, layer 5, Entorhinal area, medial part, dorsal zone, layer 6 . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0256 ENTmv-PA-COAp Glut_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type ENTmv-PA-COAp Glut_2 Osr1 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for entorhinal area, medial part, ventral zone (ENTmv), posterior amygdalar nucleus (PA), cortical amygdalar area, posterior part (COAp). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "0256 ENTmv-PA-COAp Glut_2" EXACT []
