[Term]
id: PCL:0112666
name: CA1-ProS Glut_4 Pou3f2 hippocampal CA1-3 neuron (Mmus)
def: "A hippocampal CA1-3 neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Lefty1 (Mmus), Pde11a (Mmus), Apela (Mmus), Drd5 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other CA1-ProS Glut_4 cells by expression of Pou3f2, Slc2a9, Pde7b. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a7). These cells are located in the Hippocampal region , in or close to the regions: Field CA1, stratum oriens, Field CA1, stratum radiatum . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0286 CA1-ProS Glut_4." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, CA1-ProS Glut_4 Pou3f2 does not have cells in prosubiculum (ProS). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "0286 CA1-ProS Glut_4" EXACT []
