[Term]
id: PCL:0112673
name: CA1-ProS Glut_6 Fn1 hippocampal CA1-3 neuron (Mmus)
def: "A hippocampal CA1-3 neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of C1qtnf7 (Mmus), Spink8 (Mmus), Il1rapl2 (Mmus), Fn1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other CA1-ProS Glut_6 cells by expression of Fn1, Tox3. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a7). These cells are located in the Hippocampal region, Retrohippocampal region , in or close to the regions: Field CA1, stratum radiatum, Prosubiculum . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0293 CA1-ProS Glut_6." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions.
