id: PCL:0112676
name: CA3 Glut_1 Tll2 hippocampal CA1-3 neuron (Mmus)
def: "A hippocampal CA1-3 neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Spink8 (Mmus), Nmbr (Mmus), Smoc2 (Mmus), Dcn (Mmus). It is distinguished from other CA3 Glut_1 cells by expression of Tll2, Dcn. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a7). These cells are located in the Hippocampal region, brain , in or close to the regions: Field CA1, stratum oriens, alveus, lateral ventricle . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0296 CA3 Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type CA3 Glut_1 Tll2 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for field ca3 (CA3). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "0296 CA3 Glut_1" EXACT []
