id: PCL:0112679
name: CA3 Glut_1 Ccn3 hippocampal CA1-3 neuron (Mmus)
def: "A hippocampal CA1-3 neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Armc4 (Mmus), Serpina3g (Mmus), Lrp2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other CA3 Glut_1 cells by expression of Armc4, Ccn3. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a7). These cells are located in the Hippocampal region, brain , in or close to the regions: choroid plexus, Field CA3, stratum oriens, lateral ventricle . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0299 CA3 Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions.
synonym: "0299 CA3 Glut_1" EXACT []
