[Term]
id: PCL:0112764
name: SUB-ProS Glut_1 Mctp2 hippocampal neuron (Mmus)
def: "A hippocampal neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Fn1 (Mmus), Nts (Mmus), Slc35d3 (Mmus), Slit2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other SUB-ProS Glut_1 cells by expression of Mctp2, Scn4b, Gm30094, Gucy1a1. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a7, Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Retrohippocampal region , in or close to the regions: Subiculum . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0384 SUB-ProS Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, SUB-ProS Glut_1 Mctp2 does not have cells in prosubiculum (ProS). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
