[Term]
id: PCL:0112765
name: SUB-ProS Glut_1 Lipm hippocampal neuron (Mmus)
def: "A hippocampal neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Lipm (Mmus), Gm30094 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other SUB-ProS Glut_1 cells by expression of Lipm, Npsr1. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a7, Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Retrohippocampal region , in or close to the regions: Presubiculum, Subiculum . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0385 SUB-ProS Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, SUB-ProS Glut_1 Lipm does not have cells in prosubiculum (ProS). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "0385 SUB-ProS Glut_1" EXACT []
