id: PCL:0112781
name: CA2-FC-IG Glut_2 Spaar hippocampal CA1-3 neuron (Mmus)
def: "A hippocampal CA1-3 neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Spaar (Mmus), Ntf3 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other CA2-FC-IG Glut_2 cells by expression of Spaar. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a7). These cells are located in the Hippocampal region, brain , in or close to the regions: Induseum griseum, Field CA1, stratum oriens, Fasciola cinerea . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0401 CA2-FC-IG Glut_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
