[Term]
id: PCL:0112831
name: L6 CT CTX Glut_5 Slc9a2 L6b glutamatergic cortical neuron (Mmus)
def: "A L6b glutamatergic cortical neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Alkal1 (Mmus), Trhr (Mmus), Slc9a4 (Mmus), Adam18 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other L6 CT CTX Glut_5 cells by expression of Slc9a2, Chrna5. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a7, Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Isocortex, Olfactory areas , in or close to the regions: Taenia tecta, dorsal part, Anterior cingulate area, ventral part, layer 5, Dorsal peduncular area . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0451 L6 CT CTX Glut_5." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions.
synonym: "0451 L6 CT CTX Glut_5" EXACT []
