[Term]
id: PCL:0112832
name: L6 CT CTX Glut_5 Chrnb3 L6b glutamatergic cortical neuron (Mmus)
def: "A L6b glutamatergic cortical neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Gm40518 (Mmus), Chrnb3 (Mmus), Spag16 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other L6 CT CTX Glut_5 cells by expression of Chrnb3, Egfem1. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a7). These cells are located in the Isocortex, Striatum dorsal region, Olfactory areas , in or close to the regions: Caudoputamen, Dorsal peduncular area . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0452 L6 CT CTX Glut_5." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
