[Term]
id: PCL:0112839
name: CT SUB Glut_2 Cd68 hippocampal neuron (Mmus)
def: "A hippocampal neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Prss35 (Mmus), Cenpa (Mmus), Sntb1 (Mmus), Htr2c (Mmus). It is distinguished from other CT SUB Glut_2 cells by expression of Cd68. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a7). These cells are located in the Hippocampal region, Retrohippocampal region, brain , in or close to the regions: Field CA1, stratum oriens, Prosubiculum, Subiculum . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0459 CT SUB Glut_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
