[Term]
id: PCL:0112861
name: NP SUB Glut_2 Pvalb hippocampal neuron (Mmus)
def: "A hippocampal neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of B4galnt3 (Mmus), Crybg1 (Mmus), Pvalb (Mmus), Stum (Mmus). It is distinguished from other NP SUB Glut_2 cells by expression of Pvalb, Stum. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a7, Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Retrohippocampal region , in or close to the regions: Subiculum . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0481 NP SUB Glut_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
