[Term]
id: PCL:0112862
name: NP SUB Glut_2 Htr2c hippocampal neuron (Mmus)
def: "A hippocampal neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Ly6g6e (Mmus), Crybg1 (Mmus), Sgcd (Mmus), Htr2c (Mmus). It is distinguished from other NP SUB Glut_2 cells by expression of Htr2c, B4galnt3. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a7, Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Retrohippocampal region , in or close to the regions: Prosubiculum, Subiculum . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0482 NP SUB Glut_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
