[Term]
id: PCL:0112863
name: NP PPP Glut_1 Piezo2 hippocampal neuron (Mmus)
def: "A hippocampal neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Gm40518 (Mmus), Piezo2 (Mmus), Cplx3 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other NP PPP Glut cells by expression of Piezo2. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a7, Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Isocortex, Retrohippocampal region , in or close to the regions: Postsubiculum, Parasubiculum . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0483 NP PPP Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
