name: NP PPP Glut_1 Ddit4l hippocampal neuron (Mmus)
def: "A hippocampal neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Tmem255b (Mmus), Nxph3 (Mmus), Ddit4l (Mmus). It is distinguished from other NP PPP Glut cells by expression of Ddit4l. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a7, Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Retrohippocampal region , in or close to the regions: Postsubiculum, Presubiculum . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0484 NP PPP Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
