[Term]
id: PCL:0112880
name: HPF CR Glut_1 Lef1 Cajal-Retzius cell (Mmus)
def: "A Cajal-Retzius cell of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Trp73 (Mmus), Vmn2r1 (Mmus), Lef1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other HPF CR Glut cells by expression of Lef1. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Hippocampal region, Olfactory areas, Retrohippocampal region, brain . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0500 HPF CR Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
