[Term]
id: PCL:0112882
name: DG Glut_1 Dio3 dentate gyrus granule cell (Mmus)
def: "A dentate gyrus granule cell of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Il33 (Mmus), Thsd7b (Mmus), Ecm2 (Mmus), Nell1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other DG Glut_1 cells by expression of Dio3, Tshz2. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a7). These cells are located in the Striatum-like amygdalar nuclei, brain , in or close to the regions: fiber tracts, Medial amygdalar nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0502 DG Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type DG Glut_1 Dio3 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for dentate gyrus (DG). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "0502 DG Glut_1" EXACT []
