name: DG Glut_1 Ndst4 dentate gyrus granule cell (Mmus)
def: "A dentate gyrus granule cell of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Ntn5 (Mmus), Prox1 (Mmus), Dio3 (Mmus), Ndst4 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other DG Glut_1 cells by expression of Dio3, Ndst4. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a7). These cells are located in the Hippocampal region , in or close to the regions: Dentate gyrus, polymorph layer, Field CA3, pyramidal layer, Field CA3, stratum radiatum, Dentate gyrus, molecular layer, Dentate gyrus, granule cell layer . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0503 DG Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
