[Term]
id: PCL:0112893
name: DG-PIR Ex IMN_2 Vim immature neuron (Mmus)
def: "A immature neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Neurod4 (Mmus), Mfap4 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other DG-PIR Ex IMN_2 cells by expression of Vim. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Hippocampal region, brain , in or close to the regions: Dentate gyrus, molecular layer, corpus callosum, body, Field CA3, stratum oriens, Dentate gyrus, granule cell layer . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0513 DG-PIR Ex IMN_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, DG-PIR Ex IMN_2 Vim does not have cells in piriform area (PIR). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "0513 DG-PIR Ex IMN_2" EXACT []
