[Term]
id: PCL:0112896
name: DG-PIR Ex IMN_3 Scml4 immature neuron (Mmus)
def: "A immature neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of 2610307P16Rik (Mmus), Tbr1 (Mmus), Igfbpl1 (Mmus), Scml4 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other DG-PIR Ex IMN_3 cells by expression of Scml4. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Olfactory areas, Cortical subplate , in or close to the regions: Endopiriform nucleus, dorsal part, Piriform area . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0516 DG-PIR Ex IMN_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, DG-PIR Ex IMN_3 Scml4 does not have cells in dentate gyrus (DG). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "0516 DG-PIR Ex IMN_3" EXACT []
