[Term]
id: PCL:0112941
name: OB-in Frmd7 Gaba_5 Casz1 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Rhcg (Mmus), Trhr (Mmus), Sox1ot (Mmus), Nell2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other OB-in Frmd7 Gaba_5 cells by expression of Casz1, Sox1ot, Nell2, Rhcg. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad1, Gad2, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Striatum dorsal region, Striatum ventral region, Olfactory areas , in or close to the regions: Main olfactory bulb, granule layer, Nucleus accumbens, Caudoputamen . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0561 OB-in Frmd7 Gaba_5." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
