[Term]
id: PCL:0112946
name: OB-in Frmd7 Gaba_7 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Lgr6 (Mmus), Ndnf (Mmus), Sox1ot (Mmus), Kcnb2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other OB-in Frmd7 Gaba cells by expression of Ndnf, Stxbp6. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad1, Slc32a1, Gad2). These cells are located in the Olfactory areas, brain , in or close to the regions: Main olfactory bulb, granule layer, Main olfactory bulb, outer plexiform layer . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0566 OB-in Frmd7 Gaba_7." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
