[Term]
id: PCL:0113002
name: OB-STR-CTX Inh IMN_7 immature neuron (Mmus)
def: "A immature neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Draxin (Mmus), Met (Mmus), Edar (Mmus). It is distinguished from other OB-STR-CTX Inh IMN cells by expression of Met, Edar. These cells are located in the Cortical subplate, brain , in or close to the regions: Lateral amygdalar nucleus, corpus callosum, body, external capsule . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0622 OB-STR-CTX Inh IMN_7." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, OB-STR-CTX Inh IMN_7 does not have cells in striatum (STR). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
