name: Sncg Gaba_3 Crispld2 sncg GABAergic interneuron (Mmus)
def: "A sncg GABAergic interneuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Vip (Mmus), Itih5 (Mmus), 5330429C05Rik (Mmus), Syt10 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other Sncg Gaba_3 cells by expression of Crispld2, Syt10, Edn3. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad1, Gad2, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Isocortex, Olfactory areas, Retrohippocampal region , in or close to the regions: Piriform area . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0672 Sncg Gaba_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
