id: PCL:0113061
name: Sncg Gaba_5 Evc sncg GABAergic interneuron (Mmus)
def: "A sncg GABAergic interneuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Krt73 (Mmus), Vip (Mmus), Slc17a8 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other Sncg Gaba_5 cells by expression of Evc, Stk32b. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad1, Gad2, Slc32a1, Slc17a8). These cells are located in the Hippocampal region, Cortical subplate, brain , in or close to the regions: Field CA1, stratum oriens, Field CA3, stratum oriens . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0681 Sncg Gaba_5." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
