[Term]
id: PCL:0113082
name: RHP-COA Ndnf Gaba_5 Col6a3 caudal ganglionic eminence derived interneuron (Mmus)
def: "A caudal ganglionic eminence derived interneuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Krt73 (Mmus), Calca (Mmus), Myo5b (Mmus), Npas1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other RHP-COA Ndnf Gaba_5 cells by expression of Col6a3. It is glutamatergic and GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad1, Gad2, Slc32a1, Slc17a8). These cells are located in the Hippocampal region, brain , in or close to the regions: Field CA1, stratum oriens, alveus, Field CA3, stratum oriens, Field CA3, stratum radiatum . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0702 RHP-COA Ndnf Gaba_5." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type RHP-COA Ndnf Gaba_5 Col6a3 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for retrohippocampal region (RHP), cortical amygdalar area (COA). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "0702 RHP-COA Ndnf Gaba_5" EXACT []
