[Term]
id: PCL:0113118
name: Pvalb Gaba_2 Npy2r pvalb GABAergic interneuron (Mmus)
def: "A pvalb GABAergic interneuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Cort (Mmus), Adamts5 (Mmus), Npy2r (Mmus), Npr3 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other Pvalb Gaba_2 cells by expression of Npy2r, Sema3a. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad1, Gad2, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Olfactory areas, Cortical subplate , in or close to the regions: Piriform area . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0738 Pvalb Gaba_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
