[Term]
id: PCL:0113119
name: Pvalb Gaba_2 Aox3 parvalbumin-positive basket cell (Mmus)
def: "A parvalbumin-positive basket cell of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Aox3 (Mmus), Nxph2 (Mmus), Adamtsl5 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other Pvalb Gaba_2 cells by expression of Aox3. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad1, Slc32a1, Gad2). These cells are located in the Hippocampal region, brain , in or close to the regions: Field CA1, stratum oriens, Field CA3, stratum oriens . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0739 Pvalb Gaba_2." [10.1038/s41467-020-20328-4, 10.3389/fnana.2014.00056, 10.3389/fnana.2015.00124, https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Rationale for assigning this type to reference data: Morphology-anchored patch-seq annotation transfer: Que et al. 2021 biocytin-confirmed hippocampal PV basket cells (n=62) map to this cluster at F1=0.83 (purity 0.86), cleanly separated from bistratified cells (->CLUS_0737); Pvalb defining marker concordant and CA1/CA3 stratum pyramidale location consistent. skos:closeMatch (1:1). Evidence tier: location + markers + patch-seq annotation transfer (strongest). Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. {xref="10.3389/fnana.2014.00056", xref="10.1038/s41467-020-20328-4", xref="10.3389/fnana.2015.00124"}
