[Term]
id: PCL:0113120
name: Pvalb Gaba_3 Kcns1 pvalb GABAergic interneuron (Mmus)
def: "A pvalb GABAergic interneuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Mybpc1 (Mmus), Pvalb (Mmus), Reln (Mmus), Gad1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other Pvalb Gaba_3 cells by expression of Kcns1, Reln. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad1, Gad2, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Isocortex . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0740 Pvalb Gaba_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
