[Term]
id: PCL:0113126
name: Pvalb Gaba_4 Spp1 pvalb GABAergic interneuron (Mmus)
def: "A pvalb GABAergic interneuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Cort (Mmus), Spp1 (Mmus), Prss23 (Mmus), Lrrc38 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other Pvalb Gaba_4 cells by expression of Spp1, Igf1, Lrrc38. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Isocortex . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0746 Pvalb Gaba_4." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
