[Term]
id: PCL:0113135
name: Pvalb Gaba_9 pvalb GABAergic interneuron (Mmus)
def: "A pvalb GABAergic interneuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Mybpc1 (Mmus), Postn (Mmus). It is distinguished from other Pvalb Gaba cells by expression of Postn. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Th). These cells are located in the Isocortex, Retrohippocampal region , in or close to the regions: Subiculum, Retrosplenial area, ventral part, layer 5 . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0755 Pvalb Gaba_9." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
