[Term]
id: PCL:0113155
name: Sst Gaba_3 Atp10b Oriens-Lacunosum Moleculare neuron (Mmus)
def: "A Oriens-Lacunosum Moleculare neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Rarres1 (Mmus), Tacstd2 (Mmus), Ano1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other Sst Gaba_3 cells by expression of Atp10b, Rxfp3. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Hippocampal region, Isocortex, Retrohippocampal region, brain , in or close to the regions: Field CA1, stratum oriens, Prosubiculum, Subiculum . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0775 Sst Gaba_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
