name: Sst Gaba_4 Chrna2 sst GABAergic interneuron (Mmus)
def: "A sst GABAergic interneuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Myh4 (Mmus), Sst (Mmus), St8sia6 (Mmus), Chrna2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other Sst Gaba_4 cells by expression of Chrna2, St8sia6, Myh8. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Isocortex . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0776 Sst Gaba_4." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
