name: Sst Gaba_5 Crh sst GABAergic interneuron (Mmus)
def: "A sst GABAergic interneuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Dmrt2 (Mmus), Crh (Mmus), Rgs6 (Mmus), Pdzrn3 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other Sst Gaba_5 cells by expression of Crh, Lpar1, Moxd1. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Slc32a1, Gad1). These cells are located in the Isocortex , in or close to the regions: Primary motor area, Layer 5, Secondary motor area, layer 5 . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0784 Sst Gaba_5." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
