[Term]
id: PCL:0113225
name: Sst Chodl Gaba_1 Adamts5 sst chodl GABAergic interneuron (Mmus)
def: "A sst chodl GABAergic interneuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Gm31218 (Mmus), Tshr (Mmus), Ecel1 (Mmus), Adamts5 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other Sst Chodl Gaba_1 cells by expression of Adamts5, Tshr. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad1, Gad2, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Striatum-like amygdalar nuclei, Pallidum, brain , in or close to the regions: Substantia innominata, Bed nuclei of the stria terminalis, Central amygdalar nucleus, medial part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0845 Sst Chodl Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
