[Term]
id: PCL:0113247
name: NDB-SI-MA-STRv Lhx8 Gaba_1 Moxd1 medial ganglionic eminence derived interneuron (Mmus)
def: "A medial ganglionic eminence derived interneuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Corin (Mmus), Crhr2 (Mmus), Tacr3 (Mmus), 4930509J09Rik (Mmus). It is distinguished from other NDB-SI-MA-STRv Lhx8 Gaba_1 cells by expression of Moxd1, Cxcl14, Col23a1. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Striatum-like amygdalar nuclei, Pallidum , in or close to the regions: Medial septal nucleus, Diagonal band nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0867 NDB-SI-MA-STRv Lhx8 Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, NDB-SI-MA-STRv Lhx8 Gaba_1 Moxd1 does not have cells in magnocellular nucleus (MA), striatum ventral region (STRv). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "0867 NDB-SI-MA-STRv Lhx8 Gaba_1" EXACT []
