[Term]
id: PCL:0113275
name: NDB-SI-MA-STRv Lhx8 Gaba_5 Drd3 medial ganglionic eminence derived interneuron (Mmus)
def: "A medial ganglionic eminence derived interneuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Lhx8 (Mmus), Drd3 (Mmus), Col23a1 (Mmus), Sox6 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other NDB-SI-MA-STRv Lhx8 Gaba_5 cells by expression of Drd3, Col23a1, Sox6. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad1, Gad2, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus, Pallidum, brain , in or close to the regions: Lateral septal nucleus, ventral part, Striatum, Medial septal nucleus, Diagonal band nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0895 NDB-SI-MA-STRv Lhx8 Gaba_5." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, NDB-SI-MA-STRv Lhx8 Gaba_5 Drd3 does not have cells in substantia innominata (SI), magnocellular nucleus (MA), striatum ventral region (STRv). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "0895 NDB-SI-MA-STRv Lhx8 Gaba_5" EXACT []
