[Term]
id: PCL:0113281
name: NDB-SI-MA-STRv Lhx8 Gaba_6 Chrnb3 medial ganglionic eminence derived interneuron (Mmus)
def: "A medial ganglionic eminence derived interneuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Chrna2 (Mmus), Cav1 (Mmus), Lamc3 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other NDB-SI-MA-STRv Lhx8 Gaba_6 cells by expression of Chrnb3, Lamc3. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Th). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus, Striatum-like amygdalar nuclei, Pallidum , in or close to the regions: Substantia innominata, Bed nuclei of the stria terminalis, Central amygdalar nucleus, medial part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0901 NDB-SI-MA-STRv Lhx8 Gaba_6." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, NDB-SI-MA-STRv Lhx8 Gaba_6 Chrnb3 does not have cells in diagonal band nucleus (NDB), magnocellular nucleus (MA), striatum ventral region (STRv). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "0901 NDB-SI-MA-STRv Lhx8 Gaba_6" EXACT []
