[Term]
id: PCL:0113295
name: NDB-SI-MA-STRv Lhx8 Gaba_11 medial ganglionic eminence derived interneuron (Mmus)
def: "A medial ganglionic eminence derived interneuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Lhx8 (Mmus), Ngf (Mmus), Vgll3 (Mmus), Slc5a7 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other NDB-SI-MA-STRv Lhx8 Gaba cells by expression of D7Ertd443e, Slc5a7. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Striatum ventral region, Pallidum , in or close to the regions: Substantia innominata, Nucleus accumbens, Olfactory tubercle . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0915 NDB-SI-MA-STRv Lhx8 Gaba_11." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, NDB-SI-MA-STRv Lhx8 Gaba_11 does not have cells in diagonal band nucleus (NDB), magnocellular nucleus (MA). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
