[Term]
id: PCL:0113315
name: PAL-STR Gaba-Chol_3 Pth2r medial ganglionic eminence derived interneuron (Mmus)
def: "A medial ganglionic eminence derived interneuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Gpr174 (Mmus), Chat (Mmus), Pth2r (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PAL-STR Gaba-Chol_3 cells by expression of Pth2r, Slc5a7. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Chat). These cells are located in the Lateral septal complex, Pallidum, brain , in or close to the regions: Substantia innominata, Striatum, Nucleus accumbens, Medial septal nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0935 PAL-STR Gaba-Chol_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, PAL-STR Gaba-Chol_3 Pth2r does not secrete the neurotransmitter Chol, as assessed by expression of multiple marker genes.
synonym: "0935 PAL-STR Gaba-Chol_3" EXACT []
