[Term]
id: PCL:0113317
name: PAL-STR Gaba-Chol_3 Crhbp medial ganglionic eminence derived interneuron (Mmus)
def: "A medial ganglionic eminence derived interneuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of P2ry10b (Mmus), Crhbp (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PAL-STR Gaba-Chol_3 cells by expression of Crhbp. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Pallidum, brain , in or close to the regions: Substantia innominata, Striatum, Medial septal nucleus, Diagonal band nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0937 PAL-STR Gaba-Chol_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, PAL-STR Gaba-Chol_3 Crhbp does not secrete the neurotransmitter Chol, as assessed by expression of multiple marker genes.
synonym: "0937 PAL-STR Gaba-Chol_3" EXACT []
