[Term]
id: PCL:0113393
name: STR-PAL Chst9 Gaba_5 Qrfpr lateral ganglionic eminence derived neuron (Mmus)
def: "A lateral ganglionic eminence derived neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Il1rl2 (Mmus), Tacstd2 (Mmus), Qrfpr (Mmus). It is distinguished from other STR-PAL Chst9 Gaba_5 cells by expression of Qrfpr. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Striatum-like amygdalar nuclei, Cortical subplate, brain , in or close to the regions: Basomedial amygdalar nucleus, anterior part, Striatum . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1013 STR-PAL Chst9 Gaba_5." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, STR-PAL Chst9 Gaba_5 Qrfpr does not have cells in pallidum (PAL). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "1013 STR-PAL Chst9 Gaba_5" EXACT []
