[Term]
id: PCL:0113396
name: IA Mgp Gaba_1 Tnnt1 lateral ganglionic eminence derived neuron (Mmus)
def: "A lateral ganglionic eminence derived neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Mdfic (Mmus), Col6a3 (Mmus), Tnnt1 (Mmus), Thsd7b (Mmus). It is distinguished from other IA Mgp Gaba_1 cells by expression of Tnnt1. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad1, Gad2, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Striatum dorsal region, Olfactory areas, brain , in or close to the regions: Caudoputamen, Piriform area . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1016 IA Mgp Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type IA Mgp Gaba_1 Tnnt1 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for intercalated amygdalar nucleus (IA). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "1016 IA Mgp Gaba_1" EXACT []
