[Term]
id: PCL:0113406
name: IA Mgp Gaba_5 Calb1 lateral ganglionic eminence derived neuron (Mmus)
def: "A lateral ganglionic eminence derived neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Cyp26b1 (Mmus), Col14a1 (Mmus), Nfix (Mmus), Stac (Mmus). It is distinguished from other IA Mgp Gaba_5 cells by expression of Calb1, Cadps2. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Ddc). These cells are located in the Striatum-like amygdalar nuclei, Striatum ventral region, Cortical subplate, Pallidum , in or close to the regions: Central amygdalar nucleus, capsular part, Central amygdalar nucleus, medial part, Nucleus accumbens . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1026 IA Mgp Gaba_5." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type IA Mgp Gaba_5 Calb1 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for intercalated amygdalar nucleus (IA). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "1026 IA Mgp Gaba_5" EXACT []
