[Term]
id: PCL:0113407
name: IA Mgp Gaba_5 Adora2a lateral ganglionic eminence derived neuron (Mmus)
def: "A lateral ganglionic eminence derived neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Cyp26b1 (Mmus), Sp8 (Mmus), Dusp4 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other IA Mgp Gaba_5 cells by expression of Adora2a. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Olfactory areas, brain, Pallidum, Striatum-like amygdalar nuclei, Cortical subplate , in or close to the regions: Basomedial amygdalar nucleus, anterior part, Substantia innominata, Striatum, Central amygdalar nucleus, medial part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1027 IA Mgp Gaba_5." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type IA Mgp Gaba_5 Adora2a does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for intercalated amygdalar nucleus (IA). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "1027 IA Mgp Gaba_5" EXACT []
