[Term]
id: PCL:0113412
name: NDB-SI-ant Prdm12 Gaba_1 B930025P03Rik GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Spag17 (Mmus), Prdm12 (Mmus), B930025P03Rik (Mmus). It is distinguished from other NDB-SI-ant Prdm12 Gaba_1 cells by expression of B930025P03Rik. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Striatum-like amygdalar nuclei, Olfactory areas, Pallidum, brain , in or close to the regions: Anterior olfactory nucleus, Anterior amygdalar area, Lateral septal nucleus, rostral (rostroventral) part, Striatum . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1032 NDB-SI-ant Prdm12 Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, NDB-SI-ant Prdm12 Gaba_1 B930025P03Rik does not have cells in diagonal band nucleus (NDB). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "1032 NDB-SI-ant Prdm12 Gaba_1" EXACT []
