id: PCL:0113414
name: NDB-SI-ant Prdm12 Gaba_1 Nptx2 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Pax6 (Mmus), Tac1 (Mmus), Tpbg (Mmus), Npy2r (Mmus). It is distinguished from other NDB-SI-ant Prdm12 Gaba_1 cells by expression of Nptx2. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Lateral septal complex, Olfactory areas, brain , in or close to the regions: Lateral septal nucleus, rostral (rostroventral) part, Striatum . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1034 NDB-SI-ant Prdm12 Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, NDB-SI-ant Prdm12 Gaba_1 Nptx2 does not have cells in diagonal band nucleus (NDB), substantia innominata (SI). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
