[Term]
id: PCL:0113420
name: NDB-SI-ant Prdm12 Gaba_3 Nox4 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Ntn1 (Mmus), Serpinb1b (Mmus), Ankrd63 (Mmus), Cabp7 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other NDB-SI-ant Prdm12 Gaba_3 cells by expression of Sox1ot, Nox4. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Striatum-like amygdalar nuclei, Olfactory areas, Pallidum , in or close to the regions: Anterior amygdalar area, Magnocellular nucleus, Substantia innominata, Taenia tecta, ventral part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1040 NDB-SI-ant Prdm12 Gaba_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, NDB-SI-ant Prdm12 Gaba_3 Nox4 does not have cells in diagonal band nucleus (NDB). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
