[Term]
id: PCL:0113424
name: LSX Sall3 Pax6 Gaba_2 Sulf1 striatum neuron (Mmus)
def: "A striatum neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Prdm12 (Mmus), Eya4 (Mmus), Sulf1 (Mmus), Igfbpl1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other LSX Sall3 Pax6 Gaba_2 cells by expression of Sulf1. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Lateral septal complex , in or close to the regions: Lateral septal nucleus, rostral (rostroventral) part, Lateral septal nucleus, ventral part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1044 LSX Sall3 Pax6 Gaba_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
