[Term]
id: PCL:0113438
name: LSX Otx2 Gaba_3 Sst striatum neuron (Mmus)
def: "A striatum neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Clic6 (Mmus), Otx2os1 (Mmus), H2-Q2 (Mmus), Arhgap36 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other LSX Otx2 Gaba_3 cells by expression of Sst, 6430628N08Rik. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Lateral septal complex , in or close to the regions: Lateral septal nucleus, rostral (rostroventral) part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1058 LSX Otx2 Gaba_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
