[Term]
id: PCL:0113454
name: LSX Nkx2-1 Gaba_1 Calcr striatum neuron (Mmus)
def: "A striatum neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Chat (Mmus), Calcr (Mmus), Sp8 (Mmus), Arhgap36 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other LSX Nkx2-1 Gaba_1 cells by expression of Calcr, Arhgap36, Chat. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Chat). These cells are located in the Lateral septal complex , in or close to the regions: Lateral septal nucleus, rostral (rostroventral) part, Lateral septal nucleus, ventral part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1074 LSX Nkx2-1 Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
