name: LSX Prdm12 Zeb2 Gaba_1 Hmcn1 striatum neuron (Mmus)
def: "A striatum neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Col6a3 (Mmus), Ano2 (Mmus), Hmcn1 (Mmus), Tox (Mmus). It is distinguished from other LSX Prdm12 Zeb2 Gaba_1 cells by expression of Hmcn1, Bmper, Tox, Pcp4l1. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Slc18a2). These cells are located in the Lateral septal complex , in or close to the regions: Lateral septal nucleus, caudal (caudodorsal) part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1156 LSX Prdm12 Zeb2 Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
