[Term]
id: PCL:0113579
name: MEA-BST Sox6 Gaba_3 Syndig1l GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Moxd1 (Mmus), Gm39185 (Mmus), Sox6 (Mmus), Npsr1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MEA-BST Sox6 Gaba_3 cells by expression of Syndig1l, G630016G05Rik. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus, Striatum-like amygdalar nuclei, Pallidum , in or close to the regions: Anterior amygdalar area, Magnocellular nucleus, Medial amygdalar nucleus, Central amygdalar nucleus, medial part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1199 MEA-BST Sox6 Gaba_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, MEA-BST Sox6 Gaba_3 Syndig1l does not have cells in bed nuclei of the stria terminalis (BST). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
