[Term]
id: PCL:0113613
name: MEA-BST Sox6 Gaba_9 Smoc2 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of 5830418P13Rik (Mmus), Sp8 (Mmus), Smoc2 (Mmus), Sox2ot (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MEA-BST Sox6 Gaba_9 cells by expression of Smoc2, Myh7. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Striatum-like amygdalar nuclei, Cortical subplate , in or close to the regions: Basomedial amygdalar nucleus, anterior part, Medial amygdalar nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1233 MEA-BST Sox6 Gaba_9." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, MEA-BST Sox6 Gaba_9 Smoc2 does not have cells in bed nuclei of the stria terminalis (BST). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "1233 MEA-BST Sox6 Gaba_9" EXACT []
