[Term]
id: PCL:0113616
name: MEA-BST Sox6 Gaba_10 Col27a1 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Tac2 (Mmus), Defb1 (Mmus), Angpt1 (Mmus), Npsr1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MEA-BST Sox6 Gaba_10 cells by expression of Col27a1, Npsr1, Stac. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus, Pallidum , in or close to the regions: Magnocellular nucleus, Substantia innominata, Bed nuclei of the stria terminalis . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1236 MEA-BST Sox6 Gaba_10." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, MEA-BST Sox6 Gaba_10 Col27a1 does not have cells in medial amygdalar nucleus (MEA). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
