[Term]
id: PCL:0113628
name: MEA-BST Lhx6 Sp9 Gaba_3 Gm6260 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Cyp26a1 (Mmus), Gm6260 (Mmus), Ngf (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MEA-BST Lhx6 Sp9 Gaba_3 cells by expression of Gm6260. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Striatum-like amygdalar nuclei, Pallidum , in or close to the regions: Anterior amygdalar area, Magnocellular nucleus, Substantia innominata . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1248 MEA-BST Lhx6 Sp9 Gaba_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type MEA-BST Lhx6 Sp9 Gaba_3 Gm6260 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for medial amygdalar nucleus (MEA), bed nuclei of the stria terminalis (BST). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "1248 MEA-BST Lhx6 Sp9 Gaba_3" EXACT []
