id: PCL:0113667
name: MEA-BST Lhx6 Nfib Gaba_1 Mdga1 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Esr2 (Mmus), Shisal2b (Mmus), Ntn1 (Mmus), Sfta3-ps (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MEA-BST Lhx6 Nfib Gaba_1 cells by expression of Mdga1, Gal. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Ddc). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus, Striatum-like amygdalar nuclei, Pallidum , in or close to the regions: Bed nuclei of the stria terminalis, Medial amygdalar nucleus, Central amygdalar nucleus, medial part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1287 MEA-BST Lhx6 Nfib Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
