[Term]
id: PCL:0113683
name: MEA-BST Lhx6 Nfib Gaba_4 Stat5a GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Sytl4 (Mmus), Trh (Mmus), Colec12 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MEA-BST Lhx6 Nfib Gaba_4 cells by expression of Stat5a. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus , in or close to the regions: Anteroventral preoptic nucleus, Medial preoptic area, Bed nuclei of the stria terminalis, Medial preoptic nucleus, Posterodorsal preoptic nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1303 MEA-BST Lhx6 Nfib Gaba_4." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, MEA-BST Lhx6 Nfib Gaba_4 Stat5a does not have cells in medial amygdalar nucleus (MEA). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
