[Term]
id: PCL:0113684
name: MEA-BST Lhx6 Nfib Gaba_5 Adprhl1 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Adprhl1 (Mmus), Cartpt (Mmus), Sox6 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MEA-BST Lhx6 Nfib Gaba_5 cells by expression of Adprhl1, Cbln2. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Ddc). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus, Pallidum , in or close to the regions: Bed nuclei of the stria terminalis, Medial preoptic nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1304 MEA-BST Lhx6 Nfib Gaba_5." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, MEA-BST Lhx6 Nfib Gaba_5 Adprhl1 does not have cells in medial amygdalar nucleus (MEA). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
