name: CEA-BST Six3 Cyp26b1 Gaba_2 Coch GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Slc4a11 (Mmus), Prkcd (Mmus), Dchs2 (Mmus), Pde8a (Mmus). It is distinguished from other CEA-BST Six3 Cyp26b1 Gaba_2 cells by expression of Coch, Adamtsl1. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Ddc). These cells are located in the Striatum-like amygdalar nuclei, Pallidum , in or close to the regions: Bed nuclei of the stria terminalis, Striatum, Central amygdalar nucleus, capsular part, Central amygdalar nucleus, lateral part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1332 CEA-BST Six3 Cyp26b1 Gaba_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
