[Term]
id: PCL:0113713
name: CEA-BST Six3 Cyp26b1 Gaba_2 Papln GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Upk1b (Mmus), Penk (Mmus), Papln (Mmus), Gm38413 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other CEA-BST Six3 Cyp26b1 Gaba_2 cells by expression of Papln, Bcan. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Ddc). These cells are located in the Striatum-like amygdalar nuclei, brain , in or close to the regions: Striatum, Central amygdalar nucleus, capsular part, Central amygdalar nucleus, lateral part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1333 CEA-BST Six3 Cyp26b1 Gaba_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, CEA-BST Six3 Cyp26b1 Gaba_2 Papln does not have cells in bed nuclei of the stria terminalis (BST). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
