[Term]
id: PCL:0113721
name: CEA-BST Six3 Cyp26b1 Gaba_4 Gm19689 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Upk1b (Mmus), Gm19689 (Mmus), Sv2b (Mmus). It is distinguished from other CEA-BST Six3 Cyp26b1 Gaba_4 cells by expression of Gm19689, Sv2b. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Striatum-like amygdalar nuclei , in or close to the regions: Central amygdalar nucleus, capsular part, Central amygdalar nucleus, lateral part, Central amygdalar nucleus, medial part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1341 CEA-BST Six3 Cyp26b1 Gaba_4." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
