id: PCL:0113744
name: CEA-AAA-BST Six3 Sp9 Gaba_4 Zic1 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Adora2a (Mmus), Ctxn3 (Mmus), Il1r1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other CEA-AAA-BST Six3 Sp9 Gaba_4 cells by expression of Zic1, Nts. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Striatum-like amygdalar nuclei, Olfactory areas, Cortical subplate, brain , in or close to the regions: Anterior amygdalar area, Striatum, Piriform area . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1364 CEA-AAA-BST Six3 Sp9 Gaba_4." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, CEA-AAA-BST Six3 Sp9 Gaba_4 Zic1 does not have cells in central amygdalar nucleus (CEA), bed nuclei of the stria terminalis (BST). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "1364 CEA-AAA-BST Six3 Sp9 Gaba_4" EXACT []
