id: PCL:0113748
name: CEA-AAA-BST Six3 Sp9 Gaba_5 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Glis3 (Mmus), Pax6 (Mmus), 6430628N08Rik (Mmus), Lbhd2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other CEA-AAA-BST Six3 Sp9 Gaba cells by expression of Glis3, B130024G19Rik, Six3. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Ddc). These cells are located in the Striatum-like amygdalar nuclei, Cortical subplate , in or close to the regions: Striatum, Basomedial amygdalar nucleus, anterior part, Intercalated amygdalar nucleus, Medial amygdalar nucleus, Central amygdalar nucleus, medial part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1368 CEA-AAA-BST Six3 Sp9 Gaba_5." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, CEA-AAA-BST Six3 Sp9 Gaba_5 does not have cells in anterior amygdalar area (AAA), bed nuclei of the stria terminalis (BST). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
