[Term]
id: PCL:0113756
name: ACB-BST-FS D1 Gaba_2 Lhfp GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Fst (Mmus), Isl1 (Mmus), St3gal1 (Mmus), Ptprk (Mmus). It is distinguished from other ACB-BST-FS D1 Gaba_2 cells by expression of Lhfp. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Striatum ventral region, brain , in or close to the regions: Nucleus accumbens . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1376 ACB-BST-FS D1 Gaba_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, ACB-BST-FS D1 Gaba_2 Lhfp does not have cells in bed nuclei of the stria terminalis (BST). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "1376 ACB-BST-FS D1 Gaba_2" EXACT []
is_a: PCL:0110952 ! ACB-BST-FS D1 Gaba_2 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
relationship: RO:0002215 GO:0061534 {comment="Inferred to be gamma-aminobutyric acid secretion, neurotransmission based on expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1"}
