[Term]
id: PCL:0113757
name: ACB-BST-FS D1 Gaba_2 Glp1r GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Crh (Mmus), Isl1 (Mmus), Prkcq (Mmus). It is distinguished from other ACB-BST-FS D1 Gaba_2 cells by expression of Glp1r. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Striatum ventral region, Pallidum, brain , in or close to the regions: Substantia innominata, Bed nuclei of the stria terminalis, Striatum, Nucleus accumbens . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1377 ACB-BST-FS D1 Gaba_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, ACB-BST-FS D1 Gaba_2 Glp1r does not have cells in fundus of striatum (FS). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "1377 ACB-BST-FS D1 Gaba_2" EXACT []
