[Term]
id: PCL:0113761
name: ACB-BST-FS D1 Gaba_3 Galr1 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Mbnl3 (Mmus), Slc17a8 (Mmus), Galr1 (Mmus), Nts (Mmus). It is distinguished from other ACB-BST-FS D1 Gaba_3 cells by expression of Galr1, Nts. It is glutamatergic and GABAergic (inferred from expression of Slc32a1, Ddc, Slc17a8, Gad2, Gad1). These cells are located in the Lateral septal complex, Pallidum, brain , in or close to the regions: Lateral septal nucleus, ventral part, Bed nuclei of the stria terminalis, Striatum . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1381 ACB-BST-FS D1 Gaba_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, ACB-BST-FS D1 Gaba_3 Galr1 does not have cells in nucleus accumbens (ACB), fundus of striatum (FS). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "1381 ACB-BST-FS D1 Gaba_3" EXACT []
