[Term]
id: PCL:0113775
name: CEA-BST Ebf1 Pdyn Gaba_4 Cdh23 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Cdh23 (Mmus), Htr1d (Mmus), Arx (Mmus), Ebf1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other CEA-BST Ebf1 Pdyn Gaba_4 cells by expression of Cdh23, Six3. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Striatum-like amygdalar nuclei, Pallidum , in or close to the regions: Central amygdalar nucleus, medial part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1395 CEA-BST Ebf1 Pdyn Gaba_4." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, CEA-BST Ebf1 Pdyn Gaba_4 Cdh23 does not have cells in bed nuclei of the stria terminalis (BST). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "1395 CEA-BST Ebf1 Pdyn Gaba_4" EXACT []
