[Term]
id: PCL:0113795
name: BST-SI-AAA Six3 Slc22a3 Gaba_2 Pdgfd GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Pthlh (Mmus), Slc22a3 (Mmus), Ptprq (Mmus), Lypd6b (Mmus). It is distinguished from other BST-SI-AAA Six3 Slc22a3 Gaba_2 cells by expression of Pdgfd, Lypd6b. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus, Striatum ventral region, Pallidum , in or close to the regions: Lateral preoptic area, Substantia innominata, Striatum, Nucleus accumbens . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1415 BST-SI-AAA Six3 Slc22a3 Gaba_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, BST-SI-AAA Six3 Slc22a3 Gaba_2 Pdgfd does not have cells in anterior amygdalar area (AAA). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
