[Term]
id: PCL:0113796
name: BST-SI-AAA Six3 Slc22a3 Gaba_2 Gm38505 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Slc22a3 (Mmus), Npas1 (Mmus), Gm38505 (Mmus), Egflam (Mmus). It is distinguished from other BST-SI-AAA Six3 Slc22a3 Gaba_2 cells by expression of Gm38505, Egflam. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus, Pallidum , in or close to the regions: Lateral hypothalamic area, Substantia innominata, Lateral preoptic area, Nucleus accumbens, Diagonal band nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1416 BST-SI-AAA Six3 Slc22a3 Gaba_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, BST-SI-AAA Six3 Slc22a3 Gaba_2 Gm38505 does not have cells in bed nuclei of the stria terminalis (BST), anterior amygdalar area (AAA). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
