[Term]
id: PCL:0113809
name: SI-MPO-LPO Lhx8 Gaba_2 Calcr GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Col6a5 (Mmus), Crh (Mmus), Trhr (Mmus), Zfp536 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other SI-MPO-LPO Lhx8 Gaba_2 cells by expression of Calcr, Dlx1, Nts. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus, Lateral septal complex, brain , in or close to the regions: Lateral septal nucleus, ventral part, Striatum, Medial septal nucleus, Anterodorsal preoptic nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1429 SI-MPO-LPO Lhx8 Gaba_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type SI-MPO-LPO Lhx8 Gaba_2 Calcr does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for substantia innominata (SI), medial preoptic area (MPO), lateral preoptic area (LPO). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "1429 SI-MPO-LPO Lhx8 Gaba_2" EXACT []
