[Term]
id: PCL:0113835
name: SI-MPO-LPO Lhx8 Gaba_5 Npr1 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Chrna2 (Mmus), Abca4 (Mmus), Gpr149 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other SI-MPO-LPO Lhx8 Gaba_5 cells by expression of Npr1. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Striatum ventral region, Pallidum, brain , in or close to the regions: Substantia innominata, Nucleus accumbens . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1455 SI-MPO-LPO Lhx8 Gaba_5." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, SI-MPO-LPO Lhx8 Gaba_5 Npr1 does not have cells in medial preoptic area (MPO), lateral preoptic area (LPO). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "1455 SI-MPO-LPO Lhx8 Gaba_5" EXACT []
