[Term]
id: PCL:0113849
name: MPO-ADP Lhx8 Gaba_3 Th neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Radx (Mmus), Th (Mmus), Lhx8 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MPO-ADP Lhx8 Gaba_3 cells by expression of Th, Radx. It is dopaminergic (inferred from expression of Slc32a1, Ddc, Th, Slc18a2, Gad2, Gad1). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus, brain , in or close to the regions: Periventricular hypothalamic nucleus, preoptic part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1469 MPO-ADP Lhx8 Gaba_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, MPO-ADP Lhx8 Gaba_3 Th does not have cells in anterodorsal preoptic nucleus (ADP). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "1469 MPO-ADP Lhx8 Gaba_3" EXACT []
