[Term]
id: PCL:0113852
name: MPO-ADP Lhx8 Gaba_4 Tac1 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Lhx8 (Mmus), G630016G05Rik (Mmus), Stk32a (Mmus), Gm13481 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MPO-ADP Lhx8 Gaba_4 cells by expression of Tac1, Ntn1. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Ddc). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus, Pallidum , in or close to the regions: Parastrial nucleus, Substantia innominata, Bed nuclei of the stria terminalis . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1472 MPO-ADP Lhx8 Gaba_4." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, MPO-ADP Lhx8 Gaba_4 Tac1 does not have cells in medial preoptic area (MPO). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "1472 MPO-ADP Lhx8 Gaba_4" EXACT []
