[Term]
id: PCL:0113853
name: MPO-ADP Lhx8 Gaba_4 Sst GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Lhx8 (Mmus), Stk32a (Mmus), Masp1 (Mmus), Shroom4 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MPO-ADP Lhx8 Gaba_4 cells by expression of Sst, Lypd6b, Sfta3-ps. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus, Striatum ventral region, Pallidum, brain , in or close to the regions: Substantia innominata, Striatum, Nucleus accumbens . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1473 MPO-ADP Lhx8 Gaba_4." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type MPO-ADP Lhx8 Gaba_4 Sst does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for medial preoptic area (MPO), anterodorsal preoptic nucleus (ADP). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "1473 MPO-ADP Lhx8 Gaba_4" EXACT []
