[Term]
id: PCL:0113870
name: MPN-MPO-LPO Lhx6 Zfhx3 Gaba_2 Lhx8 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Lhx8 (Mmus), Gm29683 (Mmus), Pappa (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MPN-MPO-LPO Lhx6 Zfhx3 Gaba_2 cells by expression of Lhx8, Tac2. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus, Pallidum , in or close to the regions: Lateral preoptic area, Bed nuclei of the stria terminalis . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1490 MPN-MPO-LPO Lhx6 Zfhx3 Gaba_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, MPN-MPO-LPO Lhx6 Zfhx3 Gaba_2 Lhx8 does not have cells in medial preoptic nucleus (MPN), medial preoptic area (MPO). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
