[Term]
id: PCL:0113882
name: BST Tac2 Gaba_2 Lmo2 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Atp2c2 (Mmus), Tac2 (Mmus), Ebf1 (Mmus), Adamtsl1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other BST Tac2 Gaba_2 cells by expression of Lmo2, Penk. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Striatum-like amygdalar nuclei, Pallidum , in or close to the regions: Globus pallidus, external segment, Substantia innominata, Central amygdalar nucleus, medial part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1502 BST Tac2 Gaba_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type BST Tac2 Gaba_2 Lmo2 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for bed nuclei of the stria terminalis (BST). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
