id: PCL:0113898
name: PVR Six3 Sox3 Gaba_4 Glis3 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Sox3 (Mmus), Ntn1 (Mmus), Isl1 (Mmus), C1ql3 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PVR Six3 Sox3 Gaba_4 cells by expression of Glis3, Isl1. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Lateral septal complex, Pallidum , in or close to the regions: Lateral septal nucleus, rostral (rostroventral) part, Lateral septal nucleus, ventral part, Medial septal nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1518 PVR Six3 Sox3 Gaba_4." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type PVR Six3 Sox3 Gaba_4 Glis3 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for periventricular region (PVR). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "1518 PVR Six3 Sox3 Gaba_4" EXACT []
