[Term]
id: PCL:0113921
name: BST-MPN Six3 Nrgn Gaba_3 Prdm12 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Prdm12 (Mmus), Dab2 (Mmus), Gm41414 (Mmus), Reln (Mmus). It is distinguished from other BST-MPN Six3 Nrgn Gaba_3 cells by expression of Prdm12, Reln. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus , in or close to the regions: Medial preoptic nucleus, Medial preoptic area . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1541 BST-MPN Six3 Nrgn Gaba_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, BST-MPN Six3 Nrgn Gaba_3 Prdm12 does not have cells in bed nuclei of the stria terminalis (BST). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "1541 BST-MPN Six3 Nrgn Gaba_3" EXACT []
