[Term]
id: PCL:0113940
name: BST-MPN Six3 Nrgn Gaba_6 Col12a1 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Sytl4 (Mmus), Bnc2 (Mmus), Meis2 (Mmus), Col12a1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other BST-MPN Six3 Nrgn Gaba_6 cells by expression of Col12a1, Bnc2. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Striatum-like amygdalar nuclei, Pallidum , in or close to the regions: Substantia innominata, Bed nuclei of the stria terminalis, Medial amygdalar nucleus, Central amygdalar nucleus, medial part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1560 BST-MPN Six3 Nrgn Gaba_6." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, BST-MPN Six3 Nrgn Gaba_6 Col12a1 does not have cells in medial preoptic nucleus (MPN). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "1560 BST-MPN Six3 Nrgn Gaba_6" EXACT []
