[Term]
id: PCL:0113946
name: BST-MPN Six3 Nrgn Gaba_7 Kit GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Igfbpl1 (Mmus), Prox1 (Mmus), Zan (Mmus), Ptk2b (Mmus). It is distinguished from other BST-MPN Six3 Nrgn Gaba_7 cells by expression of Igfbpl1, Kit. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus , in or close to the regions: Medial preoptic nucleus, Anterior hypothalamic nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1566 BST-MPN Six3 Nrgn Gaba_7." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, BST-MPN Six3 Nrgn Gaba_7 Kit does not have cells in bed nuclei of the stria terminalis (BST). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "1566 BST-MPN Six3 Nrgn Gaba_7" EXACT []
