[Term]
id: PCL:0113952
name: ARH-PVi Six6 Dopa-Gaba_2 dopaminergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A dopaminergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Platr21 (Mmus), 2610028E06Rik (Mmus). It is distinguished from other ARH-PVi Six6 Dopa-Gaba cells by expression of Sncg. It is dopaminergic (inferred from expression of Slc32a1, Ddc, Th, Slc18a2, Gad2, Slc6a3). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus , in or close to the regions: Periventricular hypothalamic nucleus, intermediate part, Retrochiasmatic area, Subparaventricular zone . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1572 ARH-PVi Six6 Dopa-Gaba_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, ARH-PVi Six6 Dopa-Gaba_2 does not have cells in arcuate hypothalamic nucleus (ARH). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "0428 ARH-PVi Six6 Dopa-Gaba_2" EXACT []
synonym: "1572 ARH-PVi Six6 Dopa-Gaba_2" EXACT []
