[Term]
id: PCL:0113998
name: SCH Six6 Cdc14a Gaba_3 Calca SCN pacemaker neuron (Mmus)
def: "A SCN pacemaker neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Six6 (Mmus), Calca (Mmus). It is distinguished from other SCH Six6 Cdc14a Gaba_3 cells by expression of Calca. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus, brain , in or close to the regions: Subparaventricular zone, Anterior hypothalamic nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1618 SCH Six6 Cdc14a Gaba_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type SCH Six6 Cdc14a Gaba_3 Calca does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for suprachiasmatic nucleus (SCH). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "1618 SCH Six6 Cdc14a Gaba_3" EXACT []
