[Term]
id: PCL:0114005
name: PVHd Gsc Gaba GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Gsc (Mmus), Hs3st2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other HY GABA cells by expression of Gsc, Hs3st2. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Slc32a1, Ddc, Slc18a2, Gad2, Gad1). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus , in or close to the regions: Paraventricular hypothalamic nucleus, descending division, Zona incerta, Anterior hypothalamic nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1625 PVHd Gsc Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06808-9, https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Rationale for assigning this type to reference data: Assigned by automated classification (ELK) of a definition built from soma location Hypothalamus (HY; ≥80% of grey-matter cells in both the Yao 2023 and Zhuang 2023 MERFISH atlases) and neurotransmitter GABA (all clusters) against CL 2026-06-08. Basis: NT. Other inferred CL parents: neuron of the forebrain; hypothalamus cell. [WMBO CL promotion round 1, 2026-10-13] Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. {xref="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z", xref="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06808-9"}
