id: PCL:0114012
name: PVHd-SBPV Six3 Prox1 Gaba_1 Npnt GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Aldh1a3 (Mmus), Crhbp (Mmus), Piezo2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PVHd-SBPV Six3 Prox1 Gaba_1 cells by expression of Npnt. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus , in or close to the regions: Lateral hypothalamic area, Perifornical nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1632 PVHd-SBPV Six3 Prox1 Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type PVHd-SBPV Six3 Prox1 Gaba_1 Npnt does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for paraventricular hypothalamic nucleus, descending division (PVHd), subparaventricular zone (SBPV). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "1632 PVHd-SBPV Six3 Prox1 Gaba_1" EXACT []
