[Term]
id: PCL:0114063
name: SBPV-PVa Six6 Satb2 Gaba_1 Msn neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Cd79a (Mmus), Krt90 (Mmus), Trhr (Mmus). It is distinguished from other SBPV-PVa Six6 Satb2 Gaba_1 cells by expression of Msn. It is dopaminergic (inferred from expression of Slc32a1, Ddc, Th, Slc18a2, Gad2, Gad1). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus , in or close to the regions: Periventricular hypothalamic nucleus, preoptic part, Arcuate hypothalamic nucleus, Medial preoptic nucleus, Ventromedial hypothalamic nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1683 SBPV-PVa Six6 Satb2 Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type SBPV-PVa Six6 Satb2 Gaba_1 Msn does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for subparaventricular zone (SBPV), periventricular hypothalamic nucleus, anterior part (PVa). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "1683 SBPV-PVa Six6 Satb2 Gaba_1" EXACT []
