[Term]
id: PCL:0114081
name: AHN Onecut3 Gaba_1 Cckar GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Six6 (Mmus), Cckar (Mmus), Gm41414 (Mmus), Fbn2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other AHN Onecut3 Gaba_1 cells by expression of Cckar, Lhx1os. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Ddc). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus , in or close to the regions: Suprachiasmatic nucleus, Subparaventricular zone, Anterior hypothalamic nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1701 AHN Onecut3 Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
