[Term]
id: PCL:0114088
name: AHN Onecut3 Gaba_2 Npsr1 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Onecut3 (Mmus), Dlx1 (Mmus), Npsr1 (Mmus), Grm8 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other AHN Onecut3 Gaba_2 cells by expression of Npsr1, D930028M14Rik. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Slc32a1, Ddc, Slc18a2, Gad2, Gad1). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus , in or close to the regions: Anterior hypothalamic nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1708 AHN Onecut3 Gaba_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
