[Term]
id: PCL:0114091
name: AHN Onecut3 Gaba_3 Kcnj5 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Onecut3 (Mmus), Thbs4 (Mmus), Hmcn1 (Mmus), Kcnj5 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other AHN Onecut3 Gaba_3 cells by expression of Kcnj5. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Ddc). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus, Pallidum , in or close to the regions: Retrochiasmatic area, Lateral preoptic area, Anterior hypothalamic nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1711 AHN Onecut3 Gaba_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
