[Term]
id: PCL:0114111
name: GPi core neuron (Mmus)
def: "A internal globus pallidus core projecting neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Chrnb3 (Mmus), Sp8 (Mmus), Sfta3-ps (Mmus). It is distinguished from other ZI Pax6 Gaba_3 cells by expression of Chrnb3. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Pallidum, brain , in or close to the regions: Globus pallidus, internal segment, internal capsule . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1731 ZI Pax6 Gaba_3." [https://doi.org/10.1016/j.neuron.2017.03.017, https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Rationale for assigning this type to reference data: Mapping to the general type GPi core (internal globus pallidus core projecting neuron) is based on location (soma in GPi, nested inside GPi shell neurons), prediced GABA neurotransmitter, Pvalb expression, and MapMyCells hierarchical annotation transfer mapping to primate GPi core (CS20250428_GROUP_0015). Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type ZI Pax6 Gaba_3 Chrnb3 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for zona incerta (ZI). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme. {xref="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.neuron.2017.03.017"}
synonym: "1731 ZI Pax6 Gaba_3" EXACT []
