[Term]
id: PCL:0114153
name: ZI Pax6 Gaba_8 Podn GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Podn (Mmus), Npffr1 (Mmus), Sall1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other ZI Pax6 Gaba_8 cells by expression of Podn, Adamtsl1. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus, Thalamus , in or close to the regions: Paraventricular hypothalamic nucleus, descending division, Zona incerta . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1773 ZI Pax6 Gaba_8." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
