id: PCL:0114154
name: ZI Pax6 Gaba_8 Nfib GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Pax6 (Mmus), Pgr15l (Mmus), Bmp3 (Mmus), Irs4 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other ZI Pax6 Gaba_8 cells by expression of Nfib, Irs4. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus, Thalamus , in or close to the regions: Perireunensis nucleus, Nucleus of reuniens, Zona incerta . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1774 ZI Pax6 Gaba_8." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
