[Term]
id: PCL:0114162
name: ZI Pax6 Gaba_11 Tmc1 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Tmc1 (Mmus), Onecut3 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other ZI Pax6 Gaba_11 cells by expression of Tmc1, Prdm12. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus, Thalamus , in or close to the regions: Dorsal part of the lateral geniculate complex, core, Zona incerta, Fields of Forel . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1782 ZI Pax6 Gaba_11." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
