name: DMH-LHA Gsx1 Gaba_2 Tac2 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Nkx2-4 (Mmus), Tac2 (Mmus), Hmx2 (Mmus), Otof (Mmus). It is distinguished from other DMH-LHA Gsx1 Gaba_2 cells by expression of Tac2, Dchs2. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Ddc). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus , in or close to the regions: Lateral hypothalamic area, Paraventricular hypothalamic nucleus, descending division . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1800 DMH-LHA Gsx1 Gaba_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
