[Term]
id: PCL:0114182
name: DMH-LHA Gsx1 Gaba_2 Crh GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Gsx1 (Mmus), Crh (Mmus), St18 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other DMH-LHA Gsx1 Gaba_2 cells by expression of Crh. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus , in or close to the regions: Lateral hypothalamic area, Perifornical nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1802 DMH-LHA Gsx1 Gaba_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, DMH-LHA Gsx1 Gaba_2 Crh does not have cells in dorsomedial nucleus of the hypothalamus (DMH). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "1802 DMH-LHA Gsx1 Gaba_2" EXACT []
is_a: PCL:0111041 ! DMH-LHA Gsx1 Gaba_2 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
relationship: RO:0002215 GO:0061534 {comment="Inferred to be gamma-aminobutyric acid secretion, neurotransmission based on expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1"}
