[Term]
id: PCL:0114190
name: DMH-LHA Gsx1 Gaba_3 cholinergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A cholinergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Ghrh (Mmus), Gsx1 (Mmus), Slc18a3 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other DMH-LHA Gsx1 Gaba cells by expression of Slc18a3. It is cholinergic (inferred from expression of Ddc, Th, Slc18a3, Slc32a1, Chat, Gad2, Gad1). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus , in or close to the regions: Arcuate hypothalamic nucleus, Ventromedial hypothalamic nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1810 DMH-LHA Gsx1 Gaba_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06808-9, https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Rationale for assigning this type to reference data: Assigned by automated classification (ELK) of a definition built from soma location Hypothalamus (HY; ≥80% of grey-matter cells in both the Yao 2023 and Zhuang 2023 MERFISH atlases) and neurotransmitter acetylcholine (all clusters) against CL 2026-06-08. Basis: NT. Other inferred CL parents: neuron of the forebrain; hypothalamus cell. [WMBO CL promotion round 1, 2026-10-13] Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type DMH-LHA Gsx1 Gaba_3 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for dorsomedial nucleus of the hypothalamus (DMH), lateral hypothalamic area (LHA). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme. {xref="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z", xref="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06808-9"}
