[Term]
id: PCL:0114221
name: TU-ARH Otp Six6 Gaba_1 Dnah8 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Six6 (Mmus), Dnah8 (Mmus), Otp (Mmus). It is distinguished from other TU-ARH Otp Six6 Gaba_1 cells by expression of Dnah8. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus , in or close to the regions: Arcuate hypothalamic nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1841 TU-ARH Otp Six6 Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, TU-ARH Otp Six6 Gaba_1 Dnah8 does not have cells in tuberal nucleus (TU). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
