[Term]
id: PCL:0114238
name: TU-ARH Otp Six6 Gaba_3 Pou3f1 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Six6 (Mmus), Scn11a (Mmus), Zeb2 (Mmus), Kcnj5 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other TU-ARH Otp Six6 Gaba_3 cells by expression of Pou3f1, Kcnj5. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus , in or close to the regions: Lateral hypothalamic area, Perifornical nucleus, Tuberal nucleus, Anterior hypothalamic nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1858 TU-ARH Otp Six6 Gaba_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, TU-ARH Otp Six6 Gaba_3 Pou3f1 does not have cells in arcuate hypothalamic nucleus (ARH). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "1858 TU-ARH Otp Six6 Gaba_3" EXACT []
