[Term]
id: PCL:0114273
name: PVpo-VMPO-MPN Hmx2 Gaba_2 Mafb GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Tac2 (Mmus), Esr2 (Mmus), Irs4 (Mmus), Pappa (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PVpo-VMPO-MPN Hmx2 Gaba_2 cells by expression of Mafb, Tac2, Gal. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus , in or close to the regions: Bed nuclei of the stria terminalis, Medial preoptic nucleus, Medial preoptic area . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1893 PVpo-VMPO-MPN Hmx2 Gaba_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, PVpo-VMPO-MPN Hmx2 Gaba_2 Mafb does not have cells in periventricular hypothalamic nucleus, preoptic part (PVpo), ventromedial preoptic nucleus (VMPO). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "1893 PVpo-VMPO-MPN Hmx2 Gaba_2" EXACT []
