[Term]
id: PCL:0114285
name: PVpo-VMPO-MPN Hmx2 Gaba_3 Nms neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Prdm13 (Mmus), Nms (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PVpo-VMPO-MPN Hmx2 Gaba_3 cells by expression of Nms. It is dopaminergic (inferred from expression of Slc32a1, Ddc, Th, Slc18a2, Gad2, Gad1). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus, brain , in or close to the regions: fiber tracts, anterior commissure, temporal limb . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1905 PVpo-VMPO-MPN Hmx2 Gaba_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type PVpo-VMPO-MPN Hmx2 Gaba_3 Nms does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for periventricular hypothalamic nucleus, preoptic part (PVpo), ventromedial preoptic nucleus (VMPO), medial preoptic nucleus (MPN). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "1905 PVpo-VMPO-MPN Hmx2 Gaba_3" EXACT []
