[Term]
id: PCL:0114288
name: PVpo-VMPO-MPN Hmx2 Gaba_3 Met neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Apoc3 (Mmus), Met (Mmus), Prok2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PVpo-VMPO-MPN Hmx2 Gaba_3 cells by expression of Met. It is dopaminergic (inferred from expression of Slc32a1, Ddc, Th, Slc18a2, Gad2, Gad1). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus , in or close to the regions: third ventricle, Periventricular hypothalamic nucleus, preoptic part, Medial preoptic nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1908 PVpo-VMPO-MPN Hmx2 Gaba_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, PVpo-VMPO-MPN Hmx2 Gaba_3 Met does not have cells in ventromedial preoptic nucleus (VMPO). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "1908 PVpo-VMPO-MPN Hmx2 Gaba_3" EXACT []
