[Term]
id: PCL:0114289
name: PVpo-VMPO-MPN Hmx2 Gaba_3 Grm8 neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Prdm13 (Mmus), Frem1 (Mmus), Epb41l4a (Mmus), Hmx3 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PVpo-VMPO-MPN Hmx2 Gaba_3 cells by expression of Prdm13, Grm8. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus , in or close to the regions: Periventricular hypothalamic nucleus, preoptic part, Bed nuclei of the stria terminalis, Medial preoptic nucleus, Medial preoptic area . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1909 PVpo-VMPO-MPN Hmx2 Gaba_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, PVpo-VMPO-MPN Hmx2 Gaba_3 Grm8 does not have cells in ventromedial preoptic nucleus (VMPO). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "1909 PVpo-VMPO-MPN Hmx2 Gaba_3" EXACT []
