id: PCL:0114304
name: DMH Hmx2 Gaba_1 Sostdc1 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Bsx (Mmus), Glra4 (Mmus), Tmem114 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other DMH Hmx2 Gaba_1 cells by expression of Sostdc1, Bsx. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus , in or close to the regions: Lateral hypothalamic area . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1924 DMH Hmx2 Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type DMH Hmx2 Gaba_1 Sostdc1 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for dorsomedial nucleus of the hypothalamus (DMH). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
