[Term]
id: PCL:0114316
name: DMH Hmx2 Gaba_2 Map3k19 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Apoc3 (Mmus), Eya4 (Mmus), Tac1 (Mmus), Asb4 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other DMH Hmx2 Gaba_2 cells by expression of Map3k19, Apoc3, Kl. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus , in or close to the regions: Periventricular hypothalamic nucleus, intermediate part, Arcuate hypothalamic nucleus, Ventromedial hypothalamic nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1936 DMH Hmx2 Gaba_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
