[Term]
id: PCL:0114359
name: LGv-ZI Otx2 Gaba_3 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Slc10a4 (Mmus), P2rx5 (Mmus), Ctxn3 (Mmus), Reln (Mmus). It is distinguished from other LGv-ZI Otx2 Gaba cells by expression of Egr3. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Thalamus, brain , in or close to the regions: fiber tracts, Ventral part of the lateral geniculate complex . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1979 LGv-ZI Otx2 Gaba_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, LGv-ZI Otx2 Gaba_3 does not have cells in zona incerta (ZI). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
