[Term]
id: PCL:0114370
name: TRS-BAC Sln Glut_1 Sost glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Sln (Mmus), Sost (Mmus). It is distinguished from other TRS-BAC Sln Glut_1 cells by expression of Sost. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Slc17a7). These cells are located in the Lateral septal complex, brain , in or close to the regions: third ventricle, Septofimbrial nucleus, ventral hippocampal commissure, Triangular nucleus of septum . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1990 TRS-BAC Sln Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, TRS-BAC Sln Glut_1 Sost does not have cells in bed nucleus of the anterior commissure (BAC). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "1990 TRS-BAC Sln Glut_1" EXACT []
