[Term]
id: PCL:0114383
name: MEA-COA-BMA Ccdc42 Glut_1 Arhgap36 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Krt9 (Mmus), Arhgap36 (Mmus), Pappa (Mmus), Medag (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MEA-COA-BMA Ccdc42 Glut_1 cells by expression of Zeb2, Arhgap36. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Slc17a7). These cells are located in the Striatum-like amygdalar nuclei, Cortical subplate , in or close to the regions: Intercalated amygdalar nucleus, Basomedial amygdalar nucleus, anterior part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2003 MEA-COA-BMA Ccdc42 Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, MEA-COA-BMA Ccdc42 Glut_1 Arhgap36 does not have cells in medial amygdalar nucleus (MEA). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "2003 MEA-COA-BMA Ccdc42 Glut_1" EXACT []
