[Term]
id: PCL:0114404
name: COAa-PAA-MEA Barhl2 Glut_2 Piezo2 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Vmn1r206 (Mmus), Pappa2 (Mmus), Stac (Mmus). It is distinguished from other COAa-PAA-MEA Barhl2 Glut_2 cells by expression of Piezo2, Vmn1r206. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Isocortex, Olfactory areas, Cortical subplate , in or close to the regions: Piriform area . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2024 COAa-PAA-MEA Barhl2 Glut_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, COAa-PAA-MEA Barhl2 Glut_2 Piezo2 does not have cells in medial amygdalar nucleus (MEA). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
