[Term]
id: PCL:0114405
name: COAa-PAA-MEA Barhl2 Glut_2 Hs3st3b1 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Gja3 (Mmus), Col24a1 (Mmus), Runx1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other COAa-PAA-MEA Barhl2 Glut_2 cells by expression of Hs3st3b1, C1ql1. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Olfactory areas, Cortical subplate , in or close to the regions: Anterior amygdalar area, Basomedial amygdalar nucleus, anterior part, Endopiriform nucleus, ventral part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2025 COAa-PAA-MEA Barhl2 Glut_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, COAa-PAA-MEA Barhl2 Glut_2 Hs3st3b1 does not have cells in piriform-amygdalar area (PAA), medial amygdalar nucleus (MEA). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
