[Term]
id: PCL:0114412
name: COAa-PAA-MEA Barhl2 Glut_4 Nts glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Tfap2c (Mmus), Hmcn1 (Mmus), Pappa2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other COAa-PAA-MEA Barhl2 Glut_4 cells by expression of Nts. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Striatum-like amygdalar nuclei, Olfactory areas, Cortical subplate , in or close to the regions: Piriform area, Endopiriform nucleus, ventral part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2032 COAa-PAA-MEA Barhl2 Glut_4." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, COAa-PAA-MEA Barhl2 Glut_4 Nts does not have cells in cortical amygdalar area, anterior part (COAa), piriform-amygdalar area (PAA). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
