[Term]
id: PCL:0114413
name: COAa-PAA-MEA Barhl2 Glut_4 Pnoc glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Tfap2c (Mmus), Cd24a (Mmus), Npffr1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other COAa-PAA-MEA Barhl2 Glut_4 cells by expression of Pnoc, Tfap2c. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Slc17a7). These cells are located in the Olfactory areas, Cortical subplate, brain , in or close to the regions: Anterior olfactory nucleus, Endopiriform nucleus, dorsal part, Piriform area, Endopiriform nucleus, ventral part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2033 COAa-PAA-MEA Barhl2 Glut_4." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type COAa-PAA-MEA Barhl2 Glut_4 Pnoc does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for cortical amygdalar area, anterior part (COAa), piriform-amygdalar area (PAA), medial amygdalar nucleus (MEA). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "2033 COAa-PAA-MEA Barhl2 Glut_4" EXACT []
