[Term]
id: PCL:0114419
name: COAa-PAA-MEA Barhl2 Glut_6 Cort glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Vmn1r200 (Mmus), Trpa1 (Mmus), Cort (Mmus). It is distinguished from other COAa-PAA-MEA Barhl2 Glut_6 cells by expression of Vmn1r200, Cort. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Slc17a7). These cells are located in the Isocortex, Olfactory areas , in or close to the regions: Piriform area . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2039 COAa-PAA-MEA Barhl2 Glut_6." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, COAa-PAA-MEA Barhl2 Glut_6 Cort does not have cells in cortical amygdalar area, anterior part (COAa), medial amygdalar nucleus (MEA). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "2039 COAa-PAA-MEA Barhl2 Glut_6" EXACT []
