[Term]
id: PCL:0114420
name: COAa-PAA-MEA Barhl2 Glut_6 Sla glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Trdn (Mmus), Pappa2 (Mmus), Arhgap36 (Mmus), Scn5a (Mmus). It is distinguished from other COAa-PAA-MEA Barhl2 Glut_6 cells by expression of Sla, Gpr83. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Olfactory areas, Cortical subplate , in or close to the regions: Basolateral amygdalar nucleus, anterior part, Basomedial amygdalar nucleus, anterior part, Endopiriform nucleus, ventral part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2040 COAa-PAA-MEA Barhl2 Glut_6." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, COAa-PAA-MEA Barhl2 Glut_6 Sla does not have cells in cortical amygdalar area, anterior part (COAa), piriform-amygdalar area (PAA). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "2040 COAa-PAA-MEA Barhl2 Glut_6" EXACT []
