[Term]
id: PCL:0114421
name: COAa-PAA-MEA Barhl2 Glut_7 Hgf glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Emx2 (Mmus), 6430628N08Rik (Mmus), Cck (Mmus), Col6a3 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other COAa-PAA-MEA Barhl2 Glut_7 cells by expression of Hgf, Oprk1. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Striatum-like amygdalar nuclei, brain , in or close to the regions: Basomedial amygdalar nucleus, anterior part, Medial amygdalar nucleus, Striatum, Central amygdalar nucleus, medial part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2041 COAa-PAA-MEA Barhl2 Glut_7." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, COAa-PAA-MEA Barhl2 Glut_7 Hgf does not have cells in cortical amygdalar area, anterior part (COAa), piriform-amygdalar area (PAA). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
