[Term]
id: PCL:0114427
name: COAa-PAA-MEA Barhl2 Glut_7 Adam34 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Adam34 (Mmus), Tbr1 (Mmus), C1ql1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other COAa-PAA-MEA Barhl2 Glut_7 cells by expression of Adam34, C1ql1. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Ddc, Th). These cells are located in the Striatum-like amygdalar nuclei, Pallidum , in or close to the regions: Anterior amygdalar area, Magnocellular nucleus, Diagonal band nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2047 COAa-PAA-MEA Barhl2 Glut_7." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type COAa-PAA-MEA Barhl2 Glut_7 Adam34 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for cortical amygdalar area, anterior part (COAa), piriform-amygdalar area (PAA), medial amygdalar nucleus (MEA). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "2047 COAa-PAA-MEA Barhl2 Glut_7" EXACT []
