[Term]
id: PCL:0114439
name: MS-SF Bsx Glut_1 D030045P18Rik glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Fgf8 (Mmus), D030045P18Rik (Mmus), Kcnj5 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MS-SF Bsx Glut cells by expression of D030045P18Rik, Gpr149. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Lateral septal complex, Pallidum , in or close to the regions: Lateral septal nucleus, rostral (rostroventral) part, Lateral septal nucleus, ventral part, Medial septal nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2059 MS-SF Bsx Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, MS-SF Bsx Glut_1 D030045P18Rik does not have cells in septofimbrial nucleus (SF). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "2059 MS-SF Bsx Glut_1" EXACT []
is_a: PCL:0111088 ! MS-SF Bsx Glut glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
