[Term]
id: PCL:0114440
name: MS-SF Bsx Glut_1 Angpt1 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Bsx (Mmus), Fam163a (Mmus), Otx2 (Mmus), Kcnj5 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MS-SF Bsx Glut cells by expression of Angpt1, Calb1. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Gad2). These cells are located in the Lateral septal complex, Pallidum , in or close to the regions: Lateral septal nucleus, rostral (rostroventral) part, Striatum, Medial septal nucleus, Diagonal band nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2060 MS-SF Bsx Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, MS-SF Bsx Glut_1 Angpt1 does not have cells in septofimbrial nucleus (SF). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "2060 MS-SF Bsx Glut_1" EXACT []
