[Term]
id: PCL:0114448
name: MS-SF Bsx Glut_1 Nkx2-1 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Radx (Mmus), Otx2 (Mmus), Ankrd63 (Mmus), Sfta3-ps (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MS-SF Bsx Glut cells by expression of Nkx2-1. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Slc17a6, Gad1). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus, Lateral septal complex, Pallidum , in or close to the regions: Lateral septal nucleus, ventral part, Medial preoptic area, Medial septal nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2068 MS-SF Bsx Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, MS-SF Bsx Glut_1 Nkx2-1 does not have cells in septofimbrial nucleus (SF). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
