[Term]
id: PCL:0114474
name: AVPV-MEPO-SFO Tbr1 Glut_4 Brs3 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Elf4 (Mmus), Brs3 (Mmus), Trh (Mmus). It is distinguished from other AVPV-MEPO-SFO Tbr1 Glut_4 cells by expression of Brs3, Trh. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus, Pallidum , in or close to the regions: Anteroventral periventricular nucleus, Median preoptic nucleus, Medial septal nucleus, brain . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2094 AVPV-MEPO-SFO Tbr1 Glut_4." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, AVPV-MEPO-SFO Tbr1 Glut_4 Brs3 does not have cells in subfornical organ (SFO). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "2094 AVPV-MEPO-SFO Tbr1 Glut_4" EXACT []
