id: PCL:0114477
name: AVPV-MEPO-SFO Tbr1 Glut_5 5830418P13Rik glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Gm31938 (Mmus), Crhr2 (Mmus), Neto1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other AVPV-MEPO-SFO Tbr1 Glut_5 cells by expression of 5830418P13Rik, Grin2a. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Olfactory areas, Pallidum, brain , in or close to the regions: Diagonal band nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2097 AVPV-MEPO-SFO Tbr1 Glut_5." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type AVPV-MEPO-SFO Tbr1 Glut_5 5830418P13Rik does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for anteroventral periventricular nucleus (AVPV), median preoptic nucleus (MEPO), subfornical organ (SFO). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
