id: PCL:0114484
name: LHA Barhl2 Glut_1 Clrn1 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Clrn1 (Mmus), Barhl2 (Mmus), Htr1d (Mmus), Tbr1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other LHA Barhl2 Glut_1 cells by expression of Clrn1. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus, Pallidum , in or close to the regions: Lateral preoptic area, Magnocellular nucleus, Diagonal band nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2104 LHA Barhl2 Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type LHA Barhl2 Glut_1 Clrn1 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for lateral hypothalamic area (LHA). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
