[Term]
id: PCL:0114526
name: SI-MA-LPO-LHA Skor1 Glut_2 Ngfr glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Dmrta2 (Mmus), Prokr2 (Mmus), Ngfr (Mmus), Itga8 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other SI-MA-LPO-LHA Skor1 Glut_2 cells by expression of Ngfr, Syt6. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus, Striatum-like amygdalar nuclei, Pallidum , in or close to the regions: Lateral preoptic area, Anterior amygdalar area, Substantia innominata, Central amygdalar nucleus, medial part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2146 SI-MA-LPO-LHA Skor1 Glut_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, SI-MA-LPO-LHA Skor1 Glut_2 Ngfr does not have cells in magnocellular nucleus (MA), lateral hypothalamic area (LHA). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "2146 SI-MA-LPO-LHA Skor1 Glut_2" EXACT []
