[Term]
id: PCL:0114547
name: SI-MA-LPO-LHA Skor1 Glut_4 Arhgap36 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Il31ra (Mmus), Rxfp3 (Mmus), Daam2 (Mmus), Galr1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other SI-MA-LPO-LHA Skor1 Glut_4 cells by expression of Arhgap36, Sntb1, Kcnh8, Galr1. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Pallidum , in or close to the regions: Substantia innominata . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2167 SI-MA-LPO-LHA Skor1 Glut_4." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, SI-MA-LPO-LHA Skor1 Glut_4 Arhgap36 does not have cells in magnocellular nucleus (MA), lateral preoptic area (LPO), lateral hypothalamic area (LHA). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
