name: SI-MA-LPO-LHA Skor1 Glut_5 Otx1 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Dmrta2 (Mmus), Piezo2 (Mmus), Tnc (Mmus). It is distinguished from other SI-MA-LPO-LHA Skor1 Glut_5 cells by expression of Otx1, Ankfn1. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Gad2). These cells are located in the Striatum ventral region, Pallidum , in or close to the regions: Substantia innominata, Nucleus accumbens . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2173 SI-MA-LPO-LHA Skor1 Glut_5." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, SI-MA-LPO-LHA Skor1 Glut_5 Otx1 does not have cells in magnocellular nucleus (MA), lateral preoptic area (LPO), lateral hypothalamic area (LHA). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "2173 SI-MA-LPO-LHA Skor1 Glut_5" EXACT []
