id: PCL:0114620
name: MPN-MPO-PVpo Hmx2 Glut_2 Mkx glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Csta2 (Mmus), Nptx2 (Mmus), Gm38505 (Mmus), Cartpt (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MPN-MPO-PVpo Hmx2 Glut_2 cells by expression of Mkx, Nkd2, Gpr83. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Gad2). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus , in or close to the regions: Bed nuclei of the stria terminalis, Medial preoptic nucleus, Medial preoptic area . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2240 MPN-MPO-PVpo Hmx2 Glut_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, MPN-MPO-PVpo Hmx2 Glut_2 Mkx does not have cells in periventricular hypothalamic nucleus, preoptic part (PVpo). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
