[Term]
id: PCL:0114637
name: MPN-MPO-PVpo Hmx2 Glut_5 Gpr50 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Radx (Mmus), Gpr50 (Mmus), Calcr (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MPN-MPO-PVpo Hmx2 Glut_5 cells by expression of Gpr50, Calcr. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus, brain , in or close to the regions: fiber tracts, Anteroventral periventricular nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2257 MPN-MPO-PVpo Hmx2 Glut_5." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type MPN-MPO-PVpo Hmx2 Glut_5 Gpr50 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for medial preoptic nucleus (MPN), medial preoptic area (MPO), periventricular hypothalamic nucleus, preoptic part (PVpo). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "2257 MPN-MPO-PVpo Hmx2 Glut_5" EXACT []
