[Term]
id: PCL:0114638
name: MPN-MPO-PVpo Hmx2 Glut_5 Grid2ip glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Csta2 (Mmus), Eomes (Mmus), Nts (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MPN-MPO-PVpo Hmx2 Glut_5 cells by expression of Grid2ip, Csta2. It is glutamatergic and GABAergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Gad2, Slc18a2). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus , in or close to the regions: Periventricular hypothalamic nucleus, preoptic part, Anteroventral periventricular nucleus, Vascular organ of the lamina terminalis, brain . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2258 MPN-MPO-PVpo Hmx2 Glut_5." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, MPN-MPO-PVpo Hmx2 Glut_5 Grid2ip does not have cells in medial preoptic nucleus (MPN), medial preoptic area (MPO). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "2258 MPN-MPO-PVpo Hmx2 Glut_5" EXACT []
