name: DMH-LHA Vgll2 Glut_3 Qrfp glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Qrfp (Mmus), Isl1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other DMH-LHA Vgll2 Glut_3 cells by expression of Qrfp, Isl1. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Gad1, Ddc, Gad2). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus , in or close to the regions: Periventricular hypothalamic nucleus, intermediate part, Tuberal nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2287 DMH-LHA Vgll2 Glut_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
