[Term]
id: PCL:0114689
name: VMH Nr5a1 Glut_2 Npy2r glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Nr5a1 (Mmus), Npy2r (Mmus), Prdm12 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other VMH Nr5a1 Glut_2 cells by expression of Npy2r, Prdm12. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Gad2, Ddc). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus, brain , in or close to the regions: fiber tracts, optic chiasm, Lateral hypothalamic area, Tuberal nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2309 VMH Nr5a1 Glut_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type VMH Nr5a1 Glut_2 Npy2r does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for ventromedial hypothalamic nucleus (VMH). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "2309 VMH Nr5a1 Glut_2" EXACT []
