[Term]
id: PCL:0114713
name: LHA-AHN-PVH Otp Trh Glut_2 Tac1 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Sim2 (Mmus), Cxcl14 (Mmus), Npy2r (Mmus). It is distinguished from other LHA-AHN-PVH Otp Trh Glut_2 cells by expression of Tac1, Epsti1. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Ddc, Th). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus , in or close to the regions: Medial preoptic nucleus, Medial preoptic area . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2333 LHA-AHN-PVH Otp Trh Glut_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, LHA-AHN-PVH Otp Trh Glut_2 Tac1 does not have cells in anterior hypothalamic nucleus (AHN). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
