[Term]
id: PCL:0114749
name: PVH-SO-PVa Otp Glut_2 Gch1 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Brs3 (Mmus), Trh (Mmus), Cartpt (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PVH-SO-PVa Otp Glut_2 cells by expression of Gch1. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus , in or close to the regions: Paraventricular hypothalamic nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2369 PVH-SO-PVa Otp Glut_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, PVH-SO-PVa Otp Glut_2 Gch1 does not have cells in supraoptic nucleus (SO), periventricular hypothalamic nucleus, anterior part (PVa). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
