[Term]
id: PCL:0114752
name: PVH-SO-PVa Otp Glut_2 Tcf24 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Tcf24 (Mmus), Chst9 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PVH-SO-PVa Otp Glut_2 cells by expression of Tcf24. It is glutamatergic and GABAergic (inferred from expression of Ddc, Slc17a6, Slc18a2, Gad2). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus , in or close to the regions: Paraventricular hypothalamic nucleus, descending division, Dorsomedial nucleus of the hypothalamus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2372 PVH-SO-PVa Otp Glut_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type PVH-SO-PVa Otp Glut_2 Tcf24 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for paraventricular hypothalamic nucleus (PVH), supraoptic nucleus (SO), periventricular hypothalamic nucleus, anterior part (PVa). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
