[Term]
id: PCL:0114765
name: PVH-SO-PVa Otp Glut_6 Ucn3 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Ucn3 (Mmus), Slitrk6 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PVH-SO-PVa Otp Glut_6 cells by expression of Ucn3, Penk. These cells are located in the Hypothalamus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2385 PVH-SO-PVa Otp Glut_6." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type PVH-SO-PVa Otp Glut_6 Ucn3 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for paraventricular hypothalamic nucleus (PVH), supraoptic nucleus (SO), periventricular hypothalamic nucleus, anterior part (PVa). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme. Warning: Despite its name, PVH-SO-PVa Otp Glut_6 Ucn3 does not secrete the neurotransmitter Glut, as assessed by expression of multiple marker genes.
synonym: "2385 PVH-SO-PVa Otp Glut_6" EXACT []
