[Term]
id: PCL:0114766
name: PVH-SO-PVa Otp Glut_6 6430628N08Rik glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Ucn3 (Mmus), Mc4r (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PVH-SO-PVa Otp Glut_6 cells by expression of 6430628N08Rik. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus, Pallidum , in or close to the regions: Bed nuclei of the stria terminalis, Paraventricular hypothalamic nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2386 PVH-SO-PVa Otp Glut_6." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, PVH-SO-PVa Otp Glut_6 6430628N08Rik does not have cells in supraoptic nucleus (SO), periventricular hypothalamic nucleus, anterior part (PVa). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "2386 PVH-SO-PVa Otp Glut_6" EXACT []
