name: PH-ant-LHA Otp Bsx Glut_1 Gpr88 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Sim1 (Mmus), Trbc2 (Mmus), Abtb2 (Mmus), Otp (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PH-ant-LHA Otp Bsx Glut_1 cells by expression of Gpr88, Trbc2. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus , in or close to the regions: Posterior hypothalamic nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2394 PH-ant-LHA Otp Bsx Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
