[Term]
id: PCL:0114775
name: PH-ant-LHA Otp Bsx Glut_2 Zbbx glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Bsx (Mmus), Uncx (Mmus), Nkx2-4 (Mmus), Htr1b (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PH-ant-LHA Otp Bsx Glut_2 cells by expression of Zbbx, Epb41l4a, Lhx1. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus , in or close to the regions: Periventricular hypothalamic nucleus, posterior part, Tuberal nucleus, Ventromedial hypothalamic nucleus, Dorsomedial nucleus of the hypothalamus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2395 PH-ant-LHA Otp Bsx Glut_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, PH-ant-LHA Otp Bsx Glut_2 Zbbx does not have cells in posterior hypothalamic nucleus (PH), lateral hypothalamic area (LHA). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "2395 PH-ant-LHA Otp Bsx Glut_2" EXACT []
