name: PH-ant-LHA Otp Bsx Glut_2 Cgnl1 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Bsx (Mmus), Npas1 (Mmus), Cgnl1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PH-ant-LHA Otp Bsx Glut_2 cells by expression of Cgnl1, Dach2. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus , in or close to the regions: Lateral hypothalamic area . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2399 PH-ant-LHA Otp Bsx Glut_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, PH-ant-LHA Otp Bsx Glut_2 Cgnl1 does not have cells in posterior hypothalamic nucleus (PH). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "2399 PH-ant-LHA Otp Bsx Glut_2" EXACT []
