[Term]
id: PCL:0114825
name: STN-PSTN Pitx2 Glut_3 Onecut1 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Pitx2 (Mmus), Slc10a4 (Mmus), Wnt7b (Mmus), 4930438E09Rik (Mmus). It is distinguished from other STN-PSTN Pitx2 Glut_3 cells by expression of Onecut1, Gabrq. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Gad2, Ddc). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus , in or close to the regions: Lateral hypothalamic area, Subthalamic nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2445 STN-PSTN Pitx2 Glut_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, STN-PSTN Pitx2 Glut_3 Onecut1 does not have cells in parasubthalamic nucleus (PSTN). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
