[Term]
id: PCL:0114829
name: STN-PSTN Pitx2 Glut_4 Zeb2 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Esm1 (Mmus), Mtnr1a (Mmus), Slc35d3 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other STN-PSTN Pitx2 Glut_4 cells by expression of Zeb2, Esm1. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus , in or close to the regions: Lateral hypothalamic area, Parasubthalamic nucleus, Dorsomedial nucleus of the hypothalamus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2449 STN-PSTN Pitx2 Glut_4." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, STN-PSTN Pitx2 Glut_4 Zeb2 does not have cells in subthalamic nucleus (STN). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "2449 STN-PSTN Pitx2 Glut_4" EXACT []
