[Term]
id: PCL:0114838
name: STN-PSTN Pitx2 Glut_6 Lef1 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of 4921518K17Rik (Mmus), Lef1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other STN-PSTN Pitx2 Glut_6 cells by expression of Lef1. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus , in or close to the regions: Medial mammillary nucleus, lateral part, Medial mammillary nucleus, dorsal part, Medial mammillary nucleus, median part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2458 STN-PSTN Pitx2 Glut_6." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type STN-PSTN Pitx2 Glut_6 Lef1 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for subthalamic nucleus (STN), parasubthalamic nucleus (PSTN). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
