name: PMv-TMv Pitx2 Glut_1 Barhl2 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Cd36 (Mmus), Barhl2 (Mmus), 1700028P14Rik (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PMv-TMv Pitx2 Glut_1 cells by expression of Barhl2, 1700028P14Rik. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Ddc). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus , in or close to the regions: Ventromedial hypothalamic nucleus, Dorsomedial nucleus of the hypothalamus, Posterior hypothalamic nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2460 PMv-TMv Pitx2 Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type PMv-TMv Pitx2 Glut_1 Barhl2 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for ventral premammillary nucleus (PMv), tuberomammillary nucleus, ventral part (TMv). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
