[Term]
id: PCL:0114851
name: PMv-TMv Pitx2 Glut_3 Slc6a3 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Slc6a3 (Mmus), Irx6 (Mmus), Sema3e (Mmus), Stxbp6 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PMv-TMv Pitx2 Glut_3 cells by expression of Slc6a3, Sema3e, Stxbp6. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Slc18a2, Ddc, Slc6a3). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus , in or close to the regions: Tuberal nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2471 PMv-TMv Pitx2 Glut_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type PMv-TMv Pitx2 Glut_3 Slc6a3 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for ventral premammillary nucleus (PMv), tuberomammillary nucleus, ventral part (TMv). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "2471 PMv-TMv Pitx2 Glut_3" EXACT []
