[Term]
id: PCL:0114896
name: PH-LHA Foxb1 Glut_4 Glis3 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Foxb1 (Mmus), Glis3 (Mmus), Sim1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PH-LHA Foxb1 Glut_4 cells by expression of Glis3. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus , in or close to the regions: Ventral premammillary nucleus, Lateral hypothalamic area, Medial mammillary nucleus, lateral part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2516 PH-LHA Foxb1 Glut_4." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions.
