[Term]
id: PCL:0114936
name: PH-SUM Foxa1 Glut_5 Tafa4 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Csf2rb2 (Mmus), Slc32a1 (Mmus), Tafa4 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PH-SUM Foxa1 Glut_5 cells by expression of Tafa4, Ttc6. It is glutamatergic and GABAergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Slc32a1, Slc18a2, Gad2). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus , in or close to the regions: Lateral hypothalamic area, Medial mammillary nucleus, lateral part, Medial mammillary nucleus, medial part, Medial mammillary nucleus, median part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2556 PH-SUM Foxa1 Glut_5." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type PH-SUM Foxa1 Glut_5 Tafa4 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for posterior hypothalamic nucleus (PH), supramammillary nucleus (SUM). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "2556 PH-SUM Foxa1 Glut_5" EXACT []
