id: PCL:0114962
name: MH Tac2 Glut_2 Mybpc1 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Cngb3 (Mmus), Lhfpl1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MH Tac2 Glut_2 cells by expression of Mybpc1. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Slc17a7). These cells are located in the Hippocampal region, brain , in or close to the regions: Dentate gyrus, molecular layer, third ventricle . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2582 MH Tac2 Glut_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type MH Tac2 Glut_2 Mybpc1 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for medial habenula (MH). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
