[Term]
id: PCL:0115017
name: CM-IAD-CL-PCN Sema5b Glut_2 Satb2 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Igkc (Mmus), Klhl14 (Mmus), Ntng1 (Mmus), Vwa5b1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other CM-IAD-CL-PCN Sema5b Glut_2 cells by expression of Satb2, Slc38a11, Chst9. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Thalamus , in or close to the regions: Paraventricular nucleus of the thalamus, Parataenial nucleus, Mediodorsal nucleus of thalamus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2637 CM-IAD-CL-PCN Sema5b Glut_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type CM-IAD-CL-PCN Sema5b Glut_2 Satb2 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for central medial nucleus of the thalamus (CM), interanterodorsal nucleus of the thalamus (IAD), central lateral nucleus of the thalamus (CL), paracentral nucleus (PCN). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "2637 CM-IAD-CL-PCN Sema5b Glut_2" EXACT []
