[Term]
id: PCL:0115030
name: TH Prkcd Grin2c Glut_2 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Tnnt1 (Mmus), Pik3c2g (Mmus), Dab1 (Mmus), Scn4b (Mmus). It is distinguished from other TH Prkcd Grin2c Glut cells by expression of Sp9, Eps8l2, Gabrg3. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Slc17a7). These cells are located in the Thalamus, brain , in or close to the regions: Dorsal part of the lateral geniculate complex, shell, Dorsal part of the lateral geniculate complex, core, Dorsal part of the lateral geniculate complex, ipsilateral zone . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2650 TH Prkcd Grin2c Glut_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
