name: PRC-PAG Pax6 Glut_4 Cngb3 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Cngb3 (Mmus), Frem3 (Mmus), Gabrq (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PRC-PAG Pax6 Glut_4 cells by expression of Cngb3, Gabrq. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Ddc, Gad2). These cells are located in the Midbrain , in or close to the regions: Nucleus of the posterior commissure . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2749 PRC-PAG Pax6 Glut_4." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type PRC-PAG Pax6 Glut_4 Cngb3 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for precommissural nucleus (PRC), periaqueductal gray (PAG). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "2749 PRC-PAG Pax6 Glut_4" EXACT []
