[Term]
id: PCL:0115130
name: PRC-PAG Pax6 Glut_4 Prdm6 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Prdm6 (Mmus), Pax6 (Mmus), Onecut1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PRC-PAG Pax6 Glut_4 cells by expression of Prdm6. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Gad2). These cells are located in the Midbrain , in or close to the regions: Midbrain reticular nucleus, Nucleus of the posterior commissure, Olivary pretectal nucleus, Periaqueductal gray . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2750 PRC-PAG Pax6 Glut_4." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, PRC-PAG Pax6 Glut_4 Prdm6 does not have cells in precommissural nucleus (PRC). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "2750 PRC-PAG Pax6 Glut_4" EXACT []
