[Term]
id: PCL:0115137
name: MB-ant-ve Dmrta2 Glut_1 Ramp3 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Grxcr2 (Mmus), D130009I18Rik (Mmus), C1ql4 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MB-ant-ve Dmrta2 Glut cells by expression of Ramp3. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Midbrain , in or close to the regions: Rostral linear nucleus raphe . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2757 MB-ant-ve Dmrta2 Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
