id: PCL:0115142
name: MRN-PAG Nkx6-1 Glut_1 Ccdc141 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Nkx6-1 (Mmus), Atp6v1c2 (Mmus), Gabrq (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MRN-PAG Nkx6-1 Glut_1 cells by expression of Ccdc141. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Gad2). These cells are located in the Midbrain , in or close to the regions: Pedunculopontine nucleus, Midbrain reticular nucleus, Ventral tegmental area . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2762 MRN-PAG Nkx6-1 Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
