name: IF-RL-CLI-PAG Foxa1 Glut_1 Scn11a neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Csf2rb2 (Mmus), Scn11a (Mmus), Pitx2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other IF-RL-CLI-PAG Foxa1 Glut_1 cells by expression of Scn11a. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus, Midbrain , in or close to the regions: Supramammillary nucleus, principal mammillary tract . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2767 IF-RL-CLI-PAG Foxa1 Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type IF-RL-CLI-PAG Foxa1 Glut_1 Scn11a does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for interfascicular nucleus raphe (IF), rostral linear nucleus raphe (RL), central linear nucleus raphe (CLI), periaqueductal gray (PAG). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
