[Term]
id: PCL:0115160
name: IF-RL-CLI-PAG Foxa1 Glut_5 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Dmrta2 (Mmus), Cplx3 (Mmus), Pitx2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other IF-RL-CLI-PAG Foxa1 Glut cells by expression of Slc5a7. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Gad2). These cells are located in the Midbrain, Thalamus , in or close to the regions: Subparafascicular area . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2780 IF-RL-CLI-PAG Foxa1 Glut_5." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06808-9, https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Rationale for assigning this type to reference data: Assigned by automated classification (ELK) of a definition built from soma location Brain stem (BS; ≥80% of grey-matter cells in both the Yao 2023 and Zhuang 2023 MERFISH atlases) and neurotransmitter glutamate (all clusters) against CL 2026-06-08. Basis: NT. Other inferred CL parents: central nervous system neuron. [WMBO CL promotion round 1, 2026-10-13] Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type IF-RL-CLI-PAG Foxa1 Glut_5 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for interfascicular nucleus raphe (IF), rostral linear nucleus raphe (RL), central linear nucleus raphe (CLI), periaqueductal gray (PAG). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme. {xref="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z", xref="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06808-9"}
