[Term]
id: PCL:0115170
name: PAG-SC Neurod2 Meis2 Glut_3 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Barhl1 (Mmus), Gm32828 (Mmus), Hmcn1 (Mmus), Dlk1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PAG-SC Neurod2 Meis2 Glut cells by expression of Gm32828. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Midbrain , in or close to the regions: Superior colliculus, motor related, intermediate gray layer, Midbrain reticular nucleus, Superior colliculus, motor related, intermediate white layer . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2790 PAG-SC Neurod2 Meis2 Glut_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, PAG-SC Neurod2 Meis2 Glut_3 does not have cells in periaqueductal gray (PAG). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
