[Term]
id: PCL:0115192
name: PAG Pou4f3 Glut_3 Bnc2 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of C1ql4 (Mmus), Rxfp1 (Mmus), Bnc2 (Mmus), Shox2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PAG Pou4f3 Glut_3 cells by expression of Bnc2, Gm32828. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Midbrain , in or close to the regions: Midbrain reticular nucleus, Superior colliculus, motor related, intermediate white layer . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2812 PAG Pou4f3 Glut_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type PAG Pou4f3 Glut_3 Bnc2 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for periaqueductal gray (PAG). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
