[Term]
id: PCL:0115254
name: PAG-MRN Pou3f1 Glut_5 Grp glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of C1ql4 (Mmus), Dkk2 (Mmus), Grp (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PAG-MRN Pou3f1 Glut_5 cells by expression of Grp. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Gad2). These cells are located in the Midbrain , in or close to the regions: Pedunculopontine nucleus, Midbrain reticular nucleus, Midbrain reticular nucleus, retrorubral area . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2874 PAG-MRN Pou3f1 Glut_5." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, PAG-MRN Pou3f1 Glut_5 Grp does not have cells in periaqueductal gray (PAG). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "2874 PAG-MRN Pou3f1 Glut_5" EXACT []
