[Term]
id: PCL:0115256
name: PAG-MRN Pou3f1 Glut_5 Eya2 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Krt73 (Mmus), Eya2 (Mmus), Lhx9 (Mmus), Trhr (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PAG-MRN Pou3f1 Glut_5 cells by expression of Eya2, En1, Trhr. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Midbrain, Pons , in or close to the regions: Pedunculopontine nucleus, Laterodorsal tegmental nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2876 PAG-MRN Pou3f1 Glut_5." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type PAG-MRN Pou3f1 Glut_5 Eya2 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for periaqueductal gray (PAG), midbrain reticular nucleus (MRN). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "2876 PAG-MRN Pou3f1 Glut_5" EXACT []
