[Term]
id: PCL:0115314
name: SPA-SPFm-SPFp-POL-PIL-PoT Sp9 Glut_1 Slc5a7 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Slc5a7 (Mmus), Neurod6 (Mmus), Lncenc1 (Mmus), Ackr3 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other SPA-SPFm-SPFp-POL-PIL-PoT Sp9 Glut_1 cells by expression of Slc5a7, Irx2, Nfib. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Midbrain, Thalamus , in or close to the regions: Precommissural nucleus, Subparafascicular area . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2934 SPA-SPFm-SPFp-POL-PIL-PoT Sp9 Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, SPA-SPFm-SPFp-POL-PIL-PoT Sp9 Glut_1 Slc5a7 does not have cells in subparafascicular nucleus, magnocellular part (SPFm), subparafascicular nucleus, parvicellular part (SPFp), posterior limiting nucleus of the thalamus (POL), posterior intralaminar thalamic nucleus (PIL), posterior triangular thalamic nucleus (PoT). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
