name: SPA-SPFm-SPFp-POL-PIL-PoT Sp9 Glut_3 1700023F02Rik glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of 1700023F02Rik (Mmus), Krt17 (Mmus), Ror1 (Mmus), Nts (Mmus). It is distinguished from other SPA-SPFm-SPFp-POL-PIL-PoT Sp9 Glut_3 cells by expression of 1700023F02Rik, Bmpr1b. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Midbrain, Thalamus , in or close to the regions: Precommissural nucleus, Subparafascicular area . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2947 SPA-SPFm-SPFp-POL-PIL-PoT Sp9 Glut_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, SPA-SPFm-SPFp-POL-PIL-PoT Sp9 Glut_3 1700023F02Rik does not have cells in subparafascicular nucleus, parvicellular part (SPFp), posterior limiting nucleus of the thalamus (POL), posterior intralaminar thalamic nucleus (PIL), posterior triangular thalamic nucleus (PoT). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "2947 SPA-SPFm-SPFp-POL-PIL-PoT Sp9 Glut_3" EXACT []
