id: PCL:0115347
name: SPA-SPFm-SPFp-POL-PIL-PoT Sp9 Glut_5 Qrfpr glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Gbx2 (Mmus), Qrfpr (Mmus), Npsr1 (Mmus), Tacr1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other SPA-SPFm-SPFp-POL-PIL-PoT Sp9 Glut_5 cells by expression of Qrfpr, Tacr1. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Thalamus , in or close to the regions: Posterior intralaminar thalamic nucleus, Ventral posteromedial nucleus of the thalamus, parvicellular part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2967 SPA-SPFm-SPFp-POL-PIL-PoT Sp9 Glut_5." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, SPA-SPFm-SPFp-POL-PIL-PoT Sp9 Glut_5 Qrfpr does not have cells in subparafascicular nucleus, magnocellular part (SPFm), posterior limiting nucleus of the thalamus (POL). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "2967 SPA-SPFm-SPFp-POL-PIL-PoT Sp9 Glut_5" EXACT []
