name: SPA-SPFm-SPFp-POL-PIL-PoT Sp9 Glut_7 Sox2 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Gbx2 (Mmus), Moxd1 (Mmus), Cbln2 (Mmus), B130024G19Rik (Mmus). It is distinguished from other SPA-SPFm-SPFp-POL-PIL-PoT Sp9 Glut_7 cells by expression of Moxd1, Sox2, Trpc4. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Thalamus , in or close to the regions: Medial geniculate complex, medial part, Midbrain, Posterior intralaminar thalamic nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2987 SPA-SPFm-SPFp-POL-PIL-PoT Sp9 Glut_7." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, SPA-SPFm-SPFp-POL-PIL-PoT Sp9 Glut_7 Sox2 does not have cells in subparafascicular area (SPA), subparafascicular nucleus, magnocellular part (SPFm), posterior limiting nucleus of the thalamus (POL). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "2987 SPA-SPFm-SPFp-POL-PIL-PoT Sp9 Glut_7" EXACT []
