[Term]
id: PCL:0115381
name: SPA-SPFm-SPFp-POL-PIL-PoT Sp9 Glut_10 Agtr1a glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Pth2 (Mmus), Agtr1a (Mmus). It is distinguished from other SPA-SPFm-SPFp-POL-PIL-PoT Sp9 Glut_10 cells by expression of Agtr1a. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Ddc, Th, Slc17a7). These cells are located in the Midbrain, Thalamus , in or close to the regions: Midbrain reticular nucleus, Subparafascicular nucleus, parvicellular part, Posterior intralaminar thalamic nucleus, Posterior triangular thalamic nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3001 SPA-SPFm-SPFp-POL-PIL-PoT Sp9 Glut_10." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, SPA-SPFm-SPFp-POL-PIL-PoT Sp9 Glut_10 Agtr1a does not have cells in subparafascicular area (SPA), subparafascicular nucleus, magnocellular part (SPFm), posterior limiting nucleus of the thalamus (POL). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "3001 SPA-SPFm-SPFp-POL-PIL-PoT Sp9 Glut_10" EXACT []
