[Term]
id: PCL:0115427
name: PAG-MRN Tfap2b Glut_1 Npas1 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Onecut3 (Mmus), Snorc (Mmus), Kl (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PAG-MRN Tfap2b Glut_1 cells by expression of Npas1. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Midbrain , in or close to the regions: Midbrain reticular nucleus, Retroparafascicular nucleus, Periaqueductal gray . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3047 PAG-MRN Tfap2b Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
