id: PCL:0115430
name: PAG-MRN Tfap2b Glut_1 C1ql4 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Tstd1 (Mmus), C1ql4 (Mmus), Gm32828 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PAG-MRN Tfap2b Glut_1 cells by expression of C1ql4, Hcrtr2. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Midbrain , in or close to the regions: Periaqueductal gray . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3050 PAG-MRN Tfap2b Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, PAG-MRN Tfap2b Glut_1 C1ql4 does not have cells in midbrain reticular nucleus (MRN). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "3050 PAG-MRN Tfap2b Glut_1" EXACT []
is_a: PCL:0111303 ! PAG-MRN Tfap2b Glut_1 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
relationship: RO:0002215 GO:0061535 {comment="Inferred to be glutamate secretion, neurotransmission based on expression of Slc17a6"}
