[Term]
id: PCL:0115431
name: PAG-MRN Tfap2b Glut_1 Ttc12 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Fcmr (Mmus), 5830418P13Rik (Mmus), Rxrg (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PAG-MRN Tfap2b Glut_1 cells by expression of Ttc12, Col12a1. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Midbrain , in or close to the regions: Midbrain reticular nucleus, Periaqueductal gray, Inferior colliculus, central nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3051 PAG-MRN Tfap2b Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions.
