[Term]
id: PCL:0115438
name: PAG-MRN Tfap2b Glut_1 Opn5 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Nr5a2 (Mmus), Opn5 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PAG-MRN Tfap2b Glut_1 cells by expression of Opn5. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Midbrain, Cerebellum , in or close to the regions: Lobule II . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3058 PAG-MRN Tfap2b Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type PAG-MRN Tfap2b Glut_1 Opn5 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for periaqueductal gray (PAG), midbrain reticular nucleus (MRN). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "3058 PAG-MRN Tfap2b Glut_1" EXACT []
