[Term]
id: PCL:0115439
name: PAG-MRN Tfap2b Glut_1 6430628N08Rik glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Tstd1 (Mmus), Isl1 (Mmus), Onecut3 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PAG-MRN Tfap2b Glut_1 cells by expression of 6430628N08Rik. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Cerebellum, Pons , in or close to the regions: Parabrachial nucleus, Lobule II . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3059 PAG-MRN Tfap2b Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
