[Term]
id: PCL:0115441
name: PAG-MRN Tfap2b Glut_1 Nfix glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Cubn (Mmus), Tfap2d (Mmus), Pax5 (Mmus), Trpc5 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PAG-MRN Tfap2b Glut_1 cells by expression of Nfix. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Midbrain, Cerebellum , in or close to the regions: cerebral aqueduct, Periaqueductal gray . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3061 PAG-MRN Tfap2b Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, PAG-MRN Tfap2b Glut_1 Nfix does not have cells in midbrain reticular nucleus (MRN). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
