id: PCL:0115450
name: PAG-MRN Tfap2b Glut_1 Cnga3 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Cnga3 (Mmus), Tfap2d (Mmus), Tcf7l2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PAG-MRN Tfap2b Glut_1 cells by expression of Cnga3, Tcf7l2. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Gad2). These cells are located in the Midbrain, Cerebellum , in or close to the regions: Lobule II, Lobule III . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3070 PAG-MRN Tfap2b Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type PAG-MRN Tfap2b Glut_1 Cnga3 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for periaqueductal gray (PAG), midbrain reticular nucleus (MRN). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "3070 PAG-MRN Tfap2b Glut_1" EXACT []
