[Term]
id: PCL:0115625
name: SCig-an-PPT Foxb1 Glut_1 Calca glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Foxb1 (Mmus), Calca (Mmus), Ctxn3 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other SCig-an-PPT Foxb1 Glut cells by expression of Calca. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Midbrain , in or close to the regions: Posterior pretectal nucleus, Olivary pretectal nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3245 SCig-an-PPT Foxb1 Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, SCig-an-PPT Foxb1 Glut_1 Calca does not have cells in superior colliculus, motor related, intermediate gray layer (SCig). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
