[Term]
id: PCL:0115631
name: SCig-an-PPT Foxb1 Glut_1 Ebf2 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Foxb1 (Mmus), Sst (Mmus), Scn4b (Mmus), Ebf2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other SCig-an-PPT Foxb1 Glut cells by expression of Ebf2. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Midbrain , in or close to the regions: Superior colliculus, motor related, intermediate gray layer, Superior colliculus, motor related, intermediate white layer . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3251 SCig-an-PPT Foxb1 Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, SCig-an-PPT Foxb1 Glut_1 Ebf2 does not have cells in posterior pretectal nucleus (PPT). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "3251 SCig-an-PPT Foxb1 Glut_1" EXACT []
