def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Tfap2d (Mmus), Crhr2 (Mmus), Stc1 (Mmus), En1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other IC Tfap2d Maf Glut_2 cells by expression of Crhr2, Stc1, Pcdh8. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Cerebellum , in or close to the regions: Lobule III . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3300 IC Tfap2d Maf Glut_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type IC Tfap2d Maf Glut_2 Crhr2 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for inferior colliculus (IC). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "3300 IC Tfap2d Maf Glut_2" EXACT []
