name: IC Tfap2d Maf Glut_6 Fosl2 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Cfap77 (Mmus), Tfap2d (Mmus), Lmo2 (Mmus), Hcrtr2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other IC Tfap2d Maf Glut_6 cells by expression of Fosl2, Rab3b, Pcdh19, Syt10. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Midbrain, Cerebellum , in or close to the regions: Inferior colliculus, dorsal nucleus, Inferior colliculus, external nucleus, Lobule III . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3318 IC Tfap2d Maf Glut_6." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
