[Term]
id: PCL:0115704
name: CUN-PPN Evx2 Meis2 Glut_1 Npsr1 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Evx1os (Mmus), Chrdl1 (Mmus), Foxp2 (Mmus), Prph (Mmus). It is distinguished from other CUN-PPN Evx2 Meis2 Glut_1 cells by expression of Npsr1, Cntnap3, Pvalb. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Midbrain, Cerebellum , in or close to the regions: Cuneiform nucleus, Lobule III . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3324 CUN-PPN Evx2 Meis2 Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, CUN-PPN Evx2 Meis2 Glut_1 Npsr1 does not have cells in pedunculopontine nucleus (PPN). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "3324 CUN-PPN Evx2 Meis2 Glut_1" EXACT []
