[Term]
id: PCL:0115720
name: CUN-PPN Evx2 Meis2 Glut_3 Iigp1 cholinergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A cholinergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Myl1 (Mmus), Xdh (Mmus). It is distinguished from other CUN-PPN Evx2 Meis2 Glut_3 cells by expression of Iigp1. It is cholinergic (inferred from expression of Chat, Slc18a3). These cells are located in the Midbrain, Pons , in or close to the regions: Pedunculopontine nucleus, Nucleus of the lateral lemniscus, Parabrachial nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3340 CUN-PPN Evx2 Meis2 Glut_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, CUN-PPN Evx2 Meis2 Glut_3 Iigp1 does not have cells in cuneiform nucleus (CUN). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme. Warning: Despite its name, CUN-PPN Evx2 Meis2 Glut_3 Iigp1 does not secrete the neurotransmitter Glut, as assessed by expression of multiple marker genes.
synonym: "3340 CUN-PPN Evx2 Meis2 Glut_3" EXACT []
