[Term]
id: PCL:0115727
name: CUN-PPN Evx2 Meis2 Glut_4 Mctp2 neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Prdm6 (Mmus), Mctp2 (Mmus), Nox4 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other CUN-PPN Evx2 Meis2 Glut_4 cells by expression of Mctp2, Ebf3. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Midbrain, Pons , in or close to the regions: Pedunculopontine nucleus, Pontine reticular nucleus, Parabrachial nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3347 CUN-PPN Evx2 Meis2 Glut_4." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, CUN-PPN Evx2 Meis2 Glut_4 Mctp2 does not have cells in cuneiform nucleus (CUN). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
