[Term]
id: PCL:0115732
name: PBG Mtnr1a Glut-Chol cholinergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A cholinergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Mtnr1a (Mmus), Ikzf1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MB Glut cells by expression of Mtnr1a, Ikzf1. It is cholinergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Chat, Slc18a3). These cells are located in the Midbrain, brain , in or close to the regions: lateral lemniscus, Parabigeminal nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3352 PBG Mtnr1a Glut-Chol_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06808-9, https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Rationale for assigning this type to reference data: Assigned by automated classification (ELK) of a definition built from soma location Midbrain (MB; ≥80% of grey-matter cells in both the Yao 2023 and Zhuang 2023 MERFISH atlases) and neurotransmitter acetylcholine (all clusters) against CL 2026-06-08. Basis: NT. Other inferred CL parents: central nervous system neuron. [WMBO CL promotion round 1, 2026-10-13] Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. {xref="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z", xref="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06808-9"}
synonym: "0781 PBG Mtnr1a Glut-Chol_1" EXACT []
