[Term]
id: PCL:0115733
name: PAG Tcf24 Glut dopaminergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A dopaminergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Tcf24 (Mmus), Sfta3-ps (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MB Glut cells by expression of Tcf24, Sfta3-ps. It is dopaminergic (inferred from expression of Th, Slc18a2, Ddc, Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Midbrain, Thalamus , in or close to the regions: Subparafascicular area, Periaqueductal gray . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3353 PAG Tcf24 Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06808-9, https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Rationale for assigning this type to reference data: Assigned by automated classification (ELK) of a definition built from soma location Brain stem (BS; ≥80% of grey-matter cells in both the Yao 2023 and Zhuang 2023 MERFISH atlases) and neurotransmitter dopamine (all clusters) against CL 2026-06-08. Basis: NT. Other inferred CL parents: central nervous system neuron. [WMBO CL promotion round 1, 2026-10-13] Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. {xref="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z", xref="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06808-9"}
