id: PCL:0115785
name: PPN-CUN-PCG Otp En1 Gaba_3 Gabre GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Pax7 (Mmus), 1700042O10Rik (Mmus), Glp1r (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PPN-CUN-PCG Otp En1 Gaba_3 cells by expression of Gabre, Glp1r. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Ddc). These cells are located in the Midbrain, Pons, brain , in or close to the regions: Cuneiform nucleus, arbor vitae, ventral spinocerebellar tract, Parabrachial nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3405 PPN-CUN-PCG Otp En1 Gaba_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, PPN-CUN-PCG Otp En1 Gaba_3 Gabre does not have cells in pedunculopontine nucleus (PPN), pontine central gray (PCG). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "3405 PPN-CUN-PCG Otp En1 Gaba_3" EXACT []
