[Term]
id: PCL:0115793
name: MRN-PPN-CUN Pax8 Gaba_2 Pmfbp1 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Onecut3 (Mmus), Pax8 (Mmus), Npsr1 (Mmus), Dgkk (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MRN-PPN-CUN Pax8 Gaba_2 cells by expression of Pmfbp1. It is glutamatergic and GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Midbrain, Cerebellum, brain , in or close to the regions: Periaqueductal gray, Lobule II, arbor vitae, Cuneiform nucleus, Lobule III, Parabrachial nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3413 MRN-PPN-CUN Pax8 Gaba_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, MRN-PPN-CUN Pax8 Gaba_2 Pmfbp1 does not have cells in midbrain reticular nucleus (MRN), pedunculopontine nucleus (PPN). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "3413 MRN-PPN-CUN Pax8 Gaba_2" EXACT []
