[Term]
id: PCL:0115794
name: MRN-PPN-CUN Pax8 Gaba_2 Qrfprl GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Pax8 (Mmus), Gm16551 (Mmus), Glp1r (Mmus), Oxtr (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MRN-PPN-CUN Pax8 Gaba_2 cells by expression of Qrfprl, Il1rap. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Midbrain, Cerebellum, brain , in or close to the regions: Periaqueductal gray, ventral spinocerebellar tract, Parabrachial nucleus, Lobule II . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3414 MRN-PPN-CUN Pax8 Gaba_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type MRN-PPN-CUN Pax8 Gaba_2 Qrfprl does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for midbrain reticular nucleus (MRN), pedunculopontine nucleus (PPN), cuneiform nucleus (CUN). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
