[Term]
id: PCL:0115798
name: MRN-PPN-CUN Pax8 Gaba_3 GABA-Gly neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABA-Gly neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Ptgfr (Mmus), Shisal2b (Mmus), Pax8 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MRN-PPN-CUN Pax8 Gaba cells by expression of Ptgfr. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Slc6a5). These cells are located in the Midbrain, Pons , in or close to the regions: Interpeduncular nucleus, lateral, Interpeduncular nucleus, caudal, Superior central nucleus raphe, Interpeduncular nucleus, intermediate, Interpeduncular nucleus, apical . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3418 MRN-PPN-CUN Pax8 Gaba_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06808-9, https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Rationale for assigning this type to reference data: Assigned by automated classification (ELK) of a definition built from soma location Brain stem (BS; ≥80% of grey-matter cells in both the Yao 2023 and Zhuang 2023 MERFISH atlases) and neurotransmitter GABA + glycine (all clusters) against CL 2026-06-08. Basis: NT. Other inferred CL parents: central nervous system neuron. [WMBO CL promotion round 1, 2026-10-13] Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type MRN-PPN-CUN Pax8 Gaba_3 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for midbrain reticular nucleus (MRN), pedunculopontine nucleus (PPN), cuneiform nucleus (CUN). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme. {xref="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z", xref="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06808-9"}
