[Term]
id: PCL:0115806
name: MRN-VTN-PPN Pax5 Cdh23 Gaba_2 Ccnjl GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Prokr1 (Mmus), Gli3 (Mmus), Gm6213 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MRN-VTN-PPN Pax5 Cdh23 Gaba_2 cells by expression of Ccnjl, Ptger3. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Midbrain , in or close to the regions: Periaqueductal gray . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3426 MRN-VTN-PPN Pax5 Cdh23 Gaba_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type MRN-VTN-PPN Pax5 Cdh23 Gaba_2 Ccnjl does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for midbrain reticular nucleus (MRN), ventral tegmental nucleus (VTN), pedunculopontine nucleus (PPN). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "3426 MRN-VTN-PPN Pax5 Cdh23 Gaba_2" EXACT []
