[Term]
id: PCL:0115833
name: PAG-PPN Pax5 Sox21 Gaba_3 Col24a1 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Gm4675 (Mmus), Hck (Mmus), C1ql1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PAG-PPN Pax5 Sox21 Gaba_3 cells by expression of Col24a1. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Midbrain , in or close to the regions: Substantia nigra, compact part, Substantia nigra, reticular part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3453 PAG-PPN Pax5 Sox21 Gaba_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type PAG-PPN Pax5 Sox21 Gaba_3 Col24a1 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for periaqueductal gray (PAG), pedunculopontine nucleus (PPN). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
