[Term]
id: PCL:0115847
name: IC Six3 En2 Gaba_1 Npffr2 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Pla2g5 (Mmus), Npffr2 (Mmus), Gata3 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other IC Six3 En2 Gaba_1 cells by expression of Npffr2, Sox14. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Midbrain, Cerebellum , in or close to the regions: Inferior colliculus, dorsal nucleus, Lobule III . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3467 IC Six3 En2 Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
