id: PCL:0115854
name: IC Six3 En2 Gaba_1 Pmfbp1 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Onecut3 (Mmus), Sox14 (Mmus), Nox4 (Mmus), Gata3 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other IC Six3 En2 Gaba_1 cells by expression of Pmfbp1. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Midbrain , in or close to the regions: Midbrain reticular nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3474 IC Six3 En2 Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type IC Six3 En2 Gaba_1 Pmfbp1 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for inferior colliculus (IC). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
