[Term]
id: PCL:0115858
name: IC Six3 En2 Gaba_2 Pdgfd GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Otx2os1 (Mmus), Pax8 (Mmus), Ppp1r17 (Mmus), Egflam (Mmus). It is distinguished from other IC Six3 En2 Gaba_2 cells by expression of Pdgfd, Egflam. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Midbrain, Cerebellum , in or close to the regions: Periaqueductal gray, Inferior colliculus, dorsal nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3478 IC Six3 En2 Gaba_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
