[Term]
id: PCL:0115863
name: IC Six3 En2 Gaba_3 Chrdl1 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Chrdl1 (Mmus), Six3os1 (Mmus), Nts (Mmus), Gata3 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other IC Six3 En2 Gaba_3 cells by expression of Chrdl1, Sntb1. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Midbrain , in or close to the regions: Midbrain reticular nucleus, Cuneiform nucleus, Inferior colliculus, central nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3483 IC Six3 En2 Gaba_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
