[Term]
id: PCL:0115870
name: IC Six3 En2 Gaba_4 Ctxn3 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Sox21 (Mmus), Qrfprl (Mmus), Sox3 (Mmus), Gpr101 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other IC Six3 En2 Gaba_4 cells by expression of Ctxn3, Doc2b. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Midbrain, Cerebellum , in or close to the regions: Cuneiform nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3490 IC Six3 En2 Gaba_4." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type IC Six3 En2 Gaba_4 Ctxn3 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for inferior colliculus (IC). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
