[Term]
id: PCL:0115884
name: IC Six3 En2 Gaba_6 Trpv6 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Cdh3 (Mmus), Gli3 (Mmus), Otx2os1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other IC Six3 En2 Gaba_6 cells by expression of Trpv6, Gpc4. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Midbrain, Cerebellum , in or close to the regions: Inferior colliculus, dorsal nucleus, Lobule III . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3504 IC Six3 En2 Gaba_6." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
