id: PCL:0115889
name: PAG-MRN-RN Foxa2 Gaba_1 Ush2a GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Ush2a (Mmus), Fam129a (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PAG-MRN-RN Foxa2 Gaba_1 cells by expression of Ush2a. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad1, Gad2, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus, Midbrain , in or close to the regions: Midbrain reticular nucleus, Red nucleus, Supramammillary nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3509 PAG-MRN-RN Foxa2 Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, PAG-MRN-RN Foxa2 Gaba_1 Ush2a does not have cells in periaqueductal gray (PAG). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
