[Term]
id: PCL:0115928
name: PAG-ND-PCG Onecut1 Gaba_2 Trhr GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Cd40 (Mmus), Agtr2 (Mmus), Sp9 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PAG-ND-PCG Onecut1 Gaba_2 cells by expression of Trhr. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Midbrain, Pons , in or close to the regions: Midbrain reticular nucleus, Pontine reticular nucleus, Laterodorsal tegmental nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3548 PAG-ND-PCG Onecut1 Gaba_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type PAG-ND-PCG Onecut1 Gaba_2 Trhr does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for periaqueductal gray (PAG), nucleus of darkschewitsch (ND), pontine central gray (PCG). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
