id: PCL:0115936
name: PAG-ND-PCG Onecut1 Gaba_5 Fbn2 GABA-Gly neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABA-Gly neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Gchfr (Mmus), Slc6a5 (Mmus), Ptger3 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PAG-ND-PCG Onecut1 Gaba_5 cells by expression of Fbn2. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Slc6a5). These cells are located in the Pons , in or close to the regions: Superior olivary complex, medial part, Superior olivary complex, periolivary region, Nucleus of the trapezoid body . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3556 PAG-ND-PCG Onecut1 Gaba_5." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
