[Term]
id: PCL:0115957
name: PAG-RN Nkx2-2 Otx1 Gaba_3 Ntn1 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Nkx2-2 (Mmus), Tfap2b (Mmus), Npr3 (Mmus), Ntn1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PAG-RN Nkx2-2 Otx1 Gaba_3 cells by expression of Ntn1, Npr3. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Slc6a5). These cells are located in the Midbrain , in or close to the regions: Inferior colliculus, dorsal nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3577 PAG-RN Nkx2-2 Otx1 Gaba_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type PAG-RN Nkx2-2 Otx1 Gaba_3 Ntn1 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for periaqueductal gray (PAG), red nucleus (RN). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "3577 PAG-RN Nkx2-2 Otx1 Gaba_3" EXACT []
