[Term]
id: PCL:0115958
name: PAG-RN Nkx2-2 Otx1 Gaba_3 Piezo2 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Nkx2-2 (Mmus), Tfap2b (Mmus), Piezo2 (Mmus), Npnt (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PAG-RN Nkx2-2 Otx1 Gaba_3 cells by expression of Piezo2, Cdhr1, Npnt. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Slc6a5). These cells are located in the Midbrain, Cerebellum , in or close to the regions: Periaqueductal gray, Lobule II, Lobule III . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3578 PAG-RN Nkx2-2 Otx1 Gaba_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
