id: PCL:0115959
name: PAG-RN Nkx2-2 Otx1 Gaba_3 Synpr GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Fst (Mmus), Tfap2b (Mmus), Otx2os1 (Mmus), Synpr (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PAG-RN Nkx2-2 Otx1 Gaba_3 cells by expression of Fst, Synpr. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Slc6a5). These cells are located in the Midbrain, Cerebellum , in or close to the regions: Lobule II, Lobule III . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3579 PAG-RN Nkx2-2 Otx1 Gaba_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
