[Term]
id: PCL:0115962
name: PAG-RN Nkx2-2 Otx1 Gaba_3 Sv2b GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Skor2 (Mmus), Otx1 (Mmus), Lypd1 (Mmus), Npas1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PAG-RN Nkx2-2 Otx1 Gaba_3 cells by expression of Emx1, Sv2b, Npas1. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Midbrain , in or close to the regions: Midbrain reticular nucleus, Periaqueductal gray . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3582 PAG-RN Nkx2-2 Otx1 Gaba_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, PAG-RN Nkx2-2 Otx1 Gaba_3 Sv2b does not have cells in red nucleus (RN). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "3582 PAG-RN Nkx2-2 Otx1 Gaba_3" EXACT []
