[Term]
id: PCL:0116024
name: LGv-SPFp-SPFm Nkx2-2 Tcf7l2 Gaba_2 Igfbpl1 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Cd40 (Mmus), Igfbpl1 (Mmus), Shox2 (Mmus), Ntsr1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other LGv-SPFp-SPFm Nkx2-2 Tcf7l2 Gaba_2 cells by expression of Igfbpl1, Ntsr1. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Thalamus, brain , in or close to the regions: fiber tracts, Ventral part of the lateral geniculate complex, Intergeniculate leaflet of the lateral geniculate complex . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3644 LGv-SPFp-SPFm Nkx2-2 Tcf7l2 Gaba_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, LGv-SPFp-SPFm Nkx2-2 Tcf7l2 Gaba_2 Igfbpl1 does not have cells in subparafascicular nucleus, parvicellular part (SPFp), subparafascicular nucleus, magnocellular part (SPFm). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
