[Term]
id: PCL:0116027
name: LGv-SPFp-SPFm Nkx2-2 Tcf7l2 Gaba_3 Glp1r GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Glp1r (Mmus), Nkx2-2 (Mmus), Gm20063 (Mmus), Col8a1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other LGv-SPFp-SPFm Nkx2-2 Tcf7l2 Gaba_3 cells by expression of Glp1r, Myo5b. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Midbrain, Thalamus, brain , in or close to the regions: Medial geniculate complex, ventral part, Medial geniculate complex, medial part, cerebal peduncle, Zona incerta, Posterior intralaminar thalamic nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3647 LGv-SPFp-SPFm Nkx2-2 Tcf7l2 Gaba_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type LGv-SPFp-SPFm Nkx2-2 Tcf7l2 Gaba_3 Glp1r does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for ventral part of the lateral geniculate complex (LGv), subparafascicular nucleus, parvicellular part (SPFp), subparafascicular nucleus, magnocellular part (SPFm). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "3647 LGv-SPFp-SPFm Nkx2-2 Tcf7l2 Gaba_3" EXACT []
