[Term]
id: PCL:0116044
name: LGv-SPFp-SPFm Nkx2-2 Tcf7l2 Gaba_6 Arhgap15 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Nkx2-2 (Mmus), Zic4 (Mmus), Emx2os (Mmus), Tac1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other LGv-SPFp-SPFm Nkx2-2 Tcf7l2 Gaba_6 cells by expression of Arhgap15, Zic4, L3mbtl4. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus, Thalamus , in or close to the regions: Perireunensis nucleus, Nucleus of reuniens, Zona incerta . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3664 LGv-SPFp-SPFm Nkx2-2 Tcf7l2 Gaba_6." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type LGv-SPFp-SPFm Nkx2-2 Tcf7l2 Gaba_6 Arhgap15 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for ventral part of the lateral geniculate complex (LGv), subparafascicular nucleus, parvicellular part (SPFp), subparafascicular nucleus, magnocellular part (SPFm). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "3664 LGv-SPFp-SPFm Nkx2-2 Tcf7l2 Gaba_6" EXACT []
