[Term]
id: PCL:0116224
name: SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_1 Ptprq neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Ptprq (Mmus), Lmx1a (Mmus), Lncenc1 (Mmus), Igf1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_1 cells by expression of Ptprq, Lncenc1, Igf1. It is glutamatergic and GABAergic (inferred from expression of Slc32a1, Ddc, Slc17a6, Slc18a2, Gad2). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus, Midbrain . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3844 SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_1 Ptprq does not have cells in substantia nigra, compact part (SNc). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme. Warning: Despite its name, SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_1 Ptprq does not secrete the neurotransmitter Dopa, as assessed by expression of multiple marker genes.
synonym: "3844 SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_1" EXACT []
