[Term]
id: PCL:0116244
name: SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_4 Col6a5 midbrain dopaminergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A midbrain dopaminergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Vip (Mmus), 9030622O22Rik (Mmus), Col6a5 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_4 cells by expression of Col6a5. It is dopaminergic (inferred from expression of Ddc, Slc18a2, Slc6a3, Th, Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Midbrain, brain , in or close to the regions: cerebral aqueduct, Periaqueductal gray, Dorsal nucleus raphe . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3864 SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_4." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_4 Col6a5 does not have cells in substantia nigra, compact part (SNc), ventral tegmental area (VTA). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "3864 SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_4" EXACT []
