[Term]
id: PCL:0116254
name: SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_6 Postn midbrain dopaminergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A midbrain dopaminergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Slc6a3 (Mmus), Postn (Mmus), Ebf3 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_6 cells by expression of Postn. It is dopaminergic (inferred from expression of Slc32a1, Ddc, Slc18a2, Slc6a3, Th, Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Midbrain , in or close to the regions: Midbrain reticular nucleus, Substantia nigra, reticular part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3874 SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_6." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_6 Postn does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for substantia nigra, compact part (SNc), ventral tegmental area (VTA), midbrain raphe nuclei (RAmb). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
