[Term]
id: PCL:0116256
name: SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_7 Vip midbrain dopaminergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A midbrain dopaminergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Slc6a3 (Mmus), Gna14 (Mmus), Frzb (Mmus), Npw (Mmus). It is distinguished from other SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_7 cells by expression of Vip, Tmem207. It is dopaminergic (inferred from expression of Ddc, Slc18a2, Slc6a3, Th, Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Midbrain , in or close to the regions: Central linear nucleus raphe, Dorsal nucleus raphe . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3876 SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_7." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
