[Term]
id: PCL:0116259
name: SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_8 Nts neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Card14 (Mmus), Sox2ot (Mmus). It is distinguished from other SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_8 cells by expression of Nts. It is glutamatergic and GABAergic (inferred from expression of Slc32a1, Ddc, Slc17a6, Slc18a2, Gad2). These cells are located in the Midbrain, brain , in or close to the regions: Ventral tegmental area . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3879 SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_8." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_8 Nts does not have cells in substantia nigra, compact part (SNc), midbrain raphe nuclei (RAmb). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme. Warning: Despite its name, SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_8 Nts does not secrete the neurotransmitter Dopa, as assessed by expression of multiple marker genes.
synonym: "3879 SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_8" EXACT []
