[Term]
id: PCL:0116260
name: MB-MY Tph2 Glut-Sero_1 Sox14 serotonergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A serotonergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Slc6a4 (Mmus), Sox14 (Mmus), Tinag (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MB-MY Tph2 Glut-Sero_1 cells by expression of Sox14, Tinag. It is serotonergic (inferred from expression of Ddc, Slc6a4, Tph2, Slc18a2, Gad2). These cells are located in the Midbrain , in or close to the regions: Laterodorsal tegmental nucleus, Periaqueductal gray, Dorsal nucleus raphe . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3880 MB-MY Tph2 Glut-Sero_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, MB-MY Tph2 Glut-Sero_1 Sox14 does not have cells in medulla (MY). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme. Warning: Despite its name, MB-MY Tph2 Glut-Sero_1 Sox14 does not secrete the neurotransmitter Glut, as assessed by expression of multiple marker genes.
synonym: "3880 MB-MY Tph2 Glut-Sero_1" EXACT []
