[Term]
id: PCL:0116266
name: MB-MY Tph2 Glut-Sero_1 Gm41414 serotonergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A serotonergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Slc6a4 (Mmus), Gm41414 (Mmus), 1110015O18Rik (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MB-MY Tph2 Glut-Sero_1 cells by expression of Gm41414, 1110015O18Rik. It is serotonergic (inferred from expression of Ddc, Slc6a4, Tph2, Slc18a2, Gad2). These cells are located in the Pons . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3886 MB-MY Tph2 Glut-Sero_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type MB-MY Tph2 Glut-Sero_1 Gm41414 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for midbrain (MB), medulla (MY). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme. Warning: Despite its name, MB-MY Tph2 Glut-Sero_1 Gm41414 does not secrete the neurotransmitter Glut, as assessed by expression of multiple marker genes.
synonym: "3886 MB-MY Tph2 Glut-Sero_1" EXACT []
