[Term]
id: PCL:0116270
name: MB-MY Tph2 Glut-Sero_2 Megf11 neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Fev (Mmus), Megf11 (Mmus), Sertm1 (Mmus), Tacr1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MB-MY Tph2 Glut-Sero_2 cells by expression of Megf11, Sertm1, Tacr1. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a8, Slc18a2). These cells are located in the Pons , in or close to the regions: Nucleus raphe pontis, Superior central nucleus raphe . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3890 MB-MY Tph2 Glut-Sero_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type MB-MY Tph2 Glut-Sero_2 Megf11 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for midbrain (MB), medulla (MY). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme. Warning: Despite its name, MB-MY Tph2 Glut-Sero_2 Megf11 does not secrete the neurotransmitter Sero, as assessed by expression of multiple marker genes.
synonym: "3890 MB-MY Tph2 Glut-Sero_2" EXACT []
