[Term]
id: PCL:0116280
name: MB-MY Tph2 Glut-Sero_3 Nts neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Fev (Mmus), Nts (Mmus), Galr1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MB-MY Tph2 Glut-Sero_3 cells by expression of Nts, Galr1. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a8, Ddc). These cells are located in the Midbrain , in or close to the regions: Dorsal nucleus raphe . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3900 MB-MY Tph2 Glut-Sero_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, MB-MY Tph2 Glut-Sero_3 Nts does not have cells in medulla (MY). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme. Warning: Despite its name, MB-MY Tph2 Glut-Sero_3 Nts does not secrete the neurotransmitter Sero, as assessed by expression of multiple marker genes.
synonym: "3900 MB-MY Tph2 Glut-Sero_3" EXACT []
