[Term]
id: PCL:0116282
name: MB-MY Tph2 Glut-Sero_4 Npas1 serotonergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A serotonergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Slc6a4 (Mmus), Npas1 (Mmus), Calcr (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MB-MY Tph2 Glut-Sero_4 cells by expression of Npas1, Calcr. It is serotonergic (inferred from expression of Tph2, Slc6a4, Slc18a2, Ddc). These cells are located in the Midbrain, brain , in or close to the regions: Midbrain reticular nucleus, Periaqueductal gray . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3902 MB-MY Tph2 Glut-Sero_4." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, MB-MY Tph2 Glut-Sero_4 Npas1 does not have cells in medulla (MY). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme. Warning: Despite its name, MB-MY Tph2 Glut-Sero_4 Npas1 does not secrete the neurotransmitter Glut, as assessed by expression of multiple marker genes.
