[Term]
id: PCL:0116292
name: PB Lmx1a Glut_1 Ptgfr glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Ptgfr (Mmus), Lmx1a (Mmus), Chodl (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PB Lmx1a Glut_1 cells by expression of Ptgfr, Chodl. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Pons , in or close to the regions: Koelliker-Fuse subnucleus, Parabrachial nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3912 PB Lmx1a Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
