[Term]
id: PCL:0116306
name: PB Lmx1a Glut_2 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Calca (Mmus), Grpr (Mmus), B130024G19Rik (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PB Lmx1a Glut cells by expression of Qrfpr. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Ddc). These cells are located in the Cerebellum, Pons , in or close to the regions: Koelliker-Fuse subnucleus, arbor vitae, Parabrachial nucleus, Lobule III . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3926 PB Lmx1a Glut_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06808-9, https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Rationale for assigning this type to reference data: Assigned by automated classification (ELK) of a definition built from soma location Basic cell groups and regions (grey; ≥80% of grey-matter cells in both the Yao 2023 and Zhuang 2023 MERFISH atlases) and neurotransmitter glutamate (all clusters) against CL 2026-06-08. Basis: NT. Other inferred CL parents: central nervous system neuron. [WMBO CL promotion round 1, 2026-10-13] Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. {xref="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z", xref="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06808-9"}
