[Term]
id: PCL:0116317
name: PB Lmx1a Glut_4 Slc6a2 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Slc6a2 (Mmus), Lmx1a (Mmus), Calca (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PB Lmx1a Glut_4 cells by expression of Slc6a2, Calca. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Slc6a2, Chat). These cells are located in the Cerebellum, Pons , in or close to the regions: Parabrachial nucleus, Lobule III . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3937 PB Lmx1a Glut_4." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
