[Term]
id: PCL:0116324
name: PB Lmx1a Glut_5 Agtr1b neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Six2 (Mmus), Onecut3 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PB Lmx1a Glut_5 cells by expression of Agtr1b. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Pons, brain , in or close to the regions: Koelliker-Fuse subnucleus, superior cerebelar peduncles, Parabrachial nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3944 PB Lmx1a Glut_5." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
