[Term]
id: PCL:0116330
name: PB Lmx1a Glut_5 Clec14a neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Gm10637 (Mmus), Il20ra (Mmus), Satb2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PB Lmx1a Glut_5 cells by expression of Clec14a, Layn. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Chat). These cells are located in the Cerebellum, Pons, brain , in or close to the regions: superior cerebelar peduncles, arbor vitae, Parabrachial nucleus, Lobule III . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3950 PB Lmx1a Glut_5." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
