[Term]
id: PCL:0116339
name: PSV Lmx1a Trpv6 Glut_1 Prrxl1 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Tlx1 (Mmus), Crnde (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PSV Lmx1a Trpv6 Glut cells by expression of Prrxl1. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Pons , in or close to the regions: Superior olivary complex, lateral part, Motor nucleus of trigeminal . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3959 PSV Lmx1a Trpv6 Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type PSV Lmx1a Trpv6 Glut_1 Prrxl1 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for principal sensory nucleus of the trigeminal (PSV). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
