id: PCL:0116365
name: LDT-PCG Vsx2 Lhx4 Glut_2 Pvalb glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Lhx4 (Mmus), Pvalb (Mmus), Ebf2 (Mmus), Skor1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other LDT-PCG Vsx2 Lhx4 Glut_2 cells by expression of Pvalb, Skor1. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Gad2). These cells are located in the Pons , in or close to the regions: Posterodorsal tegmental nucleus, Pontine central gray . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3985 LDT-PCG Vsx2 Lhx4 Glut_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, LDT-PCG Vsx2 Lhx4 Glut_2 Pvalb does not have cells in laterodorsal tegmental nucleus (LDT). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "3985 LDT-PCG Vsx2 Lhx4 Glut_2" EXACT []
