[Term]
id: PCL:0116372
name: LDT-PCG Vsx2 Lhx4 Glut_4 Chrnb4 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Hepacam2 (Mmus), Chrnb4 (Mmus), Satb2 (Mmus), C1ql1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other LDT-PCG Vsx2 Lhx4 Glut_4 cells by expression of Chrnb4, Cacna2d3. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Gad2). These cells are located in the Midbrain , in or close to the regions: Periaqueductal gray, Dorsal nucleus raphe . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3992 LDT-PCG Vsx2 Lhx4 Glut_4." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type LDT-PCG Vsx2 Lhx4 Glut_4 Chrnb4 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for laterodorsal tegmental nucleus (LDT), pontine central gray (PCG). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "3992 LDT-PCG Vsx2 Lhx4 Glut_4" EXACT []
