[Term]
id: PCL:0116381
name: LDT-PCG Vsx2 Lhx4 Glut_5 Meis2 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Lhx4 (Mmus), Npas1 (Mmus), Gm29683 (Mmus), Calb1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other LDT-PCG Vsx2 Lhx4 Glut_5 cells by expression of Meis2, Casz1. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Gad2). These cells are located in the Pons , in or close to the regions: crossed tectospinal pathway, Pontine reticular nucleus, caudal part, Pontine reticular nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4001 LDT-PCG Vsx2 Lhx4 Glut_5." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type LDT-PCG Vsx2 Lhx4 Glut_5 Meis2 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for laterodorsal tegmental nucleus (LDT), pontine central gray (PCG). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "4001 LDT-PCG Vsx2 Lhx4 Glut_5" EXACT []
