id: PCL:0116392
name: LDT-PCG Vsx2 Lhx4 Glut_7 Pth2r glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Lhx4 (Mmus), Npr3 (Mmus), Cpa6 (Mmus), Tent5a (Mmus). It is distinguished from other LDT-PCG Vsx2 Lhx4 Glut_7 cells by expression of Pth2r, Gm39185, Tent5a. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Gad2). These cells are located in the Pons , in or close to the regions: Pontine central gray . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4012 LDT-PCG Vsx2 Lhx4 Glut_7." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, LDT-PCG Vsx2 Lhx4 Glut_7 Pth2r does not have cells in laterodorsal tegmental nucleus (LDT). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
