[Term]
id: PCL:0116398
name: PB Evx2 Glut_1 Barhl2 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of C1ql4 (Mmus), Barhl2 (Mmus), Nr4a2 (Mmus), Cbln1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PB Evx2 Glut_1 cells by expression of Barhl2, Scn5a. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Cerebellum, Pons , in or close to the regions: Nucleus of the lateral lemniscus, Parabrachial nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4018 PB Evx2 Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
