[Term]
id: PCL:0116426
name: PB Evx2 Glut_3 Mgarp glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Mgarp (Mmus), Shisal2b (Mmus), Sln (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PB Evx2 Glut_3 cells by expression of Mgarp, Scn7a. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Ddc). These cells are located in the Midbrain, Cerebellum , in or close to the regions: Periaqueductal gray, Lobule II, Lobule III . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4046 PB Evx2 Glut_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type PB Evx2 Glut_3 Mgarp does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for parabrachial nucleus (PB). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
