[Term]
id: PCL:0116481
name: PCG-PRNr Vsx2 Nkx6-1 Glut_1 Vip glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Foxd4 (Mmus), Arhgap36 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PCG-PRNr Vsx2 Nkx6-1 Glut_1 cells by expression of Vip, Foxd4. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Pons , in or close to the regions: Pontine reticular nucleus, caudal part, Pontine reticular nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4101 PCG-PRNr Vsx2 Nkx6-1 Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, PCG-PRNr Vsx2 Nkx6-1 Glut_1 Vip does not have cells in pontine central gray (PCG). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
