id: PCL:0116484
name: PCG-PRNr Vsx2 Nkx6-1 Glut_2 Ly75 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Gm32122 (Mmus), Qrfpr (Mmus), Npy2r (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PCG-PRNr Vsx2 Nkx6-1 Glut_2 cells by expression of Ly75. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Pons , in or close to the regions: Midbrain reticular nucleus, Superior central nucleus raphe, Dorsal tegmental nucleus, Pontine central gray . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4104 PCG-PRNr Vsx2 Nkx6-1 Glut_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
