[Term]
id: PCL:0116487
name: PCG-PRNr Vsx2 Nkx6-1 Glut_2 Ptger3 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Vsx2 (Mmus), Gm4881 (Mmus), Pgr15l (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PCG-PRNr Vsx2 Nkx6-1 Glut_2 cells by expression of Ptger3. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Pons , in or close to the regions: Midbrain reticular nucleus, Pontine reticular nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4107 PCG-PRNr Vsx2 Nkx6-1 Glut_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, PCG-PRNr Vsx2 Nkx6-1 Glut_2 Ptger3 does not have cells in pontine central gray (PCG). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "4107 PCG-PRNr Vsx2 Nkx6-1 Glut_2" EXACT []
