id: PCL:0116490
name: PCG-PRNr Vsx2 Nkx6-1 Glut_3 Ntn1 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Hpse2 (Mmus), Nkx6-1 (Mmus), Qrfprl (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PCG-PRNr Vsx2 Nkx6-1 Glut_3 cells by expression of Ntn1. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Gad2). These cells are located in the Pons , in or close to the regions: Pontine central gray . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4110 PCG-PRNr Vsx2 Nkx6-1 Glut_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
