[Term]
id: PCL:0116494
name: PCG-PRNr Vsx2 Nkx6-1 Glut_3 Lrrc38 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Nkx6-1 (Mmus), Rxfp1 (Mmus), Lrrc38 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PCG-PRNr Vsx2 Nkx6-1 Glut_3 cells by expression of Lrrc38. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Gad2). These cells are located in the Midbrain, Pons , in or close to the regions: Midbrain reticular nucleus, Laterodorsal tegmental nucleus, Pontine central gray . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4114 PCG-PRNr Vsx2 Nkx6-1 Glut_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, PCG-PRNr Vsx2 Nkx6-1 Glut_3 Lrrc38 does not have cells in pontine reticular nucleus (PRNr). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
