[Term]
id: PCL:0116500
name: PCG-PRNr Vsx2 Nkx6-1 Glut_5 Kitl glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Lhx3 (Mmus), Gm12022 (Mmus), Nkx6-1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PCG-PRNr Vsx2 Nkx6-1 Glut_5 cells by expression of Kitl, Lhx4. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Medulla, Pons , in or close to the regions: Gigantocellular reticular nucleus, Pontine reticular nucleus, caudal part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4120 PCG-PRNr Vsx2 Nkx6-1 Glut_5." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
