[Term]
id: PCL:0116522
name: PRNc-PARN Tlx1 Glut_3 Pou4f1 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Vip (Mmus), D130009I18Rik (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PRNc-PARN Tlx1 Glut_3 cells by expression of Pou4f1. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Medulla, brain , in or close to the regions: Paragigantocellular reticular nucleus, lateral part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4142 PRNc-PARN Tlx1 Glut_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, PRNc-PARN Tlx1 Glut_3 Pou4f1 does not have cells in pontine reticular nucleus, caudal part (PRNc). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "4142 PRNc-PARN Tlx1 Glut_3" EXACT []
