[Term]
id: PCL:0116525
name: PB-PSV Phox2b Glut_1 Phox2a glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Atoh1 (Mmus), Ndnf (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PB-PSV Phox2b Glut cells by expression of Phox2a. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Slc18a2, Ddc). These cells are located in the Pons , in or close to the regions: Supratrigeminal nucleus, Peritrigeminal zone, Motor nucleus of trigeminal . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4145 PB-PSV Phox2b Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, PB-PSV Phox2b Glut_1 Phox2a does not have cells in principal sensory nucleus of the trigeminal (PSV). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
