[Term]
id: PCL:0116536
name: PB-NTS Phox2b Ebf3 Lmx1b Glut_1 Nts glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Phox2b (Mmus), Crb1 (Mmus), Nts (Mmus), Lmx1b (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PB-NTS Phox2b Ebf3 Lmx1b Glut_1 cells by expression of Nts. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Pons , in or close to the regions: Koelliker-Fuse subnucleus, Supratrigeminal nucleus, Parabrachial nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4156 PB-NTS Phox2b Ebf3 Lmx1b Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, PB-NTS Phox2b Ebf3 Lmx1b Glut_1 Nts does not have cells in nucleus of the solitary tract (NTS). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "4156 PB-NTS Phox2b Ebf3 Lmx1b Glut_1" EXACT []
