id: PCL:0116549
name: PB-NTS Phox2b Ebf3 Lmx1b Glut_2 Tac1 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Six2 (Mmus), Irx4 (Mmus), Tac1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PB-NTS Phox2b Ebf3 Lmx1b Glut_2 cells by expression of Irx4, Tac1. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Medulla, Pons , in or close to the regions: Spinal nucleus of the trigeminal, oral part, Supratrigeminal nucleus, Parvicellular reticular nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4169 PB-NTS Phox2b Ebf3 Lmx1b Glut_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type PB-NTS Phox2b Ebf3 Lmx1b Glut_2 Tac1 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for parabrachial nucleus (PB), nucleus of the solitary tract (NTS). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
