[Term]
id: PCL:0116565
name: IPN-LDT Vsx2 Nkx6-1 Glut_2 Fbln5 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Krt26 (Mmus), Fam163a (Mmus), Chrnb3 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other IPN-LDT Vsx2 Nkx6-1 Glut_2 cells by expression of Fbln5, Pou4f2. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Midbrain , in or close to the regions: Periaqueductal gray . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4185 IPN-LDT Vsx2 Nkx6-1 Glut_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type IPN-LDT Vsx2 Nkx6-1 Glut_2 Fbln5 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for interpeduncular nucleus (IPN), laterodorsal tegmental nucleus (LDT). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "4185 IPN-LDT Vsx2 Nkx6-1 Glut_2" EXACT []
