[Term]
id: PCL:0116576
name: NLL-SOC Spp1 Glut_2 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of 4930401C15Rik (Mmus), Prdm6 (Mmus), Onecut1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other NLL-SOC Spp1 Glut cells by expression of Zfhx4. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Pons, brain , in or close to the regions: Nucleus of the lateral lemniscus, middle cerebellar peduncle . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4196 NLL-SOC Spp1 Glut_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, NLL-SOC Spp1 Glut_2 does not have cells in superior olivary complex (SOC). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "0951 NLL-SOC Spp1 Glut_2" EXACT []
synonym: "4196 NLL-SOC Spp1 Glut_2" EXACT []
