name: PRP-NI-PRNc-GRN Otp Glut_3 Npy2r glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Skor2 (Mmus), Fam129a (Mmus), Otp (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PRP-NI-PRNc-GRN Otp Glut_3 cells by expression of Npy2r. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Pons , in or close to the regions: Tegmental reticular nucleus, Superior central nucleus raphe . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4217 PRP-NI-PRNc-GRN Otp Glut_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type PRP-NI-PRNc-GRN Otp Glut_3 Npy2r does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for nucleus prepositus (PRP), nucleus incertus (NI), pontine reticular nucleus, caudal part (PRNc), gigantocellular reticular nucleus (GRN). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "4217 PRP-NI-PRNc-GRN Otp Glut_3" EXACT []
