[Term]
id: PCL:0116598
name: PRP-NI-PRNc-GRN Otp Glut_3 Calca glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Evx2 (Mmus), Gm27239 (Mmus), Calca (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PRP-NI-PRNc-GRN Otp Glut_3 cells by expression of Calca, Evx2. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Gad2). These cells are located in the Pons , in or close to the regions: Pontine reticular nucleus, caudal part, Pontine reticular nucleus, Tegmental reticular nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4218 PRP-NI-PRNc-GRN Otp Glut_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, PRP-NI-PRNc-GRN Otp Glut_3 Calca does not have cells in nucleus prepositus (PRP), nucleus incertus (NI), gigantocellular reticular nucleus (GRN). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "4218 PRP-NI-PRNc-GRN Otp Glut_3" EXACT []
