[Term]
id: PCL:0116649
name: NTS Phox2b Glut_5 Lcp1 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Phox2a (Mmus), Lcp1 (Mmus), Abi3bp (Mmus). It is distinguished from other NTS Phox2b Glut_5 cells by expression of Lcp1, Abi3bp. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Medulla , in or close to the regions: Nucleus of the solitary tract . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4269 NTS Phox2b Glut_5." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
