[Term]
id: PCL:0116675
name: NTS Phox2b Glut_8 Dsc3 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Ptx3 (Mmus), Dbh (Mmus). It is distinguished from other NTS Phox2b Glut_8 cells by expression of Dsc3, Dbh. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Ddc, Chat, Dbh). These cells are located in the brain . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4295 NTS Phox2b Glut_8." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type NTS Phox2b Glut_8 Dsc3 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for nucleus of the solitary tract (NTS). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
