[Term]
id: PCL:0116683
name: NTS Phox2b Glut_10 Gm29683 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Phox2b (Mmus), Cdhr3 (Mmus), Sfrp2 (Mmus), Bcl11b (Mmus). It is distinguished from other NTS Phox2b Glut_10 cells by expression of Gm29683, Drd2. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Medulla , in or close to the regions: Spinal nucleus of the trigeminal, oral part, Parvicellular reticular nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4303 NTS Phox2b Glut_10." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type NTS Phox2b Glut_10 Gm29683 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for nucleus of the solitary tract (NTS). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
