id: PCL:0116685
name: NTS Phox2b Glut_10 Pdlim5 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Phox2b (Mmus), Rnf207 (Mmus), Atp10a (Mmus), Pdlim5 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other NTS Phox2b Glut_10 cells by expression of Pdlim5, Irx5, Htr1b, L3mbtl4. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Medulla , in or close to the regions: Spinal nucleus of the trigeminal, oral part, Nucleus of the solitary tract . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4305 NTS Phox2b Glut_10." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
