[Term]
id: PCL:0116691
name: PGRNd Dmbx1 Glut_1 Slc18a3 neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Mecom (Mmus), D130079A08Rik (Mmus), Tac1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PGRNd Dmbx1 Glut cells by expression of Slc18a3. It is cholinergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Chat, Slc18a3, Gad2). These cells are located in the Medulla , in or close to the regions: Gigantocellular reticular nucleus, Intermediate reticular nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4311 PGRNd Dmbx1 Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type PGRNd Dmbx1 Glut_1 Slc18a3 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for paragigantocellular reticular nucleus, dorsal part (PGRNd). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "4311 PGRNd Dmbx1 Glut_1" EXACT []
