id: PCL:0116715
name: PGRN-PARN-MDRN Hoxb5 Glut_2 Adgrf5 neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Ctcflos (Mmus), Adgrf5 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PGRN-PARN-MDRN Hoxb5 Glut_2 cells by expression of Adgrf5. It is cholinergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Chat, Slc18a3). These cells are located in the Medulla, brain , in or close to the regions: Intermediate reticular nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4335 PGRN-PARN-MDRN Hoxb5 Glut_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type PGRN-PARN-MDRN Hoxb5 Glut_2 Adgrf5 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for paragigantocellular reticular nucleus (PGRN), parvicellular reticular nucleus (PARN), medullary reticular nucleus (MDRN). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "4335 PGRN-PARN-MDRN Hoxb5 Glut_2" EXACT []
