[Term]
id: PCL:0116720
name: PGRN-PARN-MDRN Hoxb5 Glut_2 Nkx6-1 neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Serpinb7 (Mmus), Vsx2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PGRN-PARN-MDRN Hoxb5 Glut_2 cells by expression of Nkx6-1. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Medulla , in or close to the regions: Gigantocellular reticular nucleus, Magnocellular reticular nucleus, Paragigantocellular reticular nucleus, lateral part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4340 PGRN-PARN-MDRN Hoxb5 Glut_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
