name: PGRN-PARN-MDRN Hoxb5 Glut_2 Gli3 neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Mecom (Mmus), Evx2 (Mmus), Gli3 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PGRN-PARN-MDRN Hoxb5 Glut_2 cells by expression of Gli3, Otp. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Pons , in or close to the regions: Pontine reticular nucleus, caudal part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4341 PGRN-PARN-MDRN Hoxb5 Glut_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
