[Term]
id: PCL:0116728
name: PGRN-PARN-MDRN Hoxb5 Glut_2 Barhl2 neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Barhl1 (Mmus), Lhx5 (Mmus), Gm39185 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PGRN-PARN-MDRN Hoxb5 Glut_2 cells by expression of Barhl2. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Midbrain , in or close to the regions: Midbrain reticular nucleus, Anterior pretectal nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4348 PGRN-PARN-MDRN Hoxb5 Glut_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type PGRN-PARN-MDRN Hoxb5 Glut_2 Barhl2 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for paragigantocellular reticular nucleus (PGRN), parvicellular reticular nucleus (PARN), medullary reticular nucleus (MDRN). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "4348 PGRN-PARN-MDRN Hoxb5 Glut_2" EXACT []
