[Term]
id: PCL:0116762
name: PGRN-PARN-MDRN Hoxb5 Glut_5 Ttc6 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Abcc9 (Mmus), Ttc6 (Mmus), Glp1r (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PGRN-PARN-MDRN Hoxb5 Glut_5 cells by expression of Ttc6, Glp1r. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Ddc). These cells are located in the Medulla , in or close to the regions: Spinal nucleus of the trigeminal, interpolar part, Nucleus of the solitary tract, Parvicellular reticular nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4382 PGRN-PARN-MDRN Hoxb5 Glut_5." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
