[Term]
id: PCL:0116769
name: PGRN-PARN-MDRN Hoxb5 Glut_6 Glp1r glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Tlx1 (Mmus), Zeb2 (Mmus), Glp1r (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PGRN-PARN-MDRN Hoxb5 Glut_6 cells by expression of Glp1r, Tlx1. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Gad2, Ddc). These cells are located in the Pons , in or close to the regions: Pontine reticular nucleus, caudal part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4389 PGRN-PARN-MDRN Hoxb5 Glut_6." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type PGRN-PARN-MDRN Hoxb5 Glut_6 Glp1r does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for paragigantocellular reticular nucleus (PGRN), parvicellular reticular nucleus (PARN), medullary reticular nucleus (MDRN). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "4389 PGRN-PARN-MDRN Hoxb5 Glut_6" EXACT []
