[Term]
id: PCL:0116773
name: PGRN-PARN-MDRN Hoxb5 Glut_6 Slc10a4 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Onecut3 (Mmus), Slc17a8 (Mmus), Shox2 (Mmus), Met (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PGRN-PARN-MDRN Hoxb5 Glut_6 cells by expression of Slc10a4, Tll1, Shox2. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Medulla, brain , in or close to the regions: Spinal nucleus of the trigeminal, interpolar part, Spinal nucleus of the trigeminal, oral part, spinal tract of the trigeminal nerve . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4393 PGRN-PARN-MDRN Hoxb5 Glut_6." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type PGRN-PARN-MDRN Hoxb5 Glut_6 Slc10a4 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for paragigantocellular reticular nucleus (PGRN), parvicellular reticular nucleus (PARN), medullary reticular nucleus (MDRN). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "4393 PGRN-PARN-MDRN Hoxb5 Glut_6" EXACT []
