[Term]
id: PCL:0116776
name: PGRN-PARN-MDRN Hoxb5 Glut_6 Npffr2 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Tlx1 (Mmus), Phox2b (Mmus), Npffr2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PGRN-PARN-MDRN Hoxb5 Glut_6 cells by expression of Phox2b, Tlx1. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Ddc). These cells are located in the Medulla, Pons, brain , in or close to the regions: Pontine reticular nucleus, caudal part, inferior cerebellar peduncle, Intermediate reticular nucleus, Medial vestibular nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4396 PGRN-PARN-MDRN Hoxb5 Glut_6." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, PGRN-PARN-MDRN Hoxb5 Glut_6 Npffr2 does not have cells in paragigantocellular reticular nucleus (PGRN), medullary reticular nucleus (MDRN). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "4396 PGRN-PARN-MDRN Hoxb5 Glut_6" EXACT []
