[Term]
id: PCL:0116780
name: PGRN-PARN-MDRN Hoxb5 Glut_7 Irx5 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Irx3 (Mmus), Cpa6 (Mmus), Lhx1 (Mmus), Adamts18 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PGRN-PARN-MDRN Hoxb5 Glut_7 cells by expression of Irx5, Cpa6, Gad2. It is glutamatergic and GABAergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Gad2, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Medulla, Pons , in or close to the regions: Medial vestibular nucleus, Superior vestibular nucleus, Parabrachial nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4400 PGRN-PARN-MDRN Hoxb5 Glut_7." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type PGRN-PARN-MDRN Hoxb5 Glut_7 Irx5 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for paragigantocellular reticular nucleus (PGRN), parvicellular reticular nucleus (PARN), medullary reticular nucleus (MDRN). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "4400 PGRN-PARN-MDRN Hoxb5 Glut_7" EXACT []
