[Term]
id: PCL:0116833
name: CU-ECU-SPVI Foxb1 Glut_1 Klhl14 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Evx1os (Mmus), Pou4f1 (Mmus), Crh (Mmus), Klhl14 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other CU-ECU-SPVI Foxb1 Glut_1 cells by expression of Klhl14, Cp. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Medulla, brain , in or close to the regions: Spinal nucleus of the trigeminal, interpolar part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4453 CU-ECU-SPVI Foxb1 Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, CU-ECU-SPVI Foxb1 Glut_1 Klhl14 does not have cells in cuneate nucleus (CU), external cuneate nucleus (ECU). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
