[Term]
id: PCL:0116845
name: CU-ECU-SPVI Foxb1 Glut_1 Gbx2 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Foxb1 (Mmus), Gbx2 (Mmus), Trpa1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other CU-ECU-SPVI Foxb1 Glut_1 cells by expression of Gbx2, Trpa1. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Medulla, brain , in or close to the regions: Cuneate nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4465 CU-ECU-SPVI Foxb1 Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, CU-ECU-SPVI Foxb1 Glut_1 Gbx2 does not have cells in external cuneate nucleus (ECU). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "4465 CU-ECU-SPVI Foxb1 Glut_1" EXACT []
