[Term]
id: PCL:0116846
name: CU-ECU-SPVI Foxb1 Glut_1 Cckar glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Corin (Mmus), Slc5a7 (Mmus), Cckar (Mmus). It is distinguished from other CU-ECU-SPVI Foxb1 Glut_1 cells by expression of Cckar. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Slc17a8). These cells are located in the Medulla, brain , in or close to the regions: choroid plexus, lateral recess, Medial vestibular nucleus, Spinal vestibular nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4466 CU-ECU-SPVI Foxb1 Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type CU-ECU-SPVI Foxb1 Glut_1 Cckar does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for cuneate nucleus (CU), external cuneate nucleus (ECU), spinal nucleus of the trigeminal, interpolar part (SPVI). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "4466 CU-ECU-SPVI Foxb1 Glut_1" EXACT []
