[Term]
id: PCL:0116847
name: CU-ECU-SPVI Foxb1 Glut_1 Cd109 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Cd109 (Mmus), Hoxc4 (Mmus), Evx2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other CU-ECU-SPVI Foxb1 Glut_1 cells by expression of Cd109. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Medulla , in or close to the regions: Spinal nucleus of the trigeminal, interpolar part, Spinal nucleus of the trigeminal, oral part, spinal tract of the trigeminal nerve, Parvicellular reticular nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4467 CU-ECU-SPVI Foxb1 Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
