id: PCL:0116851
name: CU-ECU-SPVI Foxb1 Glut_2 Ttn glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Ttn (Mmus), Hoxc4 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other CU-ECU-SPVI Foxb1 Glut_2 cells by expression of Ttn. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Medulla, brain , in or close to the regions: Spinal nucleus of the trigeminal, interpolar part, spinal tract of the trigeminal nerve . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4471 CU-ECU-SPVI Foxb1 Glut_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, CU-ECU-SPVI Foxb1 Glut_2 Ttn does not have cells in cuneate nucleus (CU), external cuneate nucleus (ECU). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "4471 CU-ECU-SPVI Foxb1 Glut_2" EXACT []
