[Term]
id: PCL:0116868
name: MV-SPIV Phox2b Ebf3 Lbx1 Glut_4 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Rxfp2 (Mmus), Phox2b (Mmus), Kcnj5 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MV-SPIV Phox2b Ebf3 Lbx1 Glut cells by expression of Ppp1r17. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Medulla , in or close to the regions: Medial vestibular nucleus, Lateral vestibular nucleus, Parvicellular reticular nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4488 MV-SPIV Phox2b Ebf3 Lbx1 Glut_4." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, MV-SPIV Phox2b Ebf3 Lbx1 Glut_4 does not have cells in spinal vestibular nucleus (SPIV). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
