[Term]
id: PCL:0116873
name: MV-SPIV Zic4 Neurod2 Glut_1 Insrr glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Insrr (Mmus), Pou4f1 (Mmus), Hoxa5 (Mmus), Bnc2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MV-SPIV Zic4 Neurod2 Glut_1 cells by expression of Insrr, Ebf2, Bnc2. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Medulla , in or close to the regions: choroid plexus, Medial vestibular nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4493 MV-SPIV Zic4 Neurod2 Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, MV-SPIV Zic4 Neurod2 Glut_1 Insrr does not have cells in spinal vestibular nucleus (SPIV). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "4493 MV-SPIV Zic4 Neurod2 Glut_1" EXACT []
