[Term]
id: PCL:0116877
name: MV-SPIV Zic4 Neurod2 Glut_1 Npy glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Gpx2 (Mmus), Abca4 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MV-SPIV Zic4 Neurod2 Glut_1 cells by expression of Npy. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Medulla, Cerebellum , in or close to the regions: Ventral cochlear nucleus, Flocculus, Dentate nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4497 MV-SPIV Zic4 Neurod2 Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type MV-SPIV Zic4 Neurod2 Glut_1 Npy does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for medial vestibular nucleus (MV), spinal vestibular nucleus (SPIV). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
