id: PCL:0116879
name: MV-SPIV Zic4 Neurod2 Glut_2 Tnni3k glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Ucma (Mmus), D130009I18Rik (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MV-SPIV Zic4 Neurod2 Glut_2 cells by expression of Tnni3k, Ucma. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Chat). These cells are located in the Medulla, brain , in or close to the regions: Medial vestibular nucleus, Cuneate nucleus, Nodulus (X) . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4499 MV-SPIV Zic4 Neurod2 Glut_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, MV-SPIV Zic4 Neurod2 Glut_2 Tnni3k does not have cells in spinal vestibular nucleus (SPIV). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "4499 MV-SPIV Zic4 Neurod2 Glut_2" EXACT []
