[Term]
id: PCL:0116880
name: MV-SPIV Zic4 Neurod2 Glut_2 Hoxb6 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Olig3 (Mmus), Hoxb8 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MV-SPIV Zic4 Neurod2 Glut_2 cells by expression of Hoxb6. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the brain . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4500 MV-SPIV Zic4 Neurod2 Glut_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type MV-SPIV Zic4 Neurod2 Glut_2 Hoxb6 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for medial vestibular nucleus (MV), spinal vestibular nucleus (SPIV). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "4500 MV-SPIV Zic4 Neurod2 Glut_2" EXACT []
