[Term]
id: PCL:0116886
name: MV-SPIV Zic4 Neurod2 Glut_3 Pnoc neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Prrxl1 (Mmus), Serpina9 (Mmus), Bnc2 (Mmus), Lama1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MV-SPIV Zic4 Neurod2 Glut_3 cells by expression of Pnoc, Bnc2. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Medulla, brain , in or close to the regions: fourth ventricle, Medial vestibular nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4506 MV-SPIV Zic4 Neurod2 Glut_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, MV-SPIV Zic4 Neurod2 Glut_3 Pnoc does not have cells in spinal vestibular nucleus (SPIV). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "4506 MV-SPIV Zic4 Neurod2 Glut_3" EXACT []
