[Term]
id: PCL:0116890
name: MV-SPIV Zic4 Neurod2 Glut_3 Prph neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Gpx2 (Mmus), Crispld2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MV-SPIV Zic4 Neurod2 Glut_3 cells by expression of Prph. It is cholinergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Chat, Slc17a7, Slc18a3). These cells are located in the Medulla, brain , in or close to the regions: choroid plexus, fourth ventricle, Medial vestibular nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4510 MV-SPIV Zic4 Neurod2 Glut_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, MV-SPIV Zic4 Neurod2 Glut_3 Prph does not have cells in spinal vestibular nucleus (SPIV). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "4510 MV-SPIV Zic4 Neurod2 Glut_3" EXACT []
