[Term]
id: PCL:0116908
name: NTS Dbh Glut_1 Pou4f1 neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Olfr78 (Mmus), D130079A08Rik (Mmus), Shox2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other NTS Dbh Glut_1 cells by expression of Pou4f1, Shox2. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the brain . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4528 NTS Dbh Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type NTS Dbh Glut_1 Pou4f1 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for nucleus of the solitary tract (NTS). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "4528 NTS Dbh Glut_1" EXACT []
