[Term]
id: PCL:0116909
name: NTS Dbh Glut_1 Slc6a2 neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Pirt (Mmus), Asgr1 (Mmus), Slc6a2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other NTS Dbh Glut_1 cells by expression of Pou4f1, Slc6a2. It is noradrenergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Dbh, Ddc, Slc6a2). These cells are located in the Medulla, brain , in or close to the regions: Area postrema . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4529 NTS Dbh Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
