[Term]
id: PCL:0116927
name: NTS Dbh Glut_4 En1 neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Phox2a (Mmus), En1 (Mmus), H2-Q2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other NTS Dbh Glut_4 cells by expression of En1, H2-Q2. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Ddc, Gad2, Dbh). These cells are located in the Pons, brain , in or close to the regions: Barrington's nucleus, Parabrachial nucleus, Pontine central gray . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4547 NTS Dbh Glut_4." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type NTS Dbh Glut_4 En1 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for nucleus of the solitary tract (NTS). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "4547 NTS Dbh Glut_4" EXACT []
