[Term]
id: PCL:0116928
name: NTS Dbh Glut_4 Calca neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Slc6a2 (Mmus), Chrnb3 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other NTS Dbh Glut_4 cells by expression of Calca. It is noradrenergic (inferred from expression of Slc6a2, Ddc, Th, Gad2, Dbh, Slc18a2). These cells are located in the Medulla, Pons , in or close to the regions: Medial vestibular nucleus, Parabrachial nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4548 NTS Dbh Glut_4." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type NTS Dbh Glut_4 Calca does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for nucleus of the solitary tract (NTS). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme. Warning: Despite its name, NTS Dbh Glut_4 Calca does not secrete the neurotransmitter Glut, as assessed by expression of multiple marker genes.
synonym: "4548 NTS Dbh Glut_4" EXACT []
