[Term]
id: PCL:0116929
name: NTS Dbh Glut_5 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Gfral (Mmus), Pirt (Mmus), Lrat (Mmus). It is distinguished from other NTS Dbh Glut cells by expression of Nts, Lrat. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Ddc, Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Medulla, brain , in or close to the regions: Area postrema . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4549 NTS Dbh Glut_5." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06808-9, https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Rationale for assigning this type to reference data: Assigned by automated classification (ELK) of a definition built from soma location Basic cell groups and regions (grey; ≥80% of grey-matter cells in both the Yao 2023 and Zhuang 2023 MERFISH atlases) and neurotransmitter glutamate (all clusters) against CL 2026-06-08. Basis: NT. Other inferred CL parents: central nervous system neuron. [WMBO CL promotion round 1, 2026-10-13] Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type NTS Dbh Glut_5 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for nucleus of the solitary tract (NTS). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme. {xref="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z", xref="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06808-9"}
synonym: "1008 NTS Dbh Glut_5" EXACT []
