name: SPVO Mafa Meis2 Glut_1 Cryba2 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Cdh1 (Mmus), Cryba2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other SPVO Mafa Meis2 Glut cells by expression of Cryba2. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Medulla , in or close to the regions: Spinal nucleus of the trigeminal, oral part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4567 SPVO Mafa Meis2 Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
