name: SPVC Nmu Glut_1 Car12 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Nmu (Mmus), Upp1 (Mmus), Hoxb7 (Mmus), Scara5 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other SPVC Nmu Glut_1 cells by expression of Car12, Hoxb7. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the brain . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4588 SPVC Nmu Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type SPVC Nmu Glut_1 Car12 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for spinal nucleus of the trigeminal, caudal part (SPVC). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "4588 SPVC Nmu Glut_1" EXACT []
