[Term]
id: PCL:0116977
name: MDRNv Crp Glut_1 Prom1 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Lhx4 (Mmus), Ddr2 (Mmus), A730046J19Rik (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MDRNv Crp Glut cells by expression of Prom1. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Medulla, brain , in or close to the regions: Nucleus ambiguus, ventral division, Lateral reticular nucleus, magnocellular part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4597 MDRNv Crp Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
