[Term]
id: PCL:0116993
name: CS-RPO Meis2 Gaba_2 Acvr1c GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Svep1 (Mmus), Cckar (Mmus), Pax5 (Mmus), Meis2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other CS-RPO Meis2 Gaba_2 cells by expression of Acvr1c. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Midbrain, Pons , in or close to the regions: Midbrain reticular nucleus, Pontine reticular nucleus, Superior central nucleus raphe . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4613 CS-RPO Meis2 Gaba_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, CS-RPO Meis2 Gaba_2 Acvr1c does not have cells in nucleus raphe pontis (RPO). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "4613 CS-RPO Meis2 Gaba_2" EXACT []
