[Term]
id: PCL:0117010
name: CS-RPO Meis2 Gaba_5 Col6a1 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Olig3 (Mmus), Chrna2 (Mmus), Cdhr1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other CS-RPO Meis2 Gaba_5 cells by expression of Col6a1. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Pons , in or close to the regions: Tegmental reticular nucleus, Nucleus incertus, medial lemniscus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4630 CS-RPO Meis2 Gaba_5." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type CS-RPO Meis2 Gaba_5 Col6a1 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for superior central nucleus raphe (CS), nucleus raphe pontis (RPO). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
