[Term]
id: PCL:0117031
name: PRNc Otp Gly-Gaba_3 Tafa4 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Gm4881 (Mmus), Rbp1 (Mmus), Nxph4 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PRNc Otp Gly-Gaba_3 cells by expression of Tafa4, Cartpt. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Slc6a5). These cells are located in the Pons , in or close to the regions: Tegmental reticular nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4651 PRNc Otp Gly-Gaba_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type PRNc Otp Gly-Gaba_3 Tafa4 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for pontine reticular nucleus, caudal part (PRNc). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "4651 PRNc Otp Gly-Gaba_3" EXACT []
