[Term]
id: PCL:0117036
name: PRNc Otp Gly-Gaba_4 Defb1 GABA-Gly neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABA-Gly neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Clec10a (Mmus), Hgf (Mmus), Shisa8 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PRNc Otp Gly-Gaba_4 cells by expression of Defb1, Prlr. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Slc32a1, Gad1, Slc6a5). These cells are located in the Medulla, Pons, brain , in or close to the regions: Pontine reticular nucleus, caudal part, pyramid . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4656 PRNc Otp Gly-Gaba_4." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
