[Term]
id: PCL:0117047
name: PB Sst Gly-Gaba_1 Pax5 GABA-Gly neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABA-Gly neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Clec10a (Mmus), Vipr2 (Mmus), Pax5 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PB Sst Gly-Gaba_1 cells by expression of Pax5. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Slc6a5). These cells are located in the Cerebellum, brain , in or close to the regions: fourth ventricle, Lobule II . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4667 PB Sst Gly-Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type PB Sst Gly-Gaba_1 Pax5 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for parabrachial nucleus (PB). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
