[Term]
id: PCL:0117066
name: CS-PRNr-PCG Tmem163 Otp Gaba_3 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Pax3 (Mmus), Tac2 (Mmus), Igf1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other CS-PRNr-PCG Tmem163 Otp Gaba cells by expression of Pax3. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Pons , in or close to the regions: Posterodorsal tegmental nucleus, Superior central nucleus raphe, Pontine central gray . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4686 CS-PRNr-PCG Tmem163 Otp Gaba_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, CS-PRNr-PCG Tmem163 Otp Gaba_3 does not have cells in pontine reticular nucleus (PRNr). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
