[Term]
id: PCL:0117073
name: CS-PRNr-DR En1 Sox2 Gaba_1 Gm32828 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Sox14 (Mmus), Gm32828 (Mmus), Rxfp1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other CS-PRNr-DR En1 Sox2 Gaba_1 cells by expression of Gm32828, Sema3d. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Pons , in or close to the regions: Laterodorsal tegmental nucleus, Pontine central gray . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4693 CS-PRNr-DR En1 Sox2 Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type CS-PRNr-DR En1 Sox2 Gaba_1 Gm32828 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for superior central nucleus raphe (CS), pontine reticular nucleus (PRNr), dorsal nucleus raphe (DR). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "4693 CS-PRNr-DR En1 Sox2 Gaba_1" EXACT []
