[Term]
id: PCL:0117074
name: CS-PRNr-DR En1 Sox2 Gaba_2 Npy2r GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Ttc6 (Mmus), Trh (Mmus), Slc32a1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other CS-PRNr-DR En1 Sox2 Gaba_2 cells by expression of Npy2r. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Midbrain, Pons , in or close to the regions: Pontine reticular nucleus, Anterior tegmental nucleus, Superior central nucleus raphe . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4694 CS-PRNr-DR En1 Sox2 Gaba_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
