[Term]
id: PCL:0117083
name: CS-PRNr-DR En1 Sox2 Gaba_2 Cpne7 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Sox14 (Mmus), Sp9 (Mmus), Cpne7 (Mmus), Egflam (Mmus). It is distinguished from other CS-PRNr-DR En1 Sox2 Gaba_2 cells by expression of Cpne7, Egflam. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Ddc). These cells are located in the Midbrain, Pons , in or close to the regions: Interpeduncular nucleus, apical, Interpeduncular nucleus, lateral, Superior central nucleus raphe . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4703 CS-PRNr-DR En1 Sox2 Gaba_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, CS-PRNr-DR En1 Sox2 Gaba_2 Cpne7 does not have cells in dorsal nucleus raphe (DR). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
