[Term]
id: PCL:0117097
name: NI-RPO Gata3 Nr4a2 Gaba_1 Pkd2l1 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Areg (Mmus), Hoxb2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other NI-RPO Gata3 Nr4a2 Gaba_1 cells by expression of Pkd2l1, Areg. It is glutamatergic and GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Slc32a1, Gad1, Slc17a8). These cells are located in the Pons , in or close to the regions: fourth ventricle, Supragenual nucleus, Pontine central gray . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4717 NI-RPO Gata3 Nr4a2 Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type NI-RPO Gata3 Nr4a2 Gaba_1 Pkd2l1 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for nucleus incertus (NI), nucleus raphe pontis (RPO). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "4717 NI-RPO Gata3 Nr4a2 Gaba_1" EXACT []
