[Term]
id: PCL:0117107
name: NI-RPO Gata3 Nr4a2 Gaba_2 Galr1 neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Areg (Mmus), Galr1 (Mmus), C1ql1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other NI-RPO Gata3 Nr4a2 Gaba_2 cells by expression of Galr1, C1ql1. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a8, Slc32a1, Ddc). These cells are located in the Pons, brain , in or close to the regions: fourth ventricle, Nucleus incertus, Pontine central gray, Lobule II . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4727 NI-RPO Gata3 Nr4a2 Gaba_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, NI-RPO Gata3 Nr4a2 Gaba_2 Galr1 does not have cells in nucleus raphe pontis (RPO). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme. Warning: Despite its name, NI-RPO Gata3 Nr4a2 Gaba_2 Galr1 does not secrete the neurotransmitter Gaba, as assessed by expression of multiple marker genes.
synonym: "4727 NI-RPO Gata3 Nr4a2 Gaba_2" EXACT []
