[Term]
id: PCL:0117109
name: NI-RPO Gata3 Nr4a2 Gaba_3 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Tnnt1 (Mmus), Plcg2 (Mmus), Gpr101 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other NI-RPO Gata3 Nr4a2 Gaba cells by expression of Otx1, Scn5a. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Pons , in or close to the regions: Nucleus raphe pontis, Nucleus incertus, Pontine central gray . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4729 NI-RPO Gata3 Nr4a2 Gaba_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06808-9, https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Rationale for assigning this type to reference data: Assigned by automated classification (ELK) of a definition built from soma location Brain stem (BS; ≥80% of grey-matter cells in both the Yao 2023 and Zhuang 2023 MERFISH atlases) and neurotransmitter GABA (all clusters) against CL 2026-06-08. Basis: NT. Other inferred CL parents: central nervous system neuron. [WMBO CL promotion round 1, 2026-10-13] Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. {xref="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z", xref="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06808-9"}
