[Term]
id: PCL:0117111
name: NI-RPO Gata3 Nr4a2 Gaba_4 Pappa2 neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Pappa2 (Mmus), Tafa4 (Mmus), Sox14 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other NI-RPO Gata3 Nr4a2 Gaba_4 cells by expression of Pappa2. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad1, Slc32a1, Gad2). These cells are located in the Pons , in or close to the regions: Pontine reticular nucleus, Tegmental reticular nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4731 NI-RPO Gata3 Nr4a2 Gaba_4." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type NI-RPO Gata3 Nr4a2 Gaba_4 Pappa2 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for nucleus incertus (NI), nucleus raphe pontis (RPO). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
