[Term]
id: PCL:0117115
name: LDT-PCG-CS Gata3 Lhx1 Gaba_1 Tll2 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Crhbp (Mmus), Tll2 (Mmus), Gata3 (Mmus), Pdyn (Mmus). It is distinguished from other LDT-PCG-CS Gata3 Lhx1 Gaba_1 cells by expression of Tll2, Pdyn. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Midbrain, Pons , in or close to the regions: Midbrain reticular nucleus, Pontine reticular nucleus, Laterodorsal tegmental nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4735 LDT-PCG-CS Gata3 Lhx1 Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, LDT-PCG-CS Gata3 Lhx1 Gaba_1 Tll2 does not have cells in pontine central gray (PCG), superior central nucleus raphe (CS). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "4735 LDT-PCG-CS Gata3 Lhx1 Gaba_1" EXACT []
