[Term]
id: PCL:0117117
name: LDT-PCG-CS Gata3 Lhx1 Gaba_1 Ltbp1 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Otx1 (Mmus), Nts (Mmus), Gm38505 (Mmus), Ebf3 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other LDT-PCG-CS Gata3 Lhx1 Gaba_1 cells by expression of Ltbp1, Pax5. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the brain , in or close to the regions: cerebral aqueduct . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4737 LDT-PCG-CS Gata3 Lhx1 Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type LDT-PCG-CS Gata3 Lhx1 Gaba_1 Ltbp1 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for laterodorsal tegmental nucleus (LDT), pontine central gray (PCG), superior central nucleus raphe (CS). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
