[Term]
id: PCL:0117118
name: LDT-PCG-CS Gata3 Lhx1 Gaba_1 Gm12128 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Slc17a8 (Mmus), Gm12128 (Mmus), Crhbp (Mmus). It is distinguished from other LDT-PCG-CS Gata3 Lhx1 Gaba_1 cells by expression of Gm12128, Slc17a8. It is glutamatergic and GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Slc17a8). These cells are located in the Pons, brain , in or close to the regions: cerebral aqueduct, Periaqueductal gray, Dorsal tegmental nucleus, Pontine central gray . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4738 LDT-PCG-CS Gata3 Lhx1 Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, LDT-PCG-CS Gata3 Lhx1 Gaba_1 Gm12128 does not have cells in laterodorsal tegmental nucleus (LDT), superior central nucleus raphe (CS). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
