[Term]
id: PCL:0117122
name: LDT-PCG-CS Gata3 Lhx1 Gaba_2 Tril GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Tnnt1 (Mmus), Kl (Mmus), Tril (Mmus). It is distinguished from other LDT-PCG-CS Gata3 Lhx1 Gaba_2 cells by expression of Tril. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Ddc). These cells are located in the Pons , in or close to the regions: Pontine central gray . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4742 LDT-PCG-CS Gata3 Lhx1 Gaba_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, LDT-PCG-CS Gata3 Lhx1 Gaba_2 Tril does not have cells in laterodorsal tegmental nucleus (LDT), superior central nucleus raphe (CS). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
