[Term]
id: PCL:0117125
name: LDT-PCG-CS Gata3 Lhx1 Gaba_4 GABA-Glut neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABA-Glut neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Slc17a8 (Mmus), Pax5 (Mmus), Scube2 (Mmus), Slc32a1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other LDT-PCG-CS Gata3 Lhx1 Gaba cells by expression of Scube2, Pax5. It is glutamatergic and GABAergic (inferred from expression of Slc32a1, Ddc, Slc17a8, Gad2, Gad1). These cells are located in the Midbrain, Pons, brain , in or close to the regions: cerebral aqueduct, Superior central nucleus raphe, superior cerebellar peduncle decussation, Pontine central gray . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4745 LDT-PCG-CS Gata3 Lhx1 Gaba_4." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06808-9, https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Rationale for assigning this type to reference data: Assigned by automated classification (ELK) of a definition built from soma location Brain stem (BS; ≥80% of grey-matter cells in both the Yao 2023 and Zhuang 2023 MERFISH atlases) and neurotransmitter GABA + glutamate (all clusters) against CL 2026-06-08. Basis: NT. Other inferred CL parents: central nervous system neuron. [WMBO CL promotion round 1, 2026-10-13] Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, LDT-PCG-CS Gata3 Lhx1 Gaba_4 does not have cells in laterodorsal tegmental nucleus (LDT). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme. {xref="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z", xref="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06808-9"}
