[Term]
id: PCL:0117130
name: PDTg-PCG Pax6 Gaba_1 Csgalnact1 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Pdzk1ip1 (Mmus), Chrna5 (Mmus), Glp1r (Mmus), Gm31592 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PDTg-PCG Pax6 Gaba_1 cells by expression of Csgalnact1. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Pons, brain , in or close to the regions: Superior central nucleus raphe, Pontine gray, Pontine central gray, fourth ventricle, Nucleus incertus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4750 PDTg-PCG Pax6 Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
