[Term]
id: PCL:0117143
name: LDT-PCG St18 Gaba_1 2810404M03Rik GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Morc1 (Mmus), Gdf6 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other LDT-PCG St18 Gaba_1 cells by expression of 2810404M03Rik. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Pons, brain , in or close to the regions: fourth ventricle, Medial vestibular nucleus, Pontine central gray . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4763 LDT-PCG St18 Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, LDT-PCG St18 Gaba_1 2810404M03Rik does not have cells in laterodorsal tegmental nucleus (LDT). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
