[Term]
id: PCL:0117158
name: DTN-LDT-IPN Otp Pax3 Gaba_1 Glp1r GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Pax7 (Mmus), Myzap (Mmus), Glp1r (Mmus). It is distinguished from other DTN-LDT-IPN Otp Pax3 Gaba_1 cells by expression of Glp1r. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Pons , in or close to the regions: Superior central nucleus raphe, Pontine central gray . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4778 DTN-LDT-IPN Otp Pax3 Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type DTN-LDT-IPN Otp Pax3 Gaba_1 Glp1r does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for dorsal tegmental nucleus (DTN), laterodorsal tegmental nucleus (LDT), interpeduncular nucleus (IPN). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "4778 DTN-LDT-IPN Otp Pax3 Gaba_1" EXACT []
