[Term]
id: PCL:0117170
name: DTN-LDT-IPN Otp Pax3 Gaba_4 Gm39185 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Pax7 (Mmus), Gm39185 (Mmus), Il1rapl2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other DTN-LDT-IPN Otp Pax3 Gaba_4 cells by expression of Gm39185. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Pons , in or close to the regions: Laterodorsal tegmental nucleus, Pontine central gray . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4790 DTN-LDT-IPN Otp Pax3 Gaba_4." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, DTN-LDT-IPN Otp Pax3 Gaba_4 Gm39185 does not have cells in dorsal tegmental nucleus (DTN), interpeduncular nucleus (IPN). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "4790 DTN-LDT-IPN Otp Pax3 Gaba_4" EXACT []
