[Term]
id: PCL:0117176
name: DTN-LDT-IPN Otp Pax3 Gaba_5 Casr GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Pax3 (Mmus), Satb2 (Mmus), Casr (Mmus). It is distinguished from other DTN-LDT-IPN Otp Pax3 Gaba_5 cells by expression of Casr, Pde3a. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Th). These cells are located in the Midbrain , in or close to the regions: Interpeduncular nucleus, rostral, Interpeduncular nucleus, dorsolateral . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4796 DTN-LDT-IPN Otp Pax3 Gaba_5." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, DTN-LDT-IPN Otp Pax3 Gaba_5 Casr does not have cells in dorsal tegmental nucleus (DTN), laterodorsal tegmental nucleus (LDT). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
