[Term]
id: PCL:0117177
name: DTN-LDT-IPN Otp Pax3 Gaba_5 Npsr1 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Vmn1r207-ps (Mmus), Satb2 (Mmus), Lypd1 (Mmus), Chrna2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other DTN-LDT-IPN Otp Pax3 Gaba_5 cells by expression of Npsr1, Chrna2, Lypd1. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Th). These cells are located in the Midbrain , in or close to the regions: Interpeduncular nucleus, rostral, Interpeduncular nucleus, dorsolateral . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4797 DTN-LDT-IPN Otp Pax3 Gaba_5." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, DTN-LDT-IPN Otp Pax3 Gaba_5 Npsr1 does not have cells in dorsal tegmental nucleus (DTN), laterodorsal tegmental nucleus (LDT). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "4797 DTN-LDT-IPN Otp Pax3 Gaba_5" EXACT []
