[Term]
id: PCL:0117186
name: NLL Gata3 Gly-Gaba_3 GABA-Gly neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABA-Gly neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Slc6a5 (Mmus), Gata3 (Mmus), Ebf2 (Mmus), Vwc2l (Mmus). It is distinguished from other NLL Gata3 Gly-Gaba cells by expression of A330102I10Rik, Kcnip1. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Slc6a5, Slc32a1, Gad2, Gad1). These cells are located in the Medulla, Pons, brain , in or close to the regions: Superior olivary complex, lateral part, Superior olivary complex, periolivary region . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4806 NLL Gata3 Gly-Gaba_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions.
