[Term]
id: PCL:0117193
name: PRP Otp Gly-Gaba_1 E330013P04Rik GABA-Gly neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABA-Gly neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Mgam (Mmus), E330013P04Rik (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PRP Otp Gly-Gaba_1 cells by expression of E330013P04Rik, Mgam. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Slc6a5). These cells are located in the Medulla , in or close to the regions: Nucleus prepositus, Medial vestibular nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4813 PRP Otp Gly-Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
