[Term]
id: PCL:0117198
name: PRP Otp Gly-Gaba_1 Gbx2 GABA-Gly neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABA-Gly neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Foxd3 (Mmus), Frem3 (Mmus), Hmcn1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PRP Otp Gly-Gaba_1 cells by expression of Gbx2, Frem3. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Slc6a5). These cells are located in the Medulla , in or close to the regions: Medial vestibular nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4818 PRP Otp Gly-Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type PRP Otp Gly-Gaba_1 Gbx2 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for nucleus prepositus (PRP). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "4818 PRP Otp Gly-Gaba_1" EXACT []
