[Term]
id: PCL:0117199
name: PRP Otp Gly-Gaba_1 Hoxb5 GABA-Gly neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABA-Gly neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Foxd3 (Mmus), Hs3st3b1 (Mmus), Chst9 (Mmus), Hoxb5 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PRP Otp Gly-Gaba_1 cells by expression of Hoxb5, Crabp1. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Slc6a5). These cells are located in the Medulla , in or close to the regions: Gigantocellular reticular nucleus, Intermediate reticular nucleus, Nucleus prepositus, Medial vestibular nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4819 PRP Otp Gly-Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
