name: PRP Otp Gly-Gaba_2 Wnt16 GABA-Gly neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABA-Gly neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Wnt16 (Mmus), Otp (Mmus), Vcan (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PRP Otp Gly-Gaba_2 cells by expression of Wnt16, Tacr1. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Slc6a5). These cells are located in the Medulla , in or close to the regions: Nucleus prepositus, Medial vestibular nucleus, Paragigantocellular reticular nucleus, dorsal part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4822 PRP Otp Gly-Gaba_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
