[Term]
id: PCL:0117206
name: PRP Otp Gly-Gaba_3 Cntnap3 GABA-Gly neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABA-Gly neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Pax8 (Mmus), Irx3 (Mmus), Cntnap3 (Mmus), Hoxd3 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PRP Otp Gly-Gaba_3 cells by expression of Cntnap3, Irx3. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Slc6a5). These cells are located in the Medulla , in or close to the regions: Nucleus prepositus, Medial vestibular nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4826 PRP Otp Gly-Gaba_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
