id: PCL:0117214
name: PRP Otp Gly-Gaba_4 Nr4a2 GABA-Gly neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABA-Gly neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Gm4881 (Mmus), Npy (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PRP Otp Gly-Gaba_4 cells by expression of Nr4a2. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Slc6a5). These cells are located in the Medulla , in or close to the regions: Gigantocellular reticular nucleus, fourth ventricle, Nucleus prepositus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4834 PRP Otp Gly-Gaba_4." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
