id: PCL:0117219
name: PRP Otp Gly-Gaba_5 Corin GABA-Gly neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABA-Gly neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Corin (Mmus), C1ql2 (Mmus), Ngfr (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PRP Otp Gly-Gaba_5 cells by expression of Corin, Adamts19. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Slc32a1, Gad1, Slc6a5). These cells are located in the Medulla , in or close to the regions: Gigantocellular reticular nucleus, Magnocellular reticular nucleus, Paragigantocellular reticular nucleus, dorsal part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4839 PRP Otp Gly-Gaba_5." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
