[Term]
id: PCL:0117232
name: MY Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_1 Nr4a2 neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Pax8 (Mmus), Nr4a2 (Mmus), 9530026P05Rik (Mmus), Slc6a5 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MY Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_1 cells by expression of Nr4a2, Calb1, Pax8. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Slc6a5). These cells are located in the Medulla, Pons , in or close to the regions: Gigantocellular reticular nucleus, Pontine reticular nucleus, caudal part, Intermediate reticular nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4852 MY Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
