[Term]
id: PCL:0117236
name: MY Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_1 Fibcd1 neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Pax8 (Mmus), Fibcd1 (Mmus), Otp (Mmus), Nell1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MY Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_1 cells by expression of Fibcd1, Otp, Galr1. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Slc32a1, Gad1, Slc6a5). These cells are located in the Pons , in or close to the regions: Pontine reticular nucleus, caudal part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4856 MY Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions.
