[Term]
id: PCL:0117249
name: MY Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_1 Ano2 neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Olfr48 (Mmus), Nr5a2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MY Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_1 cells by expression of Ano2. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc6a5, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Medulla , in or close to the regions: Gigantocellular reticular nucleus, Magnocellular reticular nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4869 MY Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
