[Term]
id: PCL:0117250
name: MY Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_1 Hmx2 neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of C1qtnf3 (Mmus), Hmx2 (Mmus), Slc6a5 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MY Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_1 cells by expression of Hmx2. It is cholinergic (inferred from expression of Slc18a3, Slc6a5, Slc32a1, Chat, Gad2, Gad1). These cells are located in the Medulla, brain , in or close to the regions: Paragigantocellular reticular nucleus, lateral part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4870 MY Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
