[Term]
id: PCL:0117256
name: MY Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_2 Unc5b GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Pax8 (Mmus), Unc5b (Mmus), Fras1 (Mmus), Chrm3 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MY Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_2 cells by expression of Unc5b, Pax8. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Slc6a5, Gad2, Slc32a1, Gad1). These cells are located in the Medulla , in or close to the regions: Medial vestibular nucleus, Spinal vestibular nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4876 MY Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions.
