[Term]
id: PCL:0117272
name: MY Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_3 Ikzf1 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Ikzf1 (Mmus), Irx4 (Mmus), A330008L17Rik (Mmus), Slc6a5 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MY Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_3 cells by expression of Ikzf1, Hs3st3b1, Grm8. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Slc32a1, Slc6a5, Gad1). These cells are located in the Pons , in or close to the regions: Peritrigeminal zone, Nucleus of the lateral lemniscus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4892 MY Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type MY Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_3 Ikzf1 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for medulla (MY). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "4892 MY Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_3" EXACT []
