[Term]
id: PCL:0117277
name: MY Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_3 Prrxl1 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Prrxl1 (Mmus), Rxfp3 (Mmus), Kcnj16 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MY Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_3 cells by expression of Prrxl1, Rxfp3. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Slc6a5). These cells are located in the Medulla, Pons , in or close to the regions: Pontine reticular nucleus, caudal part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4897 MY Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
