[Term]
id: PCL:0117279
name: MY Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_3 Frzb GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Skor1 (Mmus), Prokr2 (Mmus), Tfap2a (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MY Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_3 cells by expression of Igfbpl1, Frzb. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Medulla, Pons, brain , in or close to the regions: Koelliker-Fuse subnucleus, Principal sensory nucleus of the trigeminal . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4899 MY Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, MY Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_3 Frzb does not secrete the neurotransmitter Gly, as assessed by expression of multiple marker genes.
synonym: "4899 MY Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_3" EXACT []
