[Term]
id: PCL:0117282
name: MY Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_3 Tfap2e GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Tfap2e (Mmus), Piezo2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MY Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_3 cells by expression of Tfap2e, Piezo2. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Slc6a5). These cells are located in the Pons , in or close to the regions: Pontine reticular nucleus, caudal part, Peritrigeminal zone, Parabrachial nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4902 MY Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type MY Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_3 Tfap2e does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for medulla (MY). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
