[Term]
id: PCL:0117296
name: MY Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_5 Tac2 GABA-Gly neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABA-Gly neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Tac2 (Mmus), Pax8 (Mmus), Scn7a (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MY Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_5 cells by expression of Tac2. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Slc6a5, Slc32a1, Gad1). These cells are located in the Medulla, brain , in or close to the regions: Spinal nucleus of the trigeminal, interpolar part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4916 MY Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_5." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
