[Term]
id: PCL:0117301
name: MY Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_6 Sox6 GABA-Gly neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABA-Gly neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Mecom (Mmus), Skor1 (Mmus), Pgr15l (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MY Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_6 cells by expression of Sox6, Pgr15l. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Slc6a5). These cells are located in the Medulla , in or close to the regions: Lateral vestibular nucleus, Spinal nucleus of the trigeminal, oral part, Facial motor nucleus, Parvicellular reticular nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4921 MY Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_6." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions.
