[Term]
id: PCL:0117305
name: MY Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_8 GABA-Gly neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABA-Gly neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Esrrb (Mmus), Npy2r (Mmus), Rab38 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MY Lhx1 Gly-Gaba cells by expression of Rab38, Esrrb. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Slc6a5). These cells are located in the Medulla, Pons, brain , in or close to the regions: Spinal nucleus of the trigeminal, oral part, Principal sensory nucleus of the trigeminal, spinal tract of the trigeminal nerve . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4925 MY Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_8." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06808-9, https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Rationale for assigning this type to reference data: Assigned by automated classification (ELK) of a definition built from soma location Hindbrain (HB; ≥80% of grey-matter cells in both the Yao 2023 and Zhuang 2023 MERFISH atlases) and neurotransmitter GABA + glycine (all clusters) against CL 2026-06-08. Basis: NT. Other inferred CL parents: central nervous system neuron. [WMBO CL promotion round 1, 2026-10-13] Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. {xref="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z", xref="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06808-9"}
