[Term]
id: PCL:0117315
name: MV-SPIV-PRP Dmbx1 Gly-Gaba_1 Anxa11 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Nccrp1 (Mmus), Sox14 (Mmus), Tfap2b (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MV-SPIV-PRP Dmbx1 Gly-Gaba_1 cells by expression of Anxa11. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad1, Gad2, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Medulla, Cerebellum , in or close to the regions: Superior vestibular nucleus, Vestibulocerebellar nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4935 MV-SPIV-PRP Dmbx1 Gly-Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, MV-SPIV-PRP Dmbx1 Gly-Gaba_1 Anxa11 does not have cells in spinal vestibular nucleus (SPIV), nucleus prepositus (PRP). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme. Warning: Despite its name, MV-SPIV-PRP Dmbx1 Gly-Gaba_1 Anxa11 does not secrete the neurotransmitter Gly, as assessed by expression of multiple marker genes.
synonym: "4935 MV-SPIV-PRP Dmbx1 Gly-Gaba_1" EXACT []
