[Term]
id: PCL:0117326
name: MV-SPIV-PRP Dmbx1 Gly-Gaba_2 Gm15934 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Gm16685 (Mmus), Tfap2b (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MV-SPIV-PRP Dmbx1 Gly-Gaba_2 cells by expression of Gm15934. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Slc6a5). These cells are located in the Medulla, brain , in or close to the regions: fourth ventricle, Nucleus prepositus, Medial vestibular nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4946 MV-SPIV-PRP Dmbx1 Gly-Gaba_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, MV-SPIV-PRP Dmbx1 Gly-Gaba_2 Gm15934 does not have cells in spinal vestibular nucleus (SPIV). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme. Warning: Despite its name, MV-SPIV-PRP Dmbx1 Gly-Gaba_2 Gm15934 does not secrete the neurotransmitter Gly, as assessed by expression of multiple marker genes.
synonym: "4946 MV-SPIV-PRP Dmbx1 Gly-Gaba_2" EXACT []
