[Term]
id: PCL:0117330
name: MDRN Hoxb5 Ebf2 Gly-Gaba_1 Arhgap15 GABA-Gly neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABA-Gly neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Hoxb6 (Mmus), Sp8 (Mmus), Lgr6 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MDRN Hoxb5 Ebf2 Gly-Gaba cells by expression of Arhgap15. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc6a5, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Medulla, brain . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4950 MDRN Hoxb5 Ebf2 Gly-Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
