[Term]
id: PCL:0117340
name: MY Prox1 Lmo7 Gly-Gaba_1 Pgr15l GABA-Gly neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABA-Gly neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Wnt11 (Mmus), C1ql2 (Mmus), Pgr15l (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MY Prox1 Lmo7 Gly-Gaba cells by expression of Pgr15l. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc6a5, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Medulla , in or close to the regions: Intermediate reticular nucleus, Facial motor nucleus, Parvicellular reticular nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4960 MY Prox1 Lmo7 Gly-Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
