[Term]
id: PCL:0117346
name: NTS-MDRNd Prox1 Zic1 Gly-Gaba_1 Armh1 GABA-Gly neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABA-Gly neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Hoxb8 (Mmus), Neurog2 (Mmus), 1700012C08Rik (Mmus). It is distinguished from other NTS-MDRNd Prox1 Zic1 Gly-Gaba_1 cells by expression of Armh1. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Slc6a5). These cells are located in the brain . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4966 NTS-MDRNd Prox1 Zic1 Gly-Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type NTS-MDRNd Prox1 Zic1 Gly-Gaba_1 Armh1 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for nucleus of the solitary tract (NTS), medullary reticular nucleus, dorsal part (MDRNd). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "4966 NTS-MDRNd Prox1 Zic1 Gly-Gaba_1" EXACT []
