id: PCL:0117353
name: MV Nkx6-1 Gly-Gaba_1 Glp1r GABA-Gly neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABA-Gly neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Hpse (Mmus), Tmem72 (Mmus), Hoxc4 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MV Nkx6-1 Gly-Gaba_1 cells by expression of Glp1r. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Slc6a5). These cells are located in the Medulla , in or close to the regions: Medial vestibular nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4973 MV Nkx6-1 Gly-Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
