[Term]
id: PCL:0117368
name: PAS-MV Ebf2 Gly-Gaba_3 L3mbtl4 GABA-Gly neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABA-Gly neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Neurog2 (Mmus), Adamtsl3 (Mmus), Skor1 (Mmus), Tacr3 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PAS-MV Ebf2 Gly-Gaba_3 cells by expression of L3mbtl4. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Slc6a5). These cells are located in the Medulla , in or close to the regions: Medial vestibular nucleus, Spinal nucleus of the trigeminal, interpolar part, Parvicellular reticular nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4988 PAS-MV Ebf2 Gly-Gaba_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, PAS-MV Ebf2 Gly-Gaba_3 L3mbtl4 does not have cells in parasolitary nucleus (PAS). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
