[Term]
id: PCL:0117382
name: RPA Pax6 Hoxb5 Gly-Gaba_1 Vwa5a GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Sox14 (Mmus), Hoxb5 (Mmus), Cd24a (Mmus). It is distinguished from other RPA Pax6 Hoxb5 Gly-Gaba cells by expression of Vwa5a. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Slc6a5). These cells are located in the Medulla . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:5002 RPA Pax6 Hoxb5 Gly-Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type RPA Pax6 Hoxb5 Gly-Gaba_1 Vwa5a does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for nucleus raphe pallidus (RPA). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "5002 RPA Pax6 Hoxb5 Gly-Gaba_1" EXACT []
