[Term]
id: PCL:0117390
name: PRP Gata3 Slc6a5 Gly-Gaba_1 Pkhd1l1 GABA-Gly neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABA-Gly neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Tmem233 (Mmus), Pkhd1l1 (Mmus), Nxph4 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PRP Gata3 Slc6a5 Gly-Gaba cells by expression of Pkhd1l1, Nxph4. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Slc6a5). These cells are located in the Medulla, brain , in or close to the regions: fourth ventricle, Nucleus prepositus, Medial vestibular nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:5010 PRP Gata3 Slc6a5 Gly-Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions.
