[Term]
id: PCL:0117391
name: PRP Gata3 Slc6a5 Gly-Gaba_1 Tpbgl GABA-Gly neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABA-Gly neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Crabp1 (Mmus), Pdgfd (Mmus), Epha8 (Mmus), Nxph4 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PRP Gata3 Slc6a5 Gly-Gaba cells by expression of Tpbgl. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad1, Slc32a1, Gad2, Slc6a5). These cells are located in the Medulla , in or close to the regions: Nucleus prepositus, Medial vestibular nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:5011 PRP Gata3 Slc6a5 Gly-Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
