[Term]
id: PCL:0117401
name: PARN-MDRNd-NTS Gbx2 Gly-Gaba_1 B130024G19Rik GABA-Gly neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABA-Gly neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Hpse2 (Mmus), Pax8 (Mmus), Kcnab3 (Mmus), Ebf3 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PARN-MDRNd-NTS Gbx2 Gly-Gaba_1 cells by expression of B130024G19Rik, Cbln2, Cntn5. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Slc6a5). These cells are located in the Medulla , in or close to the regions: Spinal nucleus of the trigeminal, oral part, Parvicellular reticular nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:5021 PARN-MDRNd-NTS Gbx2 Gly-Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, PARN-MDRNd-NTS Gbx2 Gly-Gaba_1 B130024G19Rik does not have cells in medullary reticular nucleus, dorsal part (MDRNd), nucleus of the solitary tract (NTS). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "5021 PARN-MDRNd-NTS Gbx2 Gly-Gaba_1" EXACT []
