id: PCL:0117421
name: PARN-MDRNd-NTS Gbx2 Gly-Gaba_3 Krt19 GABA-Gly neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABA-Gly neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Krt19 (Mmus), Abcc9 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PARN-MDRNd-NTS Gbx2 Gly-Gaba_3 cells by expression of Krt19. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Slc32a1, Gad1, Slc6a5). These cells are located in the Medulla , in or close to the regions: Parvicellular reticular nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:5041 PARN-MDRNd-NTS Gbx2 Gly-Gaba_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, PARN-MDRNd-NTS Gbx2 Gly-Gaba_3 Krt19 does not have cells in medullary reticular nucleus, dorsal part (MDRNd), nucleus of the solitary tract (NTS). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "5041 PARN-MDRNd-NTS Gbx2 Gly-Gaba_3" EXACT []
