[Term]
id: PCL:0117428
name: PARN-MDRNd-NTS Gbx2 Gly-Gaba_4 Npas1 GABA-Gly neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABA-Gly neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Skor2 (Mmus), Cd24a (Mmus), Gbx2 (Mmus), Ecel1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PARN-MDRNd-NTS Gbx2 Gly-Gaba_4 cells by expression of Npas1, Cd24a. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Slc6a5). These cells are located in the Medulla, brain , in or close to the regions: Spinal nucleus of the trigeminal, interpolar part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:5048 PARN-MDRNd-NTS Gbx2 Gly-Gaba_4." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type PARN-MDRNd-NTS Gbx2 Gly-Gaba_4 Npas1 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for parvicellular reticular nucleus (PARN), medullary reticular nucleus, dorsal part (MDRNd), nucleus of the solitary tract (NTS). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "5048 PARN-MDRNd-NTS Gbx2 Gly-Gaba_4" EXACT []
