[Term]
id: PCL:0117445
name: PARN-MDRNd-NTS Gbx2 Gly-Gaba_7 Plekhg1 GABA-Gly neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABA-Gly neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Abca4 (Mmus), Tmem114 (Mmus), Mc4r (Mmus), Hoxb4 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PARN-MDRNd-NTS Gbx2 Gly-Gaba_7 cells by expression of Tmem114, Plekhg1. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Slc32a1, Gad1, Slc6a5). These cells are located in the Medulla , in or close to the regions: Spinal vestibular nucleus, Nucleus of the solitary tract . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:5065 PARN-MDRNd-NTS Gbx2 Gly-Gaba_7." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, PARN-MDRNd-NTS Gbx2 Gly-Gaba_7 Plekhg1 does not have cells in parvicellular reticular nucleus (PARN), medullary reticular nucleus, dorsal part (MDRNd). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
