[Term]
id: PCL:0117446
name: MV Nr4a2 Gly-Gaba dopaminergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A dopaminergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Adam34 (Mmus), Slc6a5 (Mmus), Th (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MY GABA cells by expression of Adam34, Slc6a5, Th. It is dopaminergic (inferred from expression of Slc32a1, Ddc, Th, Slc18a2, Slc6a5, Gad2, Gad1). These cells are located in the Medulla, Pons , in or close to the regions: Superior olivary complex, lateral part, Supratrigeminal nucleus, Parvicellular reticular nucleus, Koelliker-Fuse subnucleus, Medial vestibular nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:5066 MV Nr4a2 Gly-Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06808-9, https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Rationale for assigning this type to reference data: Assigned by automated classification (ELK) of a definition built from soma location Hindbrain (HB; ≥80% of grey-matter cells in both the Yao 2023 and Zhuang 2023 MERFISH atlases) and neurotransmitter dopamine (all clusters) against CL 2026-06-08. Basis: NT. Other inferred CL parents: central nervous system neuron. [WMBO CL promotion round 1, 2026-10-13] Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. {xref="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z", xref="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06808-9"}
