[Term]
id: PCL:0117448
name: IRN Dmbx1 Pax2 Gly-Gaba_1 Pax5 GABA-Gly neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABA-Gly neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Dmbx1 (Mmus), Hoxa5 (Mmus), Skor2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other IRN Dmbx1 Pax2 Gly-Gaba cells by expression of Pax5. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc6a5, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Medulla, brain , in or close to the regions: Nucleus of the solitary tract, Parvicellular reticular nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:5068 IRN Dmbx1 Pax2 Gly-Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type IRN Dmbx1 Pax2 Gly-Gaba_1 Pax5 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for intermediate reticular nucleus (IRN). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
