[Term]
id: PCL:0117452
name: NTS-PARN Neurod2 Gly-Gaba_1 Scn7a GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Zbtb42 (Mmus), Hoxb8 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other NTS-PARN Neurod2 Gly-Gaba_1 cells by expression of Scn7a, Chrna3. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Slc6a5). These cells are located in the brain . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:5072 NTS-PARN Neurod2 Gly-Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type NTS-PARN Neurod2 Gly-Gaba_1 Scn7a does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for nucleus of the solitary tract (NTS), parvicellular reticular nucleus (PARN). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
