[Term]
id: PCL:0117472
name: NTS-PARN Neurod2 Gly-Gaba_3 C1ql1 GABA-Gly neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABA-Gly neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Cyp1b1 (Mmus), Slc6a5 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other NTS-PARN Neurod2 Gly-Gaba_3 cells by expression of C1ql1. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Slc6a5, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Pons, brain , in or close to the regions: rubrospinal tract . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:5092 NTS-PARN Neurod2 Gly-Gaba_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type NTS-PARN Neurod2 Gly-Gaba_3 C1ql1 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for nucleus of the solitary tract (NTS), parvicellular reticular nucleus (PARN). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
