id: PCL:0117474
name: NTS-PARN Neurod2 Gly-Gaba_3 Slc35d3 GABA-Gly neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABA-Gly neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Lbx1 (Mmus), Cdh23 (Mmus), Rgs5 (Mmus), Edil3 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other NTS-PARN Neurod2 Gly-Gaba_3 cells by expression of Slc35d3, Cdh23. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Slc32a1, Gad1, Slc6a5). These cells are located in the Medulla , in or close to the regions: Spinal nucleus of the trigeminal, interpolar part, Spinal nucleus of the trigeminal, oral part, spinal tract of the trigeminal nerve, Parvicellular reticular nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:5094 NTS-PARN Neurod2 Gly-Gaba_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, NTS-PARN Neurod2 Gly-Gaba_3 Slc35d3 does not have cells in nucleus of the solitary tract (NTS). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "5094 NTS-PARN Neurod2 Gly-Gaba_3" EXACT []
