[Term]
id: PCL:0117480
name: NTS-PARN Neurod2 Gly-Gaba_4 Bmp3 GABA-Gly neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABA-Gly neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Zbtb42 (Mmus), Col12a1 (Mmus), Gmnc (Mmus), Lama1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other NTS-PARN Neurod2 Gly-Gaba_4 cells by expression of Bmp3, Gmnc, Lepr. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Slc6a5). These cells are located in the Medulla , in or close to the regions: Spinal vestibular nucleus, Nucleus of the solitary tract, Parasolitary nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:5100 NTS-PARN Neurod2 Gly-Gaba_4." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, NTS-PARN Neurod2 Gly-Gaba_4 Bmp3 does not have cells in parvicellular reticular nucleus (PARN). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "5100 NTS-PARN Neurod2 Gly-Gaba_4" EXACT []
