[Term]
id: PCL:0117488
name: NTS-PARN Neurod2 Gly-Gaba_5 Rgs13 GABA-Gly neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABA-Gly neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Rgs13 (Mmus), Hoxc4 (Mmus), Adgrg6 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other NTS-PARN Neurod2 Gly-Gaba_5 cells by expression of Rgs13, Syt6. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Slc6a5). These cells are located in the Medulla, brain , in or close to the regions: Spinal vestibular nucleus, Nucleus of the solitary tract . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:5108 NTS-PARN Neurod2 Gly-Gaba_5." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, NTS-PARN Neurod2 Gly-Gaba_5 Rgs13 does not have cells in parvicellular reticular nucleus (PARN). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
