[Term]
id: PCL:0117490
name: NTS-PARN Neurod2 Gly-Gaba_5 Vwa5a GABA-Gly neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABA-Gly neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Chrdl2 (Mmus), Pax5 (Mmus), Bmp2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other NTS-PARN Neurod2 Gly-Gaba_5 cells by expression of Vwa5a, Gm13986. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc6a5, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Medulla, brain , in or close to the regions: Spinal vestibular nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:5110 NTS-PARN Neurod2 Gly-Gaba_5." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type NTS-PARN Neurod2 Gly-Gaba_5 Vwa5a does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for nucleus of the solitary tract (NTS), parvicellular reticular nucleus (PARN). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "5110 NTS-PARN Neurod2 Gly-Gaba_5" EXACT []
