[Term]
id: PCL:0117491
name: NTS-PARN Neurod2 Gly-Gaba_5 Zfpm2 GABA-Gly neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABA-Gly neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Chrdl2 (Mmus), Adgrg6 (Mmus), Vwc2 (Mmus), Hoxa5 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other NTS-PARN Neurod2 Gly-Gaba_5 cells by expression of Zfpm2, Adgrg6, Dlgap2. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Slc6a5). These cells are located in the Medulla, brain , in or close to the regions: Area postrema, Nucleus of the solitary tract . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:5111 NTS-PARN Neurod2 Gly-Gaba_5." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
