[Term]
id: PCL:0117500
name: SPVI-SPVC Sall3 Nfib Gly-Gaba_1 A730046J19Rik GABA-Gly neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABA-Gly neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Cdh3 (Mmus), A730046J19Rik (Mmus), Pax2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other SPVI-SPVC Sall3 Nfib Gly-Gaba_1 cells by expression of A730046J19Rik. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Slc6a5). These cells are located in the Medulla, Cerebellum , in or close to the regions: Copula pyramidis, Spinal nucleus of the trigeminal, interpolar part, Spinal nucleus of the trigeminal, oral part, Nucleus of the solitary tract . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:5120 SPVI-SPVC Sall3 Nfib Gly-Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, SPVI-SPVC Sall3 Nfib Gly-Gaba_1 A730046J19Rik does not have cells in spinal nucleus of the trigeminal, caudal part (SPVC). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
