name: SPVI-SPVC Sall3 Nfib Gly-Gaba_2 Hpse GABA-Gly neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABA-Gly neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Hpse (Mmus), Ddr2 (Mmus), Meis2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other SPVI-SPVC Sall3 Nfib Gly-Gaba_2 cells by expression of Hpse, Pde5a. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad1, Slc6a5, Gad2, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Medulla, brain , in or close to the regions: Spinal nucleus of the trigeminal, interpolar part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:5137 SPVI-SPVC Sall3 Nfib Gly-Gaba_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
