[Term]
id: PCL:0117519
name: SPVI-SPVC Sall3 Nfib Gly-Gaba_2 Has2os GABA-Gly neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABA-Gly neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Hoxb8 (Mmus), Has2os (Mmus), Gm26644 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other SPVI-SPVC Sall3 Nfib Gly-Gaba_2 cells by expression of Has2os. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Slc6a5). These cells are located in the brain . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:5139 SPVI-SPVC Sall3 Nfib Gly-Gaba_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type SPVI-SPVC Sall3 Nfib Gly-Gaba_2 Has2os does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for spinal nucleus of the trigeminal, interpolar part (SPVI), spinal nucleus of the trigeminal, caudal part (SPVC). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "5139 SPVI-SPVC Sall3 Nfib Gly-Gaba_2" EXACT []
is_a: PCL:0111707 ! SPVI-SPVC Sall3 Nfib Gly-Gaba_2 GABA-Gly neuron (Mmus)
relationship: RO:0002215 GO:0061534 {comment="Inferred to be gamma-aminobutyric acid secretion, neurotransmission, glycine secretion, neurotransmission based on expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Slc6a5"}
relationship: RO:0002215 GO:0061537 {comment="Inferred to be gamma-aminobutyric acid secretion, neurotransmission, glycine secretion, neurotransmission based on expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Slc6a5"}
