[Term]
id: PCL:0117529
name: SPVI-SPVC Sall3 Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_1 Rai14 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Hoxb8 (Mmus), Rai14 (Mmus), B130024G19Rik (Mmus), Scn4b (Mmus). It is distinguished from other SPVI-SPVC Sall3 Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_1 cells by expression of Rai14, Scn4b. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Slc6a5, Slc32a1, Gad2, Gad1). These cells are located in the Medulla, brain , in or close to the regions: Spinal nucleus of the trigeminal, interpolar part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:5149 SPVI-SPVC Sall3 Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, SPVI-SPVC Sall3 Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_1 Rai14 does not have cells in spinal nucleus of the trigeminal, caudal part (SPVC). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "5149 SPVI-SPVC Sall3 Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_1" EXACT []
