[Term]
id: PCL:0117536
name: SPVI-SPVC Sall3 Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_2 Mctp2 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Gbx1 (Mmus), Hpse (Mmus), Them7 (Mmus), Slc6a5 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other SPVI-SPVC Sall3 Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_2 cells by expression of Mctp2, Them7. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad1, Gad2, Slc32a1, Slc6a5). These cells are located in the Medulla, brain , in or close to the regions: Spinal nucleus of the trigeminal, interpolar part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:5156 SPVI-SPVC Sall3 Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, SPVI-SPVC Sall3 Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_2 Mctp2 does not have cells in spinal nucleus of the trigeminal, caudal part (SPVC). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
