[Term]
id: PCL:0117538
name: SPVI-SPVC Sall3 Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_2 Kcng1 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Hoxb8 (Mmus), Met (Mmus), Syt10 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other SPVI-SPVC Sall3 Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_2 cells by expression of Kcng1, Eya2. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad1, Gad2, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the brain . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:5158 SPVI-SPVC Sall3 Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type SPVI-SPVC Sall3 Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_2 Kcng1 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for spinal nucleus of the trigeminal, interpolar part (SPVI), spinal nucleus of the trigeminal, caudal part (SPVC). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme. Warning: Despite its name, SPVI-SPVC Sall3 Lhx1 Gly-Gaba_2 Kcng1 does not secrete the neurotransmitter Gly, as assessed by expression of multiple marker genes.
