[Term]
id: PCL:0117544
name: RO-RPA Pkd2l1 Gaba_1 Grap2 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Pkd1l2 (Mmus), Grap2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other RO-RPA Pkd2l1 Gaba cells by expression of Grap2. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1, Ddc). These cells are located in the brain . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:5164 RO-RPA Pkd2l1 Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type RO-RPA Pkd2l1 Gaba_1 Grap2 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for nucleus raphe obscurus (RO), nucleus raphe pallidus (RPA). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
