[Term]
id: PCL:0117558
name: candelabrum cell (Mmus)
def: "A candelabrum cell of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Cdh1 (Mmus), Bhlhe22 (Mmus), Aldh1a3 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other CB PLI Gly-Gaba_1 cells by expression of Cdh1, Pde10a. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Cerebellum, brain , in or close to the regions: Simple lobule . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:5178 CB PLI Gly-Gaba_1." [https://10.5281/zenodo.17543831, https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-021-03220-z., https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z, https://doi.org/10.1038/s41593-022-01057-x]
comment: Rationale for assigning this type to reference data: Mapping of this cell type is supported by high group purity (94%), high target purity (95%), and consistent GABA neurotransmitter predictions and neurotransmitter agreement. Mapping of this cell type is corroborated by MAPMYCELLS-based bioinformatic analysis of Osorno et al., 2022 and its spatial localization profile. Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, CB PLI Gly-Gaba_1 Cdh1 does not secrete the neurotransmitter Gly, as assessed by expression of multiple marker genes. {xref="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41593-022-01057-x", xref="https://10.5281/zenodo.17543831", xref="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-021-03220-z."}
synonym: "5178 CB PLI Gly-Gaba_1" EXACT []
