[Term]
id: PCL:0117562
name: CB PLI Gly-Gaba_2 Sv2b Lugaro cell (Mmus)
def: "A Lugaro cell of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Hmga2 (Mmus), Pthlh (Mmus), Oprm1 (Mmus), Slc6a5 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other CB PLI Gly-Gaba_2 cells by expression of Sv2b, Tenm4. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad1, Gad2, Slc6a5, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Cerebellum, brain , in or close to the regions: Paraflocculus, arbor vitae . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:5182 CB PLI Gly-Gaba_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
