[Term]
id: PCL:0117566
name: CBX Golgi Gly-Gaba_1 Gm17634 cerebellar Golgi cell (Mmus)
def: "A cerebellar Golgi cell of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Zfp385c (Mmus), Megf11 (Mmus), Gm17634 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other CBX Golgi Gly-Gaba cells by expression of Gm17634. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Gad1, Gad2, Slc6a5, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Cerebellum, brain . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:5186 CBX Golgi Gly-Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
