id: PCL:0117579
name: CB Granule Glut_1 Rgs6 cerebellar granule cell (Mmus)
def: "A cerebellar granule cell of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Cbln3 (Mmus), Tmem132d (Mmus). It is distinguished from other CB Granule Glut_1 cells by expression of Rgs6. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a7, Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Medulla, Cerebellum, brain , in or close to the regions: Dentate nucleus, Dorsal cochlear nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:5199 CB Granule Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
