name: CB Granule Glut_2 Gap43 cerebellar granule cell (Mmus)
def: "A cerebellar granule cell of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Gabra6 (Mmus), Gap43 (Mmus), Il1rap (Mmus). It is distinguished from other CB Granule Glut_2 cells by expression of Gap43, Kcnq5. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a7). These cells are located in the Cerebellum, brain , in or close to the regions: Paraflocculus, Nodulus (X), arbor vitae, Uvula (IX), Flocculus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:5200 CB Granule Glut_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
