[Term]
id: PCL:0117583
name: DCO UBC Glut_1 Slc4a4 unipolar brush cell (Mmus)
def: "A unipolar brush cell of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Sln (Mmus), Asic5 (Mmus), Slc4a4 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other DCO UBC Glut cells by expression of Slc4a4. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a7, Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Medulla, Cerebellum , in or close to the regions: Paraflocculus, Flocculus, Dentate nucleus, Dorsal cochlear nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:5203 DCO UBC Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions.
