[Term]
id: PCL:0117584
name: DCO UBC Glut_1 Calb2 unipolar brush cell (Mmus)
def: "A unipolar brush cell of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Sln (Mmus), Cbln3 (Mmus), Rgs6 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other DCO UBC Glut cells by expression of Calb2, Rgs6. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a7, Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Medulla, Cerebellum , in or close to the regions: Dorsal cochlear nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:5204 DCO UBC Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
