[Term]
id: PCL:0117618
name: Astroependymal NN_1 Cidea cell (Mmus)
def: "A cell of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Myoc (Mmus), Slc13a4 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other Astroependymal NN_1 cells by expression of Cidea. These cells are located in the Hippocampal region, brain , in or close to the regions: Dentate gyrus, molecular layer, third ventricle . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:5238 Astroependymal NN_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
