name: Ependymal NN_1 Tagln ependymal cell (Mmus)
def: "A ependymal cell of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Ccdc153 (Mmus), Qrfp (Mmus), Col6a5 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other Ependymal NN_1 cells by expression of Tagln. These cells are located in the Cerebellum, brain , in or close to the regions: fourth ventricle, lateral ventricle, Lobule II . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:5255 Ependymal NN_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
